8,"sha":"98221c5ef81c5979e0853df8ca8f7e46e7bee64b"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"boschtech","providerType":"User"},"email":"admin@boschtechnologies.com","name":"boschtech"},"authoredDate":"2026-04-14T15:23:48Z","committedDate":"2026-04-14T15:23:48Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"boschtech","providerType":"User"},"email":"admin@boschtechnologies.com","name":"boschtech"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:38:38.533Z","repositoryId":1210604798,"sha":"a18b372da3824e88310cf954c7679488bc0a5c19"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"boschtech","providerType":"User"},"email":"admin@boschtechnologies.com","name":"boschtech"},"authoredDate":"2026-04-14T15:20:59Z","committedDate":"2026-04-14T15:20:59Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:38:38.533Z","repositoryId":1210604798,"sha":"189b1e5808699b19203dec2d7c7108ad16d84a14"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:38:38.533Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/198587710?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boschtech","id":198587710,"login":"boschtech","node_id":"U_kgDOC9Y1Pg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/product-service/commits/155c1313452a3a535aca4475ef292709c42070af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T15:57:14Z","email":"admin@boschtechnologies.com","name":"boschtech"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T15:57:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: raise RATE_LIMIT_RPM for the E2E job only (#10)\n\nThe E2E job (E2E Tests (@product-service)) failed on this PR with 3 failed /\n20 passed. Traces from all three failures show the same pattern the code\nchange targets: GET /api/products returning HTTP 429 six times versus 200\nthree times, because every Playwright worker shares the runner''s IP and the\nper-IP bucket defaults to 100 requests per minute.\n\nSet RATE_LIMIT_RPM: ''100000'' on the \"Start product-service\" and\n\"Start order-service\" steps of the E2E job so the limiter is effectively\ndisabled for that suite.\n\nThe Security Penetration Test job is deliberately left alone: its scan fires\na 120-request burst and raises a MEDIUM finding unless it observes a 429, so\nit must keep running at the default of 100.\n\nCo-authored-by: Oz <oz-agent@warp.dev>","tree":{"sha":"494793e50af156bf8cfb87454e4a53c64004e88c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/product-service/git/trees/494793e50af156bf8cfb87454e4a53c64004e88c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/product-service/git/commits/155c1313452a3a535aca4475ef292709c42070af","verification":{"payload":"tree 494793e50af156bf8cfb87454e4a53c64004e88c\nparent bbc06416c979888fd34f50b6a326d4ebb2e403a5\nauthor boschtech <admin@boschtechnologies.com> 1785945434 +0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785945434 +0400\n\nci: raise RATE_LIMIT_RPM for the E2E job only (#10)\n\nThe E2E job (E2E Tests (@product-service)) failed on this PR with 3 failed /\n20 passed. Traces from all three failures show the same pattern the code\nchange targets: GET /api/products returning HTTP 429 six times versus 200\nthree times, because every Playwright worker shares the runner''s IP and the\nper-IP bucket defaults to 100 requests per minute.\n\nSet RATE_LIMIT_RPM: ''100000'' on the \"Start product-service\" and\n\"Start order-service\" steps of the E2E job so the limiter is effectively\ndisabled for that suite.\n\nThe Security Penetration Test job is deliberately left alone: its scan fires\na 120-request burst and raises a MEDIUM finding unless it observes a 429, so\nit must keep running at the default of 100.\n\nCo-authored-by: Oz <oz-agent@warp.dev>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc11aCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXHEQADjL/1jv+rYsdD+w5/b9h240\ny+3Pz3OzBc/6AqiiKrTT7rhtsDienMfhJ49jHjcobLwWh4/wZjfN9LzA9PW7/Yfe\nz38Qz8yGeoD9LXkGb4z+0yb9xp6vUErACya+O8XyX907V6dTiDx80f61hp/kMPdp\no+7A9s9xbak3kJz23LGxsvkpgv9RZHgvz9nctp9M4/ZSrHFIXTq1zMm3bo2yQqiW\n+b1IRD8Wwr7qdOm5RqM6EgcsyCpbAmhVMFm63zozN+DneBU7MpI90LX6Gnp4djU/\nt1g41VGF0sbCEPfIA/yC5tf0qbwyUq5DlRuK3XeCtBpPT9IE0pvLH5CUOdCDXOf1\nFpciM3ZhClMLTnbf5lh7F+iTKzU83u1MoHDVSnxCAepi6QNvh8sdvRBGmHzJpqkn\nmDkFD1mt36H5r4uP8HxbfuItMEi284LtwPfJdLW+TpajGyDJ8q5YrUmnhUWlgWyi\n+/+yl0gg+Pv9i4ctTfHyf4winOisKRWd1RxvKLlw+93QIIjwd3ZgQvhTBKhHOzGO\nxo1DGfatiRJdPbOuHkc63QXgfXsY0RH6wnggKTeNXKjM7jTwDk0fBQuk9uZWwva+\nfJqi8vY1jT/sHmbOneAPMARoVw+t7uH/VdZ5bt0iqOsmyaSApVenUTx8I73ltwt1\nxR9JG3dFVg+kfV0/TXfJ\n=Coqn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-05T17:26:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/boschtech/product-service/commit/155c1313452a3a535aca4475ef292709c42070af","node_id":"C_kwDOSChc_toAKDE1NWMxMzEzNDUyYTNhNTM1YWNhNDQ3NWVmMjkyNzA5YzQyMDcwYWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/boschtech/product-service/commit/bbc06416c979888fd34f50b6a326d4ebb2e403a5","sha":"bbc06416c979888fd34f50b6a326d4ebb2e403a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/product-service/commits/bbc06416c979888fd34f50b6a326d4ebb2e403a5"}],"sha":"155c1313452a3a535aca4475ef292709c42070af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/product-service/commits/155c1313452a3a535aca4475ef292709c42070af"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/198587710?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boschtech","id":198587710,"login":"boschtech","node_id":"U_kgDOC9Y1Pg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/product-service/commits/bbc06416c979888fd34f50b6a326d4ebb2e403a5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T15:21:52Z","email":"admin@boschtechnologies.com","name":"boschtech"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T15:21:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(security): make per-IP rate limit configurable and skip actuator (#9)\n\nRateLimitFilter hardcoded 100 requests per client IP per minute. In CI every\nPlaywright worker hits the service from the same client IP, so the E2E suite\nexhausts the bucket: a Playwright trace from a failed test recorded\nGET /api/products returning HTTP 429 six times versus 200 three times, which\nmakes the frontend render \"Failed to load products\".\n\n- Add app.security.rate-limit.requests-per-minute (env var RATE_LIMIT_RPM)\n  so CI can raise the limit without a code change.\n- Inject the limit via constructor (@Value), keeping a no-arg constructor that\n  defaults to 100. The injectable constructor is annotated @Autowired because\n  the filter is a @Component with more than one constructor.\n- Keep the default at 100: the existing tests assert a 429 on the 101st\n  request, and security-pentest/src/scans/rate-limit.ts fires a 120-request\n  burst and raises a MEDIUM finding if it never observes a 429.\n- Move the token count off static state onto the bucket instance so each\n  filter instance honours its configured limit.\n- Skip rate limiting for /actuator paths so health polling no longer consumes\n  the API budget.\n- Extend RateLimitFilterTest with coverage for a lower configured limit and\n  for /actuator/health bypassing the limiter.\n\nCo-authored-by: Oz <oz-agent@warp.dev>","tree":{"sha":"e4c55ae2431dc91c9ddd965bd2292f4a62d3c37d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/product-service/git/trees/e4c55ae2431dc91c9ddd965bd2292f4a62d3c37d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/product-service/git/commits/bbc06416c979888fd34f50b6a326d4ebb2e403a5","verification":{"payload":"tree e4c55ae2431dc91c9ddd965bd2292f4a62d3c37d\nparent 56c34e4f720b6f54960fc65d3936ac5059d0d86e\nauthor boschtech <admin@boschtechnologies.com> 1785943312 +0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785943312 +0400\n\nfix(security): make per-IP rate limit configurable and skip actuator (#9)\n\nRateLimitFilter hardcoded 100 requests per client IP per minute. In CI every\nPlaywright worker hits the service from the same client IP, so the E2E suite\nexhausts the bucket: a Playwright trace from a failed test recorded\nGET /api/products returning HTTP 429 six times versus 200 three times, which\nmakes the frontend render \"Failed to load products\".\n\n- Add app.security.rate-limit.requests-per-minute (env var RATE_LIMIT_RPM)\n  so CI can raise the limit without a code change.\n- Inject the limit via constructor (@Value), keeping a no-arg constructor that\n  defaults to 100. The injectable constructor is annotated @Autowired because\n  the filter is a @Component with more than one constructor.\n- Keep the default at 100: the existing tests assert a 429 on the 101st\n  request, and security-pentest/src/scans/rate-limit.ts fires a 120-request\n  burst and raises a MEDIUM finding if it never observes a 429.\n- Move the token count off static state onto the bucket instance so each\n  filter instance honours its configured limit.\n- Skip rate limiting for /actuator paths so health polling no longer consumes\n  the API budget.\n- Extend RateLimitFilterTest with coverage for a lower configured limit and\n  for /actuator/health bypassing the limiter.\n\nCo-authored-by: Oz <oz-agent@warp.dev>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc1UQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5MUQAAy6LCIGIvaZzSWtS9CuxJq3\nHDp7wOEolHKQla6WaZsUN7nMeKqPRJunCecZ1FjNyyEJojzycUsLJXd3Bo1acGOJ\nuy4Ul4r2Iv45sp6iAIQVCN9+1HEVWTYOqVi5k3TtufqjRDOA6/TA50YALEjNrQmO\nVS7xoLN40xnuxFsT0Ohg33T2sQRFhEgt0VOY2gxL4pm7eO/uLydBM9sdJFSnnCww\nZVd1SORkDwNfAOcXufVNL1OTkKxpH2Fol1dlHux4AlL5gXRFt1Tni7kZb5ZJsdSx\nbh3zp50AgJloZYAoOlk7VhGOquikrYxKK+EQO0O