7ed32cb68ce6b71aed19439ebed4701bce9bf4a2","sha":"7ed32cb68ce6b71aed19439ebed4701bce9bf4a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/order-service/commits/7ed32cb68ce6b71aed19439ebed4701bce9bf4a2"}],"sha":"322563b8beafefe2a3ebd0e9ce324b216f17502a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/order-service/commits/322563b8beafefe2a3ebd0e9ce324b216f17502a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/198587710?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boschtech","id":198587710,"login":"boschtech","node_id":"U_kgDOC9Y1Pg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/order-service/commits/7ed32cb68ce6b71aed19439ebed4701bce9bf4a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T15:18:39Z","email":"admin@boschtechnologies.com","name":"boschtech"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T15:18:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(security): make per-IP rate limit configurable and skip actuator (#7)\n\nRateLimitFilter hardcoded 100 requests per client IP per minute. In CI every\nPlaywright worker hits the services from the same client IP, so the E2E suite\nexhausts the bucket: a Playwright trace from a failed test recorded\nGET /api/products returning HTTP 429 six times versus 200 three times, which\nmakes the frontend render \"Failed to load products\". order-service is behind\nthe same limiter, so it is raised in lockstep.\n\n- Add app.security.rate-limit.requests-per-minute (env var RATE_LIMIT_RPM)\n  so CI can raise the limit without a code change.\n- Inject the limit via constructor (@Value), keeping a no-arg constructor that\n  defaults to 100. The injectable constructor is annotated @Autowired because\n  the filter is a @Component with more than one constructor.\n- Keep the default at 100: the existing tests assert a 429 on the 101st\n  request, and security-pentest/src/scans/rate-limit.ts fires a 120-request\n  burst and raises a MEDIUM finding if it never observes a 429.\n- Move the token count off static state onto the bucket instance so each\n  filter instance honours its configured limit.\n- Skip rate limiting for /actuator paths so health polling no longer consumes\n  the API budget.\n- Extend RateLimitFilterTest with coverage for a lower configured limit and\n  for /actuator/health bypassing the limiter.\n\nCo-authored-by: Oz <oz-agent@warp.dev>","tree":{"sha":"549935ace0c7815b01ebd370a36620f0ea2091cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/order-service/git/trees/549935ace0c7815b01ebd370a36620f0ea2091cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/order-service/git/commits/7ed32cb68ce6b71aed19439ebed4701bce9bf4a2","verification":{"payload":"tree 549935ace0c7815b01ebd370a36620f0ea2091cd\nparent 77054e9ccbc5fed9cacf55dd04e6f1490b6fcb81\nauthor boschtech <admin@boschtechnologies.com> 1785943119 +0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785943119 +0400\n\nfix(security): make per-IP rate limit configurable and skip actuator (#7)\n\nRateLimitFilter hardcoded 100 requests per client IP per minute. In CI every\nPlaywright worker hits the services from the same client IP, so the E2E suite\nexhausts the bucket: a Playwright trace from a failed test recorded\nGET /api/products returning HTTP 429 six times versus 200 three times, which\nmakes the frontend render \"Failed to load products\". order-service is behind\nthe same limiter, so it is raised in lockstep.\n\n- Add app.security.rate-limit.requests-per-minute (env var RATE_LIMIT_RPM)\n  so CI can raise the limit without a code change.\n- Inject the limit via constructor (@Value), keeping a no-arg constructor that\n  defaults to 100. The injectable constructor is annotated @Autowired because\n  the filter is a @Component with more than one constructor.\n- Keep the default at 100: the existing tests assert a 429 on the 101st\n  request, and security-pentest/src/scans/rate-limit.ts fires a 120-request\n  burst and raises a MEDIUM finding if it never observes a 429.\n- Move the token count off static state onto the bucket instance so each\n  filter instance honours its configured limit.\n- Skip rate limiting for /actuator paths so health polling no longer consumes\n  the API budget.\n- Extend RateLimitFilterTest with coverage for a lower configured limit and\n  for /actuator/health bypassing the limiter.\n\nCo-authored-by: Oz <oz-agent@warp.dev>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc1RPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1mQQAKrbrAI7JoTpm+/ShLmGyGk9\nPJ+1lGKmvMkyr/PKOBepAoqI7bsuplI6CRUWwv7vdK3TaI7K9FT2XLj2iFp+Ndqr\n7CUlBZp9FwvFJOISxonbXrX6bMyP//xIFDcgTaz4ECsckQ861mS32VHQF6+pM8kU\nsLRnRkHwf7oq3FV2i5P07mb+4hyEU71nhBVC+byr/hrM2TqFLrZlmI1yv+m5gtbD\nZluM3a6rLXc/pyYoFbaVQ9pC89icRR0wSRqIiHJOLLdaTmXXeNKBT3Zz0VYXRdko\nJ38IWPv562ZI5Cy3zELt+Jb4MZ9y3GpMDiNtaE8pZ+8UA+QjS/UXl2X0rqvK0wn5\nXCcGWXb/dPjIRDfXMRmYe9pBeLC7OssAnN3Jk+lRCpFZwD2In4AB620h+Gn/0ZI7\ntcZBbGkCIP8jYyicFBu8WprGIoFXE2FSTGJ52hFcE6co5A82HBqXwNndO9exutrM\nnnl2G5pa7ucB9etaAAbo/LgVV99gh16bX4KKGffWOn/oAgci2l+3KLCP0iZA0igY\nGq66cMRsLbpBnjO1kHCW63ZSU9V04meczRzuH+9rz9pSsgm/rmc+Vj7feh9e0tRI\nMl2Q49Kg55ffV/c7AxI50Uh66h4LOXzKz9wgeH543hqVenhK20l7F4h0wr73sDv2\nZKHiZ3qlOR6BWMbj0uij\n=sXla\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":