,"commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T15:27:27Z","email":"admin@boschtechnologies.com","name":"boschtech"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T15:27:27Z","email":"admin@boschtechnologies.com","name":"boschtech"},"message":"Merge PR #13: give security-scan a real stack and lift the E2E rate limit\n\nConsolidates the CI hardening onto this branch so the search fix, the\ndependency upgrades from #12 and the workflow changes are all validated\nby one pipeline run before landing on main.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Oz <oz-agent@warp.dev>","tree":{"sha":"1df8dcbed8bbc11bc8026c7b0cd269c757cb3463","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/micro-frontend/git/trees/1df8dcbed8bbc11bc8026c7b0cd269c757cb3463"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/micro-frontend/git/commits/fe50d4c26c3a76b00d8938c98bf22af62933fcaa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/198587710?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boschtech","id":198587710,"login":"boschtech","node_id":"U_kgDOC9Y1Pg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/boschtech/micro-frontend/commit/fe50d4c26c3a76b00d8938c98bf22af62933fcaa","node_id":"C_kwDOSCngeNoAKGZlNTBkNGMyNmMzYTc2YjAwZDg5MzhjOThiZjIyYWY2MjkzM2ZjYWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/boschtech/micro-frontend/commit/4f9a80bdfc41174062be121613a46af6e30300a3","sha":"4f9a80bdfc41174062be121613a46af6e30300a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/micro-frontend/commits/4f9a80bdfc41174062be121613a46af6e30300a3"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/boschtech/micro-frontend/commit/ad73ef75f26ce7ad150ed967f3251e7a08782d46","sha":"ad73ef75f26ce7ad150ed967f3251e7a08782d46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/micro-frontend/commits/ad73ef75f26ce7ad150ed967f3251e7a08782d46"}],"sha":"fe50d4c26c3a76b00d8938c98bf22af62933fcaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/micro-frontend/commits/fe50d4c26c3a76b00d8938c98bf22af62933fcaa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/198587710?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boschtech","id":198587710,"login":"boschtech","node_id":"U_kgDOC9Y1Pg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/micro-frontend/commits/ad73ef75f26ce7ad150ed967f3251e7a08782d46/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T15:09:39Z","email":"admin@boschtechnologies.com","name":"boschtech"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T15:20:30Z","email":"admin@boschtechnologies.com","name":"boschtech"},"message":"ci: give security-scan a real stack and lift the E2E rate limit\n\nsecurity-scan was a false green: it had no Postgres service, so both\nSpring Boot jars failed to build their EntityManagerFactory\n(`ddl-auto: update` + PostgreSQL dialect, defaulting to\njdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/{product,order}_db) and never bound a\nport. Its `Wait for services` loop was `curl -sf ... && break || sleep 2`,\nwhich can never fail the step, so the pentest happily scanned nothing and\nreported success.\n\n- Add the same postgres:16 service container e2e-tests uses (same env,\n  5432:5432, pg_isready health options).\n- Add the \"Create service databases\" step creating product_db/order_db.\n- Split the single `Start stack` step into per-service steps so each gets\n  its own DATABASE_URL (product_db vs order_db) plus credentials; a shared\n  `env:` block cannot express two different databases.\n- Replace the non-asserting wait loop with the asserting `wait_for` helper\n  from e2e-tests, tailing /tmp/product.log, /tmp/order.log and\n  /tmp/frontend.log on timeout.\n\nRATE_LIMIT_RPM is deliberately NOT set in security-scan:\nsecurity-pentest/src/scans/rate-limit.ts fires a 120-request burst and\nraises RATE-001 unless it observes a 429, so that job must keep the\ndefault limit of 100/min.\n\nIn e2e-tests, set RATE_LIMIT_RPM=100000 on both service start steps. All\nPlaywright workers share the runner''s single outbound IP, so the suite\nexhausts RateLimitFilter''s 100 req/min per-IP bucket; a trace from run\n31014149793 recorded six 429s on GET /api/products, rendering \"Failed to\nload products\" (1 failed + 7 flaky).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Oz <oz-agent@warp.dev>","tree":{"sha":"1df8dcbed8bbc11bc8026c7b0cd269c757cb3463","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/micro-frontend/git/trees/1df8dcbed8bbc11bc8026c7b0cd269c757cb3463"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/micro-frontend/git/commits/ad73ef75f26ce7ad150ed967f3251e7a08782d46","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/198587710?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boschtech","id":198587710,"login":"boschtech","node_id":"U_kgDOC9Y1Pg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/boschtech/micro-frontend/commit/ad73ef75f26ce7ad150ed967f3251e7a08782d46","node_id":"C_kwDOSCngeNoAKGFkNzNlZjc1ZjI2Y2U3YWQxNTBlZDk2N2YzMjUxZTdhMDg3ODJkNDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/boschtech/micro-frontend/commit/4f9a80bdfc41174062be121613a46af6e30300a3","sha":"4f9a80bdfc41174062be121613a46af6e30300a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/micro-frontend/commits/4f9a80bdfc41174062be121613a46af6e30300a3"}],"sha":"ad73ef75f26ce7ad150ed967f3251e7a08782d46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/micro-frontend/commits/ad73ef75f26ce7ad150ed967f3251e7a08782d46"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/198587710?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boschtech","id":198587710,"login":"boschtech","node_id":"U_kgDOC9Y1Pg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/micro-frontend/commits/4f9a80bdfc41174062be121613a46af6e30300a3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T15:19:33Z","email":"admin@boschtechnologies.com","name":"boschtech"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T15:19:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(deps): resolve all 16 npm audit vulnerabilities (#12)\n\nUpgrade direct dependencies out of vulnerable ranges and refresh the\nlockfile so every transitive advisory is resolved.\n\nDirect upgrades:\n- react-router 7.14.1 -> 8.3.0 (production dep; fixes the vendored\n  turbo-stream TYPE_ERROR deserialization unauth RCE, GHSA-49rj-9fvp-4h2h,\n  plus 7 further react-router advisories; all of 6.x/7.x/<=8.2.0 is affected)\n- react / react-dom ^19.0.0 -> ^19.2.7 (19.2.8), the minimum peer required\n  by react-router 8\n- vite 6.4.2 -> 6.4.3 (server.fs.deny bypass, optimized deps `.map` path\n  traversal, launch-editor UNC disclosure; also pulls esbuild 0.25.x)\n- vitest / @vitest/coverage-v8 2.1.9 -> 3.2.7 (critical Vitest UI arbitrary\n  file read/execute, fixed in >=3.2.6)\n\nTransitive upgrades via `npm audit fix`: axios 1.19.0, brace-expansion\n1.1.18/2.1.4/5.0.9, form-data 4.0.6, js-yaml 4.3.1, postcss 8.5.25,\nws 8.21.2, qs 6.15.3, body-parser 2.3.0, @babel/core 7.29.7.\n\nnpm audit: 16 vulnerabilities (2 critical, 8 high, 4 moderate, 2 low) -> 0.\n\nNo source or config changes were required. The app only uses react-router''s\ndeclarative APIs (BrowserRouter, MemoryRouter, Routes, Route, Link, NavLink,\nuseParams, useNavigate), none of which changed in v8, and the v8 framework-mode\nrequirements (vite 7+, middleware, meta/loaderData) do not apply here. The 95%\ncoverage thresholds in vitest.config.ts are unchanged.\n\nCo-authored-by: Oz <oz-agent@warp.dev>","tree":{"sha":"dbfeb12c558aeee490943cdae93b828bd9b3cab9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/micro-frontend/git/trees/dbfeb12c558aeee490943cdae93b828bd9b3cab9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/micro-frontend/git/commits/4f9a80bdfc41174062be121613a46af6e30300a3","verification":{"payload":"tree dbfeb12c558aeee490943cdae93b828bd9b3cab9\nparent e5248d4979cbd0e2d042c9decd958a9630b41651\nauthor boschtech <admin@boschtechnologies.com> 1785943173 +0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785943173 +0400\n\nchore(deps): resolve all 16 npm audit vulnerabilities (#12)\n\nUpgrade direct dependencies out of vulnerable ranges and refresh the\nlockfile so every transitive advisory is resolved.\n\nDirect upgrades:\n- react-router 7.14.1 -> 8.3.0 (production dep; fixes the vendored\n  turbo-stream TYPE_ERROR deserialization unauth RCE, GHSA-49rj-9fvp-4h2h,\n  plus 7 further react-router advisories; all of 6.x/7.x/<=8.2.0 is affected)\n- react / react-dom ^19.0.0 -> ^19.2.7 (19.2.8), the minimum peer required\n  by react-router 8\n- vite 6.4.2 -> 6.4.3 (server.fs.deny bypass, optimized deps `.map` path\n  traversal, launch-editor UNC disclosure; also pulls esbuild 0.25.x)\n- vitest / @vitest/coverage-v8 2.1.9 -> 3.2.7 (critical Vitest UI arbitrary\n  file read/execute, fixed in >=3.2.6)\n\nTransitive upgrades via `npm audit fix`: axios 1.19.0, brace-expansion\n1.1.18/2.1.4/5.0.9, form-data 4.0.6, js-yaml 4.3.1, postcss 8.5.25,\nws 8.21.2, qs 6.15.3, body-parser 2.3.0, @babel/core 7.29.7.\n\nnpm audit: 16 vulnerabilities (2 critical, 8 high, 4 moderate, 2 low) -> 0.\n\nNo source or config changes were required. The app only uses react-router''s\ndeclarative APIs (BrowserRouter, MemoryRouter, Routes, Route, Link, NavLink,\nuseParams, useNavigate), none of which changed in v8, and the v8 framework-mode\nrequirements (vite 7+, middleware, meta/loaderData) do not apply here. The 95%\ncoverage thresholds in vitest.config.ts are unchanged.\n\nCo-authored-by: Oz <oz-agent@warp.dev>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc1SFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAylMQABvmjxuVixDlTfLj/59/R8sK\nZr9BY2QTIiG9Pcdke2a6tKqezVuQkUgySnV/8gjKBiprO+eUSGCrsZYBbJMiz6w5\nDOsAkPmf1u5k/ytFqSHKpUdyfn9zy4+ommnKw0uLaN4ZRqJ2pMQ+71+YAfgKmXSm\nx2tvMjBk8gat//yRDUXmncIErwvB507fo1wfSED4ji/0775LRJDBeSZUl+UgefuH\nAJBJ1kfKHB1z0MSyQTgE4l0n2WXjj8rlaiz/G5qhMpOCPDnaGSwgrnbYNJtrh8cE\nzBmFeL5a3cjMVSLsKDvcq3HIUY8j1j2Sm/aO7W868qF45Cf5IybnR9iJTMmj8Cww\nWbW+CRzwf4BWTdcV+RblH9JlZtw6TKnRIrWRy/VgHqZhJp4ngrBxyyquXWXsvmq4\nnG91jldkA57CRefgCsbY0fdLkGGtt6LKxONkRRuPRTG7ubvK6U762Tv4GcYWmjlN\ncgWWbtRSprAsPTpamAKkm2bMlDxYqAugahgmepuvMotj82EvC8k47jzFrR98dwr0\nD+q8P66yLmzfRWqK4RWUb3e+wsY4BMfe33nBpDlp+iqQGEO0eLfWS9nRDUHXblpT\nt8eYyBB3nCMKutdzxBcVflSzeGu4voMgn+viY9t79iTkqjKd7NKu/3rH+P/E8K71\nQpNjXf7AUL4S3kwi5f+K\n=iV/a\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-05T15:28:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/user