":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/micro-frontend/commits/e5248d4979cbd0e2d042c9decd958a9630b41651/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T14:13:54Z","email":"admin@boschtechnologies.com","name":"boschtech"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T14:13:54Z","email":"admin@boschtechnologies.com","name":"boschtech"},"message":"ci: provision Postgres for the E2E job\n\nThe \"Wait for services to be healthy\" step failed on every run, timing out\nafter 120s on http://localhost:8080/actuator/health.\n\nBoth product-service and order-service are Spring Boot + JPA apps configured\nwith `ddl-auto: update` and the PostgreSQL dialect, and they default to\njdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/{product,order}_db. The e2e-tests job never\nprovisioned a database, so Hibernate could not open a connection, the\nentityManagerFactory bean failed, and neither service ever bound its port:\n\n  Unable to open JDBC Connection for DDL execution\n  [Connection to localhost:5432 refused ...]\n\nH2 is only a test-scope dependency, so the packaged jars cannot fall back to\nan in-memory database.\n\n- Add a postgres:16 service container to the e2e-tests job\n- Create product_db and order_db before the services start\n- Pass DATABASE_URL/DATABASE_USERNAME/DATABASE_PASSWORD to each service\n- Dump the tail of the relevant service log when a health check times out,\n  so future startup failures are diagnosable from the job output\n\nCo-Authored-By: Oz <oz-agent@warp.dev>","tree":{"sha":"08c9e3703a5a9a99bba4b3f0898eb08b5df1f7d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/micro-frontend/git/trees/08c9e3703a5a9a99bba4b3f0898eb08b5df1f7d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/micro-frontend/git/commits/e5248d4979cbd0e2d042c9decd958a9630b41651","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/198587710?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boschtech","id":198587710,"login":"boschtech","node_id":"U_kgDOC9Y1Pg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/boschtech/micro-frontend/commit/e5248d4979cbd0e2d042c9decd958a9630b41651","node_id":"C_kwDOSCngeNoAKGU1MjQ4ZDQ5NzljYmQwZTJkMDQyYzlkZWNkOTU4YTk2MzBiNDE2NTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/boschtech/micro-frontend/commit/c97d7c62449b66a4cc52cc5912fea7cc4bf2cb47","sha":"c97d7c62449b66a4cc52cc5912fea7cc4bf2cb47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/micro-frontend/commits/c97d7c62449b66a4cc52cc5912fea7cc4bf2cb47"}],"sha":"e5248d4979cbd0e2d042c9decd958a9630b41651","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/micro-frontend/commits/e5248d4979cbd0e2d042c9decd958a9630b41651"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/198587710?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/boschtech","id":198587710,"login":"boschtech","node_id":"U_kgDOC9Y1Pg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/boschtech","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/micro-frontend/commits/c97d7c62449b66a4cc52cc5912fea7cc4bf2cb47/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T13:47:28Z","email":"admin@boschtechnologies.com","name":"boschtech"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T13:47:28Z","email":"admin@boschtechnologies.com","name":"boschtech"},"message":"fix: prevent product search crash on null description\n\nTyping in the product search bar blanked the entire page. The filter\ncalled product.description.toLowerCase() directly, but the product\nservice allows a null description (the Product entity has no @NotBlank\nand no nullable = false on that column, unlike name, price and\ncategory). The live catalog contains such a product (\"Run Shorts\"), so\nany term that did not match its name threw\n\"TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading ''toLowerCase'')\"\nduring render, which unmounted the whole React tree.\n\n- Type Product.description as string | null to match the backend contract\n- Filter through a null-safe helper and drop the products! assertion\n- Add a regression test covering a product with a null description\n\nCo-Authored-By: Oz <oz-agent@warp.dev>","tree":{"sha":"91acd2eefb4e27297631a64afeea9be5ae6f12bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/micro-frontend/git/trees/91acd2eefb4e27297631a64afeea9be5ae6f12bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/boschtech/micro-frontend/git/commits/c97d7c62449b66a4cc52cc5912fea7cc4bf2cb47","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}