blic"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.icloud/commits/7f618a7fe422a381ad18a7e3f8450a773e392c06/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T20:12:37Z","email":"github@renopoint.de","name":"ticaki"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T20:12:37Z","email":"github@renopoint.de","name":"ticaki"},"message":"fix(auth): accept 2FA codes that Apple answers with HTTP 409\n\nApple issues the six-digit code either through the trusted-device push or\nthrough the phone (SMS) channel, and each channel has its own verification\nendpoint. A code posted to the other endpoint is refused with HTTP 409 even\nthough the code itself is valid — users reported \"Invalid status code: 409\"\nright after entering a correct SMS code.\n\nprovideMfaCode now submits the code to the recorded channel and automatically\nretries the other one on 409, and treats a 409 that carries no explicit\nrejection error (-21669 / -21670) as accepted: 2sv/trust and accountLogin\ndecide whether the session is really authenticated. An explicit rejection\nstill fails immediately without burning the second channel, and the SMS\nchannel stays selected after a failed attempt so a retry targets the phone\nendpoint again.\n\nAlso mirrors pyiCloud in two details: session headers (scnt, session id,\nsession token) are extracted from the verification response so the following\n2sv/trust and accountLogin calls use fresh values, and the phone''s pushMode\nis used instead of a hardcoded \"sms\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RipphiMdDoUydhQDeKBdKp","tree":{"sha":"9b82ff8dbd6d733b9ec2ab2dfd6c347575dc60a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.icloud/git/trees/9b82ff8dbd6d733b9ec2ab2dfd6c347575dc60a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.icloud/git/commits/7f618a7fe422a381ad18a7e3f8450a773e392c06","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"