starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commit/f8012fd9abe11f9b70a2bbfc18f42217067cbdd8","node_id":"C_kwDOSDZWYNoAKGY4MDEyZmQ5YWJlMTFmOWI3MGEyYmJmYzE4ZjQyMjE3MDY3Y2JkZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commit/3e73224ed712188cf90fa4156e37a2965b3f5747","sha":"3e73224ed712188cf90fa4156e37a2965b3f5747","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/3e73224ed712188cf90fa4156e37a2965b3f5747"}],"sha":"f8012fd9abe11f9b70a2bbfc18f42217067cbdd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/f8012fd9abe11f9b70a2bbfc18f42217067cbdd8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15245608?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix","id":15245608,"login":"clicktronix","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjQ1NjA4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/3e73224ed712188cf90fa4156e37a2965b3f5747/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:37:18Z","email":"s28.morgan@gmail.com","name":"Vladislav Manakov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:37:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: close issues #33-#39; pure functions in contracts.ts, invalidation by operation (#40)\n\n* fix: close issues #33-#39 from the marqa 4.4 adoption review\n\n- actionValueExport reports only exports syntax proves are not async functions; wrapper calls such\n  as withAuth(async () => ...) are left to Next.js''s load-time check (#33)\n- import(''...'').X and typeof import(''...'') are type-only edges in the ESLint ownership rule and in\n  moduleEdges (#39)\n- runtime-markers checks marker presence, not position (#38)\n- cache docs state the privileged-store/tenant-predicate obligation and the real semantics of\n  ''use cache: private'' (#35)\n- RequestIdentity drops roles everywhere (#36); the port gate is the only rule in\n  dependency-categories (#37); skills name the normative contract and contracts.ts is default-on\n  in every listing (#34)\n\nCloses #33\nCloses #34\nCloses #35\nCloses #36\nCloses #37\nCloses #38\nCloses #39\n\n* fix(rules): read TSImportType.source before the deprecated argument key\n\n* fix(rules): report import-then-export from actions.ts and align the remaining docs\n\nReview of the #33-#39 fix found three gaps:\n\n- Treating an imported binding as \"unknown\" let `import { x } from …; export { x }` and\n  `export default x` through, which main reported. It is a value re-export and is reported as\n  `actionReexport` again; `-1` and `undefined` are reported as non-functions.\n- The action-shape constants move to module scope, and the message and comment no longer claim a\n  literal is the only build-time rejection or that a class fails the load-time check.\n- runtime-boundaries.md and modules-and-imports.md still described the stricter declared-there\n  rule; the three skills state the normative source in one shared wording; the redundant\n  marker-type fixture is gone; CHANGELOG drops issue numbers to match earlier entries.\n\n* fix: close the four findings of the PR #40 review\n\n- runtime-markers ignored importKind, so `import type {} from ''server-only''` counted as a marker\n  although TypeScript erases it; type-only imports no longer mark, with fixtures for both markers.\n- The action classifier returned unknown for arithmetic and enum bindings, so `export const\n  answer = 1 + 2` and `export { Status }` passed where main reported them; BinaryExpression and\n  TSEnumName are provable non-functions again.\n- #36: the work-items runtime pilot still kept roles in RequestIdentity and checked them there.\n  The capability now owns its role vocabulary and resolves it through an access dependency; the\n  change is recorded as a 2026-09-27 revision in candidate-plan.json.\n- #35: an anonymous store stays under row-level security as `anon`; only a privileged store\n  bypasses it. The contract and cache reference now separate the privileged tenant-private read\n  from the anonymous public read.\n\n* test(rules): split the arithmetic and enum action fixtures\n\nOne fixture carried both protections, so removing either left the suite green. Each now has its\nown fixture, and each fails when its classifier branch is removed.\n\n* feat(contract): pure functions in contracts.ts, operation-chosen invalidation\n\nArchitecture review of PR #40 (A1-A4), all pre-existing:\n\n- A4: contracts.ts may publish the pure functions of its domain, so one rule serves a neighbour''s\n  domain, the server and the browser. Purity is held by the neutral surface''s import direction;\n  the declaration classifier behind contractSurfaceBehaviour (contract-paths.mjs, ~250 lines) and\n  its fixtures are removed, replaced by a pure-API fixture and a neutralDirection mutation.\n- A2: the operation picks the revalidateTag profile, ''max'' or { expire: 0 }, instead of a fixed\n  ''max''.\n- A1: a worker outside the Next.js server cannot call next/cache; it notifies the owning app\n  through a Route Handler or bounds staleness with cacheLife.\n- A3: the owner''s server.ts publishes an invalidator that takes the writer''s primitive, so a\n  neighbour or orchestrator invalidates without learning the tags; the work-items fixture''s action\n  uses this shape (pilot revision updated).\n\n* docs(contract): pure-API constraints for contracts.ts; publish an invalidator only for a real outside writer\n\n- contracts.ts functions take time, randomness and other changing inputs as arguments and keep no\n  module state; a result computed in the browser is a preview the server recomputes.\n- The owner''s server.ts publishes an invalidator only when a neighbour or orchestrator writes\n  through its operation; inside the capability the channel takes the tag from server/**.\n\n* docs(contract): revalidateTag runs only in a Server Function or Route Handler\n\n\"A job running inside the Next.js server\" did not guarantee the context revalidateTag needs. A\nbackground job outside a Server Function or Route Handler, even in the same process, calls an\nauthenticated Route Handler of the owning app instead.","tree":{"sha":"741f225a63040e153378fdf68cbd32340b53fc27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/trees/741f225a63040e153378fdf68cbd32340b53fc27"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/commits/3e73224ed712188cf90fa4156e37a2965b3f5747","verification":{"payload":"tree 741f225a63040e153378fdf68cbd32340b53fc27\nparent 781ce1c0dc1e92060e7df2d55a431bc7de701fdd\nauthor Vladislav Manakov <s28.morgan@gmail.com> 1790519838 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790519838 +0500\n\nfix: close issues #33-#39; pure functions in contracts.ts, invalidation by operation (#40)\n\n* fix: close issues #33-#39 from the marqa 4.4 adoption review\n\n- actionValueExport reports only exports syntax proves are not async functions; wrapper calls such\n  as withAuth(async () => ...) are left to Next.js''s load-time check (#33)\n- import(''...'').X and typeof import(''...'') are type-only edges in the ESLint ownership rule and in\n  moduleEdges (#39)\n- runtime-markers checks marker presence, not position (#38)\n- cache docs state the privileged-store/tenant-predicate obligation and the real semantics of\n  ''use cache: private'' (#35)\n- RequestIdentity drops roles everywhere (#36); the port gate is the only rule in\n  dependency-categories (#37); skills name the normative contract and contracts.ts is default-on\n  in every listing (#34)\n\nCloses #33\nCloses #34\nCloses #35\nCloses #36\nCloses #37\nCloses #38\nCloses #39\n\n* fix(rules): read TSImportType.source before the deprecated argument key\n\n* fix(rules): report import-then-export from actions.ts and align the remaining docs\n\nReview of the #33-#39 fix found three gaps:\n\n- Treating an imported binding as \"unknown\" let `import { x } from …; export { x }` and\n  `export default x` through, which main reported. It is a value re-export and is reported as\n  `actionReexport` again; `-1` and `undefined` are reported as non-functions.\n- The action-shape constants move to module scope, and the message and comment no longer claim a\n  literal is the only build-time rejection or that a class fails the load-time check.\n- runtime-boundaries.md and modules-and-imports.md still described the stricter declared-there\n  rule; the three skills state the normative source in one shared wording; the redundant\n  marker-type fixture is gone; CHANGELOG drops issue numbers to match earlier entries.\n\n* fix: close the four findings of the PR #40 review\n\n- runtime-markers ignored importKind, so `import type {} from ''server-only''` counted as a marker\n  although TypeScript erases it; type-only imports no longer mark, with fixtures for both markers.\n- The action classifier returned unknown for arithmetic and enum bindings, so `export const\n  answer = 1 + 2` and `export { Status }` passed where main reported them; BinaryExpression and\n  TSEnumName are provable non-functions again.\n- #36: the work-items runtime pilot still kept roles in RequestIdentity and checked them there.\n  The capability now owns its role vocabulary and resolves it through an access dependency; the\n  change is recorded as a 2026-09-27 revision in candidate-plan.json.\n- #35: an anonymous store stays under row-level security as `anon`; only a privileged store\n  bypasses it. The contract and cache reference now separate the privileged tenant-private read\n  from the anonymous public read.\n\n* test(rules): split the arithmetic and enum action fixtures\n\nOne fixture carried both protections, so removing either left the suite green. Each now has its\nown fixture, and each fails when its classifier branch is removed.\n\n* feat(contract): pure functions in contracts.ts, operation-chosen invalidation\n\nArchitecture review of PR #40 (A1-A4), all pre-existing:\n\n- A4: contracts.ts may publish the pure functions of its domain, so one rule serves a neighbour''s\n  domain, the server and the browser. Purity is held by the neutral surface''s import direction;\n  the declaration classifier behind contractSurfaceBehaviour (contract-paths.mjs, ~250 lines) and\n  its fixtures are removed, replaced by a pure-API fixture and a neutralDirection mutation.\n- A2: the operation picks the revalidateTag profile, ''max'' or { expire: 0 }, instead of a fixed\n  ''max''.\n- A1: a worker outside the Next.js server cannot call next/cache; it notifies the owning app\n  through a Route Handler or bounds staleness with cacheLife.\n- A3: the owner''s server.ts publishes an invalidator that takes the writer''s primitive, so a\n  neighbour or orchestrator invalidates without learning the tags; the work-items fixture''s action\n  uses this shape (pilot revision updated).\n\n* docs(contract): pure-API constraints for contracts.ts; publish an invalidator only for a real outside writer\n\n- contracts.ts functions take time, randomness and other changing inputs as arguments and keep no\n  module state; a result computed in the browser is a preview the server recomputes.\n- The owner''s server.ts publishes an invalidator only when a neighbour or orchestrator writes\n  through its operation; inside the capability the channel takes the tag from server/**.\n\n* docs(contract): revalidateTag runs only in a Server Function or Route Handler\n\n\"A job running inside the Next.js server\" did not guarantee the context revalidateTag needs. A\nbackground job outside a Server Function or Route Handler, even in the same process, calls an\nauthenticated Route Handler of the owning app instead.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquSoeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAu7IQAIHdrS6yILDl8pf7xCbhY/Z1\nMg75LwN8/UA/pXtwFO5YiFxvLP1DMCnn3OzUq7UlaNkKvFBzEV4hHY/afwa8eQoD\nRm8PNlgfV0rsAbPPN8UJG1d9d/YeTmQYDzB+Pp2CvPkT5Ec9s/YcbMIV4EXKWCiR\nI2vzi0gV5C5z3NNk5nBX0uGz+vZNgSKYpVwLXXVEv+WbCQZzJuaSGZXIwSMKaVdq\n3Iz9MN4UV4ewFXgI1PYO5iIZu/5zKjOguHyhQD4pe92LGjqdePeP9rL5SRpGOKpE\nDkD6kz74AljJYXqaNvXFk7LBvxbLMXGNip/MRs7sy9fL4OAtn4wSI7MAzQj2mpMq\n0plqc3QrL6TRLgyglMiVkEca2GqY0Gst4ZLkXsvoIZDuH6af79g9DTI7SjWUMv5K\npuNnOjIxlZETztWjDrSCfziHy+WqGh+kHq+MSVNeHZ2mSEpGhOOU9Vj07eRtxb39\neINxOcYbyKiLG44oWfdEddtg1eVc4B/1H9qyOyG+b2qASvjq1WUOQMhsfiPXBB+5\nFRSAwE69IJBCMuAnFQaDpvZU8lUP/uXlaAxR8Wq31mqaR7br8kBY4fb1I/5r/Dab\nuCYlIrMRX2yOutd/ykP8JPpTK7B6kFj+uqlQrCI3dCagHF/NcpV9ulm0/b15mr/J\nZLOFFsoGjCZAgIsOb5dD\n=7KlF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T14:37:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html