x/nextjs-clean-skills/commit/fa08f196ec6d4eee419333e459a1c6555c67b5c8","sha":"fa08f196ec6d4eee419333e459a1c6555c67b5c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/fa08f196ec6d4eee419333e459a1c6555c67b5c8"}],"sha":"ba897c033800547231f98ade675a3ec9f2d0d024","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/ba897c033800547231f98ade675a3ec9f2d0d024"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15245608?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix","id":15245608,"login":"clicktronix","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjQ1NjA4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/fa08f196ec6d4eee419333e459a1c6555c67b5c8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T09:18:21Z","email":"s28.morgan@gmail.com","name":"Vladislav Manakov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T09:18:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: audit capability module cohesion (#29)\n\n* fix: audit capability module cohesion\n\n* fix(migrating-architecture): restore dropped check-record facts\n\nThe audit-cohesion PR rewrote the check-record paragraph in move-and-verify.md\nand silently dropped two load-bearing facts: that the record is the only\nevidence a reviewer gets, and the SIGKILL-after-grace-period behaviour of a\nkilled check wrapper. Restore the original wording; that rewrite was outside\nthe PR''s stated subject. Trim adjacent prose elsewhere in the file to stay\nunder the reference length budget.\n\n* feat(rules): mechanically enforce two module-cohesion properties\n\nAdd rules/check-module-cohesion.mjs, a standalone directory-shape checker in\nthe same style as the existing check-*.mjs tools: it walks moduleRoot and\nflags (a) a directory whose production content, recursively, is nothing but\n__tests__/__mocks__/fixtures or dev-suffixed files, and (b) lib.ts coexisting\nwith a sibling lib/ under one owner. Both were previously documented as\nreview-only; they are directory-shape properties a static walk can prove,\nunlike private-filename prefix repetition or role naming, which stay review\nfindings because they require reading what a file means.\n\nWire the tool into `npm run validate` via scripts/validate-module-cohesion.mjs\n(clean fixture plus one failing mutation per property, following\nvalidate-contract-tools.mjs), register it in rules/README.md as the tool''s\nEnforced Invariant #8, and note the split in docs/architecture-contract.md''s\nInternal Cohesion section. Also document, in the same Public Surfaces\nsection, that no root surface other than actions.ts may define behaviour\n(wrappers, closures, status maps) — surfaces publish named re-exports, and\nactions.ts is the one inversion the ''use server'' compiler constraint forces\n— and extend the migration verify.js reviewer prompt with that check plus a\ncheck for stale mock.module() paths after a move. Update CHANGELOG.md so the\n\"all cohesion properties are review-only\" claim no longer covers these two.\n\n* docs(designing-architecture): positive cohesion rule and schema kinds\n\nmodule-cohesion.md defined cohesion only by negation. Add the positive\n\"two names, two jobs\" rule from the platform''s modules.md: a scenario folder\nnames a verb+object product operation, a file names its architectural role\n(query.ts/command.ts/orchestrator.ts, data.ts/repository.ts/http.ts,\nquery.ts/mutation.ts/store.ts), flat-until-a-second-production-file promotes\nto a folder, and use-case.ts/bare adapter.ts-service.ts-manager.ts/generic\nsubject buckets are banned. Add the read-verb vocabulary (list-/read-, never\nget-/load-; authorization is a role such as rsc.ts, never a verb) and\nrestate lib.ts/lib/ as \"never both, name lib/ files by behaviour\" per finding.\n\nSplit the three schema kinds (input, record, row) into a new portable\nreference, references/outbound/schema-kinds.md, linked from both\nmodule-cohesion.md and row-vs-domain-types.md — keeping the distinction in\nmodule-cohesion.md itself blew the reference''s 2600-char budget, and the\nkinds are a portable rule on their own. This is the fix for the record/row\nconflation bug class: a read projection parsed with the input schema\nrewrote stored data and crashed on a legitimately empty stored string.\n\nAlso: client-cache.md documents the second, independent driver for\npromoting a query-key factory to root query-cache.ts (''use client'' cannot\npublish a runtime-neutral value to a server consumer, regardless of\nconsumer count); the module-internal-cohesion.json scenario gains a case\nthe reference does not literally list (list-/load- variants of the same\nread scattered across two files, one secretly meaning \"authorized\"); and\nSKILL.md links the new schema-kinds reference.\n\n* fix: preserve resource folders and distinct schema contracts\n\n* docs: align cohesion guidance with schema ownership","tree":{"sha":"748c69f5faea67637e2bdae15cfc84d5676f118e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/trees/748c69f5faea67637e2bdae15cfc84d5676f118e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/commits/fa08f196ec6d4eee419333e459a1c