onix/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/1f6f7697fbfc9f555137a9d9f2cc4dd680d89994/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T16:07:54Z","email":"s28.morgan@gmail.com","name":"Vladislav Manakov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T16:07:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(docs): compress ADR 0001, drop decision maps, fold three references, soften the orchestrator rule (#27)\n\nWave 4 of the 2026-09-10 audit (C5, C9, D).\n\n- ADR 0001 reduced to Context / Decision / Validation / Consequences. Its fourteen sections had\n  restated the contract and drifted in four places; each decision now points at the contract or\n  runtime-boundaries section that states it.\n- docs/agent-decision-maps.md removed; the one map without a counterpart in the contract (review\n  order) moved to adoption-and-enforcement.md. docs/README.md and README.md updated.\n- placement/capabilities-and-ownership.md, placement/runtime-vs-compile-time.md and\n  use-cases/channel-boundaries.md folded into capability-granularity.md,\n  when-a-use-case-exists.md (new \"Orchestrating Capability\" section), modules-and-imports.md,\n  composition-without-di.md and failure-at-the-boundary.md. The nested-composition scenario now\n  points at the new section; tests/scenarios/README.md coverage row updated.\n- Orchestrator rule softened (C5): an orchestrating operation may take a sibling''s public\n  server.ts contract as a type; port + private adapter only when the mapping carries policy.\n  Contract prose and diagram rewritten; the pilot analyzer draws the type-only distinction\n  (cross-capability public root only; own runtime surface and value imports stay red, two\n  mutations); board-workflow loses adapters.ts and its ports are Picks of the siblings''\n  contracts, registered as a dated revision in candidate-plan.json; a clean ESLint fixture\n  covers the admitted shape.\n\nnpm run validate: green (39 clean / 44 mutations / 16 canaries; 20 pilot mutations; docs 18\nfiles, 112 links, 24 diagrams).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b87180f80bc4616dc115b41c4a8406aef6711856","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/trees/b87180f80bc4616dc115b41c4a8406aef6711856"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/commits/1f6f7697fbfc9f555137a9d9f2cc4dd680d89994","verification":{"payload":"tree b87180f80bc4616dc115b41c4a8406aef6711856\nparent b9a80b61803aa7709b83bba7d27dda1a523f2337\nauthor Vladislav Manakov <s28.morgan@gmail.com> 1789142874 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789142874 +0500\n\nrefactor(docs): compress ADR 0001, drop decision maps, fold three references, soften the orchestrator rule (#27)\n\nWave 4 of the 2026-09-10 audit (C5, C9, D).\n\n- ADR 0001 reduced to Context / Decision / Validation / Consequences. Its fourteen sections had\n  restated the contract and drifted in four places; each decision now points at the contract or\n  runtime-boundaries section that states it.\n- docs/agent-decision-maps.md removed; the one map without a counterpart in the contract (review\n  order) moved to adoption-and-enforcement.md. docs/README.md and README.md updated.\n- placement/capabilities-and-ownership.md, placement/runtime-vs-compile-time.md and\n  use-cases/channel-boundaries.md folded into capability-granularity.md,\n  when-a-use-case-exists.md (new \"Orchestrating Capability\" section), modules-and-imports.md,\n  composition-without-di.md and failure-at-the-boundary.md. The nested-composition scenario now\n  points at the new section; tests/scenarios/README.md coverage row updated.\n- Orchestrator rule softened (C5): an orchestrating operation may take a sibling''s public\n  server.ts contract as a type; port + private adapter only when the mapping carries policy.\n  Contract prose and diagram rewritten; the pilot analyzer draws the type-only distinction\n  (cross-capability public root only; own runtime surface and value imports stay red, two\n  mutations); board-workflow loses adapters.ts and its ports are Picks of the siblings''\n  contracts, registered as a dated revision in candidate-plan.json; a clean ESLint fixture\n  covers the admitted shape.\n\nnpm run validate: green (39 clean / 44 mutations / 16 canaries; 20 pilot mutations; docs 18\nfiles, 112 links, 24 diagrams).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpCdaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAllIQAJtxoXr04M2HMSDa96f80ZGZ\n/AVbqFVvqfv1bQtN/PZNNSpwgaDD7k30NPQyuYmxul56tehTDYRRApZ/5vGCAL76\nzvhXbNOHPQuY0n09VxqBPEEQtgPRLjuPfwwc7CyfD/vOMorwyJf1vNuQ2cCiayGG\nFgeoqhb09T5OLbU2gJXCDARFxkhv2oI5/6WHh3YWBGq2/6N1xDRukGdIzZct35eu\n16XgUKPLgXly3f7vyZ3lHPhh+os9CsEH4roOXjLs7/wymnD+0yYx7Du94VIXyxPu\nK09TQ2pLZo0pNCaT0ddlCZMRo2ClqSx6p5Mj6tvlzykqNITBX1IFM50WSov2SM79\nIjz0emyUbm0IXblEzdN/X0QlmcLzdvsKnnIIDJO4ForPNSVHQuWloVjzfjyhz7v3\nmw/QQKCppb7FmIuv4rRJqtoPPhtmaYTttkVxSxjvKcaMrjWUdT9rlVhFsoOOVPv6\nxpLSkewwzjV1rKHrrg5CxWtagMFYUbbgQYcHs6NlvYIY3PoJlW9Z1Ur6HhVbf3Vc\nAwOWKB4pbEJN7To74hXUS6pAe5lVFGmw6ki8AVVGdeo1DhSkaJGnZU6zYlBraGsN\nbZCAPKr05bVSOTOqcAzesWQBxlvbnwPc1MyFTp+cEinR2sh18z4up6ytPpiK8L8l\nAk4Mh65RICayFW0/3zHu\n=w2Pr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T16:07:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commit/1f6f7697fbfc9f555137a9d9f2cc4dd680d89994","node_id":"C_kwDOSDZWYNoAKDFmNmY3Njk3ZmJmYzlmNTU1MTM3YTlkOWYyY2M0ZGQ2ODBkODk5OTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commit/b9a80b61803aa7709b83bba7d27dda1a523f2337","sha":"b9a80b61803aa7709b83bba7d27dda1a523f2337","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/b9a80b61803aa7709b83bba7d27dda1a523f2337"}],"sha":"1f6f7697fbfc9f555137a9d9f2cc4dd680d89994","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/1f6f7697fbfc9f555137a9d9f2cc4dd680d89994"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15245608?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix","id":15245608,"login":"clicktronix","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjQ1NjA4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/b9a80b61803aa7709b83bba7d27dda1a523f2337/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T16:06:23Z","email":"s28.morgan@gmail.com","name":"Vladislav Manakov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T16:06:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(contract): Cache Components, one invalidation owner, actions.ts directive check, fixture in the real action shape (#26)\n\nDocs half of wave 3 from the 2026-09-10 audit (C1, C2, C6, C7-shared, S5, Sp1).\n\n- Cache Components section in the contract and a caching/cache-components.md reference:\n  ''use cache'' sits in server/** below the identity boundary and receives serializable scope\n  only; per-user data is ''use cache: private'' or uncached; tags are a private server/**\n  vocabulary; the channel that wrote invalidates (updateTag in actions.ts,\n  revalidateTag(tag, ''max'') in handlers and jobs); current-request reads from rsc.ts render\n  under Suspense. The README had promised the profile and no document mentioned the directive.\n- Four contradictions resolved in favour of the contract: invalidation owner (ADR §8 and\n  runtime-boundaries now defer to the contract), re-export rule (ADR follows the contract''s\n  conditions), RequestIdentity as the one identity type in shared/kernel with an \"admitted\n  infrastructure\" clause (a capability never lends its *domain* identity), forbidden as a typed\n  value.\n- actions.ts check completed: the base tier reports a missing or late ''use server'' directive\n  (actionDirective) and any value export that is not an async function declared in the file\n  (actionValueExport), including `export { helper }` of a local binding. Five mutation fixtures\n  and one clean fixture with every accepted shape.\n- work-items fixture: the Server Action takes (previousState, formData) and resolves identity,\n  reporter and the cache primitive from request scope; refusal is a typed forbidden value on\n  every channel; cache-tags.ts and a runtime memo live in server/**. Registered as a dated\n  revision in candidate-plan.json; results.json''s file count follows the inventory; measured\n  scenarios stay bound to their commits.\n- creating-react-components gains an Adoption Boundary section in its own words (no linter\n  change needed).\n\nnpm run validate: green (38 clean / 44 mutations / 16 canaries; pilot runtime ok).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c479895e7b340947e1c758a3b735922c460fb4d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/trees/c479895e7b340947e1c758a3b735922c460fb4d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/commits/b9a80b61803aa7709b83bba7d27dda1a523f2337","verification":{"payload":"tree c479895e7b340947e1c758a3b735922c460fb4d1\nparent e59a84492085847c60b748fe5e86d3edb8aaac9a\nauthor Vladislav Manakov <s28.morgan@gmail.com> 1789142783 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789142783 +0500\n\nfeat(contract): Cache Components, one invalidation owner, actions.ts directive check, fixture in the real action shape (#26)\n\nDocs half of wave 3 from the 2026-09-10 audit (C1, C2, C6, C7-shared, S5, Sp1).\n\n- Cache Components section in the contract and a caching/cache-components.md reference:\n  ''use cache'' sits in server/** below the identity boundary and receives serializable scope\n  only; per-user data is ''use cache: private'' or uncached; tags are a private server/**\n  vocabulary; the channel that wrote invalidates (updateTag in actions.ts,\n  revalidateTag(tag, ''max'') in handlers and jobs); current-request reads from rsc.ts render\n  under Suspense. The README had promised the profile and no document mentioned the directive.\n- Four contradictions resolved in favour of the contract: invalidation owner (ADR §8 and\n  runtime-boundaries now defer to the contract), re-export rule (ADR follows the contract''s\n  conditions), RequestIdentity as the one identity type in shared/kernel with an \"admitted\n  infrastructure\" clause (a capability never lends its *domain* identity), forbidden as a typed\n  value.\n- actions.ts check completed: the base tier reports a missing or late ''use server'' directive\n  (actionDirective) and any value export that is not an async function declared in the file\n  (actionValueExport), including `export { helper }` of a local binding. Five mutation fixtures\n  and one clean fixture with every accepted shape.\n- work-items fixture: the Server Action takes (previousState, formData) and resolves identity,\n  reporter and the cache primitive from request scope; refusal is a typed forbidden value on\n  every channel; cache-tags.ts and a runtime memo live in server/**. Registered as a dated\n  revision in candidate-plan.json; results.json''s file count follows the inventory; measured\n  scenarios stay bound to their commits.\n- creating-react-components gains an Adoption Boundary section in its own words (no linter\n  change needed).\n\nnpm run validate: green (38 clean / 44 mutations / 16 canaries; pilot runtime ok).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpCb/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6OcQAEd+nDyC8+/3V29Ql3dcB6oZ\n3ZNRT3cve8IHsOuz28BJ81t2GjFZ65Ulhxu50yQdiQGZ5oy/uCCW1d4xFr8rwAUa\nbMonx6KMUrISjF4OWMu7GR4aMZuICXUhQ8U19dJ51p9Xena3s64HtbjgOGY+XThL\ngUc1gZp29xI/DfGOug5752jgyn63hm7ReauPqwLtn4tOdI53vSQEsckUjNEk6fM1\nVwbhZ1SBy/Z8a40+rUvuyWU5b7zxDWXmENUhNr7wyiCMPF/TNGoYnyrq830Tr79+\nwQyGoBzhSU8POG0U3aJmLp9tUXJYeftOtilSL6KT3exfSQdN0z7ULns/MRBKxfie\nOeRqfgdTPUnoVcSnB4xnqgwzujIX9q3FW+igZ2NW+6tBxjM0dMjODDC89FeQCRud\nyArxsjMqFP6jQf