vatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15245608?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix","id":15245608,"login":"clicktronix","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjQ1NjA4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/e59a84492085847c60b748fe5e86d3edb8aaac9a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T09:27:55Z","email":"s28.morgan@gmail.com","name":"Vladislav Manakov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T09:27:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(rules): type-only edges, structural contract surfaces, runtime markers, server UI by directive, table writers (#25)\n\n* feat(rules): type-only edges, structural contract surfaces, runtime markers, server UI by directive, table writers\n\nType-only imports no longer carry a runtime direction (ownership still\napplies). contracts.ts is an admitted neutral surface whose value exports\nare classified structurally by reading the declaration — a function named\nchargeCardSchema is behaviour whatever its name. import x = require() and\nmodule.require() are visited; @scope/pkg/sub inherits @scope/pkg''s class;\na constant template literal is a constant specifier. server-only and\nclient-only markers are required first on the surfaces they guard. A\nui/** file is client only by its ''use client'' directive, so a Server\nComponent there may read its own rsc.ts. databaseResources gains an\noptional writers list; consumers keep their read-and-RPC meaning.\n\nEvery behaviour carries a clean fixture and a failing mutation; the set\nwas checked against the pre-change rules.\n\n* fix(rules): constructors are behaviour, derived schemas are schemas, server UI stops at rsc.ts\n\nA binding imported bare from a schema package is a constructor and its\nre-export is behaviour; only a call rooted in it yields a schema. Imported\nbindings are classified before the fixed point so a const derived from a\nsibling''s schema is a schema. The reader caches by content, not mtime. A\nServer Component under ui/** may read its own rsc.ts and nothing else on\nthe server side (serverUiReach). The runtime marker must precede the first\nvalue import; erased type imports do not count.\n\n* fix(rules): look up an import alias by its imported name; classify per call; erase inline type imports\n\n`import { X as Y }` is looked up as X in the source module. A classification\ndepends on every file it follows, so only parses are cached and a change in\na schema''s source file is seen inside one ESLint process. `import { type M }`\nis erased like `import type`, so the runtime marker may follow it.","tree":{"sha":"aaf7dbaf3dcbfefcf95c40e28f5be982c61c7f6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/trees/aaf7dbaf3dcbfefcf95c40e28f5be982c61c7f6d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/commits/e59a84492085847c60b748fe5e86d3edb8aaac9a","verification":{"payload":"tree aaf7dbaf3dcbfefcf95c40e28f5be982c61c7f6d\nparent e2f21d0390755dbd045216eb3ef83ec0c7451fe8\nauthor Vladislav Manakov <s28.morgan@gmail.com> 1789118875 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789118875 +0500\n\nfeat(rules): type-only edges, structural contract surfaces, runtime markers, server UI by directive, table writers (#25)\n\n* feat(rules): type-only edges, structural contract surfaces, runtime markers, server UI by directive, table writers\n\nType-only imports no longer carry a runtime direction (ownership still\napplies). contracts.ts is an admitted neutral surface whose value exports\nare classified structurally by reading the declaration — a function named\nchargeCardSchema is behaviour whatever its name. import x = require() and\nmodule.require() are visited; @scope/pkg/sub inherits @scope/pkg''s class;\na constant template literal is a constant specifier. server-only and\nclient-only markers are required first on the surfaces they guard. A\nui/** file is client only by its ''use client'' directive, so a Server\nComponent there may read its own rsc.ts. databaseResources gains an\noptional writers list; consumers keep their read-and-RPC meaning.\n\nEvery behaviour carries a clean fixture and a failing mutation; the set\nwas checked against the pre-change rules.\n\n* fix(rules): constructors are behaviour, derived schemas are schemas, server UI stops at rsc.ts\n\nA binding imported bare from a schema package is a constructor and its\nre-export is behaviour; only a call rooted in it yields a schema. Imported\nbindings are classified before the fixed point so a const derived from a\nsibling''s schema is a schema. The reader caches by content, not mtime. A\nServer Component under ui/** may read its own rsc.ts and nothing else on\nthe server side (serverUiReach). The runtime marker must precede the first\nvalue import; erased type imports do not count.\n\n* fix(rules): look up an import alias by its imported name; classify per call; erase inline type imports\n\n`import { X as Y }` is looked up as X in the source module. A classification\ndepends on every file it follows, so only parses are cached and a change in\na schema''s source file is seen inside one ESLint process. `import { type M }`\nis erased like `import type`, so the runtime marker may follow it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo8mbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvrMQABNzHaKp1ZgfBfD5vRSvU8wU\nqEdNs7OIZQGpLeNKYtC99JrNMD48dtiHrS2NmsgcC/Cc7Z7AeVTPbsuIgW1AeuIA\nyG6sIEIV4s3sjlvEfQg28VE+i3T0uhtA2JtoDSjSuWkSehih6W7e/um18hm+2zM4\nWcaeCcwp3kQ2qsqT87oLpvzlbSwO6DZsyHEkdbOAlE1u/6GuhV9LSFRKBQsExjuA\nKZbFgSx0whMJgHyztU+LPTdAFC9z98qtmE1/uT8fh5xfI/UIIEGDqYUal6o9mXdz\nrZej0AkTg4KVCVlSEzKUp/GOGTpmIdQvE88qBP6+zDry787+ubW5zKfsJ+7uvL6t\n5EFBGhfNlq0GIuVkPqpbtTbJFI1Ssh5HKGCk3i8DuhzS9y1QmRAkb5kpEbw+nwFS\ncLWiZLP0oSDcwI5jB06+xnajK2ExfV+p6JXYRDnRE0z4rS+aWRXXum/+Xi8N2hHH\nYcrqWqn2jsR8ltC45x6/QCb1RERZB4iLZYDRQCWQTRBfEm29gEpggjZm69szbtdD\nrFPEaevMlLs4c+nNOPrIbawalMlQSHYReauIkksjE1BQTaEqOUJ6K5B8NRoH3b1E\n6MruJnv4Pji2mNa8Jaz/W0LNG5eNoGB+4mC12znJpNeXVBV1r1Bn0xIQcxjxrokV\nTQWJQknyks8fgXTYP/Xn\n=yTCM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T09:27:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commit/e59a84492085847c60b748fe5e86d3edb8aaac9a","node_id":"C_kwDOSDZWYNoAKGU1OWE4NDQ5MjA4NTg0N2M2MGI3NDhmZTVlODZkM2VkYjhhYWFjOWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commit/e2f21d0390755dbd045216eb3ef83ec0c7451fe8","sha":"e2f21d0390755dbd045216eb3ef83ec0c7451fe8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/e2f21d0390755dbd045216eb3ef83ec0c7451fe8"}],"sha":"e59a84492085847c60b748fe5e86d3edb8aaac9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/e59a84492085847c60b748fe5e86d3edb8aaac9a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15245608?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix","id":15245608,"login":"clicktronix","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjQ1NjA4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/e2f21d0390755dbd045216eb3ef83ec0c7451fe8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T09:25:32Z","email":"s28.morgan@gmail.com","name":"Vladislav Manakov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T09:25:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(migration)!: the session owns the migration; workflows shrink to inventory and verify (#24)\n\n* feat(migration)!: the session owns the migration; workflows shrink to inventory and verify\n\nReplaces prepare-architecture-migration and migrate-capability with the\nmigrating-architecture skill, bin/migration.mjs and two small workflows.\nThe script lists files, expands coverage rules, computes destinations,\nscreens plans, runs the target''s check as an owned child process with a\nrecord of command, exit code and tree state, counts the census and decides\nthe gate. Agents remain for judgement: six lenses, one assignment, one\nreviewer, an advisory radius, and per-slice movers.\n\nA repeated slice failure returns to the owner; a silent reviewer is no\nverdict; cap-reached is a budget; a grown radius is a note; should-fix\nreaches the owner; blocking lint entries are scoped to migrated roots.\n\nvalidate-workflows.mjs runs the two scripts as scenarios;\nvalidate-migration-lib.mjs unit-tests the script, including a 301-file\ntree with a loose file beside two 150-file children.\n\n* fix(migration): records survive signals and large trees; paths cannot leave the project\n\nTree state is a git tree object built in a temporary index, so a quoted\npath or a multi-megabyte diff cannot hide a change; the check runs in its\nown process group with output streamed to the record file, and a signal to\nthe wrapper reaches the check and still leaves a record naming it.\ndestination and plan screening refuse a capability that is not one\nkebab-case segment and a module root outside the project. plan-check reads\nwhat expand wrote. census reports scope, never a clean zero for a slice it\nwas not given, and zero-fills baseline keys so 1 -> 0 is measured.\nAn exhausted reviewer is no verdict, with its partial findings kept. The\nCLI runs through a symlinked path. Validator scenarios hand the script a\nfile list and prove it never reaches an agent. One lint run per tree state.\n\n* fix(migration): a record waits for its check, binds its artifacts, and sees force-added files\n\nA forwarded signal is followed by waiting for the process group to end\n(SIGKILL after a grace period) before the record is written, so a record\nnever describes a check still running; the record carries the child pid.\nArtifacts named with --artifact are hashed into the record and census reads\na lint JSON only while its hash matches — a swapped file under the same\nrecord id is refused. The temporary index starts from the repository''s\nindex, so a file force-added in an ignored directory counts. Every recipe\nin the skill carries its full context. The cancel test checks the recorded\npid instead of searching the machine by name.\n\n* fix(migration): artifacts live in the run''s own empty directory; a record waits for the whole group\n\nAn artifact hashed after the command proved nothing about who wrote it: a\ngreen JSON left over from an earlier run was accepted under a new record.\nEach record now creates an empty <id>.artifacts directory, exports it as\n$NCS_ARTIFACTS, and binds only files found there — a command that did not\nwrite the file leaves a record saying so, and census refuses it.\n\nAfter a forwarded signal the wrapper no longer finishes on the leader''s\nexit: a grandchild that ignored SIGTERM kept running with the record\nalready written. It polls the process group, sends SIGKILL to the group\nafter --kill-after, and writes the record only when nothing in the group\nanswers. The lib test reproduces both with a shell leader and a node\ngrandchild ignoring SIGTERM.\n\nREADME: reviewerBudget is a brief-level turn count, not a runtime limit;\nthe \"missing record\" scenario proves the argument guard, freshness is the\nCLI''s.\n\n* fix(migration): escalate from the signal, not the leader''s exit; claim the run id exclusively\n\nA shell leader that ignores SIGTERM never exits, so a group watch started\non its exit never started and the record never came. The watch now starts\nthe moment a signal is forwarded, SIGKILLs the group after --kill-after,\nand writes the record once no member answers; the test bounds the wait\nfrom above as well as below. Two runs in one millisecond with the same\nlabel and command shared an id and an artifact directory; the id is now\nclaimed by creating that directory exclusively, with a random suffix on\ncollision. Recipes single-quote the check so $NCS_ARTIFACTS expands in the\nchild; the README no longer promises a runtime reviewer limit or a file\ncheck the workflow cannot make.\n\n* fix(migration): observing a group is not cancelling it; the recipe chains checks with &&\n\nA leader that exited normally with a child still running was watched with\nthe cancellation deadline, so the child was SIGKILLed and the record said\nexitCode 0. The deadline now starts only when a signal is forwarded; a\nnatural exit waits for the group with no kill and reports the leader''s\ncode, and a record carries `killed` so a kill can never read as success.\nThe reference recipe joined lint to tests with `;`, which let a red lint\nend in a green exit code; it is `&&` throughout.","tree":{"sha":"e8416d6ddfcff3c06fe4831c648a2f0cd17f2b03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/trees/e8416d6ddfcff3c06fe4831c648a2f0cd17f2b03"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/commits/e2f21d0390755dbd045216eb3ef83ec0c7451fe8","verification":{"payload":"tree e8416d6ddfcff3c06fe4831c648a2f0cd17f2b03\nparent d3f89d78f643ba99bcd3a114e2dd37ad6c5c2788\nauthor Vladislav Manakov <s28.morgan@gmail.com> 1789118732 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789118732 +0500\n\nfeat(migration)!: the session owns the migration; workflows shrink to inventory and verify (#24)\n\n* feat(migration)!: the session owns the migration; workflows shrink to inventory and verify\n\nReplaces prepare-architecture-migration and migrate-capability with the\nmigrating-architecture skill, bin/migration.mjs and two small workflows.\nThe script lists files, expands coverage rules, computes destinations,\nscreens plans, runs the target''s check as an owned child process with a\nrecord of command, exit code and tree state, counts the census and decides\nthe gate. Agents remain for judgement: six lenses, one assignment, one\nreviewer, an advisory radius, and per-slice movers.\n\nA repeated slice failure returns to the owner; a silent reviewer is no\nverdict; cap-reached is a budget; a grown radius is a note; should-fix\nreaches the owner; blocking lint entries are scoped to migrated roots.\n\nvalidate-workflows.mjs runs the two scripts as scenarios;\nvalidate-migration-lib.mjs unit-tests the script, including a 301-file\ntree with a loose file beside two 150-file children.\n\n* fix(migration): records survive signals and large trees; paths cannot leave the project\n\nTree state is a git tree object built in a temporary index, so a quoted\npath or a multi-megabyte diff cannot hide a change; the check runs in its\nown process group with output streamed to the record file, and a signal to\nthe wrapper reaches the check and still leaves a record naming it.\ndestination and plan screening refuse a capability that is not one\nkebab-case segment and a module root outside the project. plan-check reads\nwhat expand wrote. census reports scope, never a clean zero for a slice it\nwas not given, and zero-fills baseline keys so 1 -> 0 is measured.\nAn exhausted reviewer is no verdict, with its partial findings kept. The\nCLI runs through a symlinked path. Validator scenarios hand the script a\nfile list and prove it never reaches an agent. One lint run per tree state.\n\n* fix(migration): a record waits for its check, binds its artifacts, and sees force-added files\n\nA forwarded signal is followed by waiting for the process group to end\n(SIGKILL after a grace period) before the record is written, so a record\nnever describes a check still running; the record carries the child pid.\nArtifacts named with --artifact are hashed into the record and census reads\na lint JSON only while its hash matches — a swapped file under the same\nrecord id is refused. The temporary index starts from the repository''s\nindex, so a file force-added in an ignored directory counts. Every recipe\nin the skill carries its full context. The cancel test checks the recorded\npid instead of searching the machine by name.\n\n* fix(migration): artifacts live in the run''s own empty directory; a record waits for the whole group\n\nAn artifact hashed after the command proved nothing about who wrote it: a\ngreen JSON left over from an earlier run was accepted under a new record.\nEach record now creates an empty <id>.artifacts directory, exports it as\n$NCS_ARTIFACTS, and binds only files found there — a command that did not\nwrite the file leaves a record saying so, and census refuses it.\n\nAfter a forwarded signal the wrapper no longer finishes on the leader''s\nexit: a grandchild that ignored SIGTERM kept running with the record\nalready written. It polls the process group, sends SIGKILL to the group\nafter --kill-after, and writes the record only when nothing in the group\nanswers. The lib test reproduces both with a shell leader and a node\ngrandchild ignoring SIGTERM.\n\nREADME: reviewerBudget is a brief-level turn count, not a runtime limit;\nthe \"missing record\" scenario proves the argument guard, freshness is the\nCLI''s.\n\n* fix(migration): escalate from the signal, not the leader''s exit; claim the run id exclusively\n\nA shell leader that ignores SIGTERM never exits, so a group watch started\non its exit never started and the record never came. The watch now starts\nthe moment a signal is forwarded, SIGKILLs the group after --kill-after,\nand writes the record once no member answers; the test bounds the wait\nfrom above as well as below. Two runs in one millisecond with the same\nlabel and command shared an id and an artifact directory; the id is now\nclaimed by creating that directory exclusively, with a random suffix on\ncollision. Recipes single-quote the check so $NCS_ARTIFACTS expands in the\nchild; the README no longer promises a runtime reviewer limit or a file\ncheck the workflow cannot make.\n\n* fix(migration): observing a group is not cancelling it; the recipe chains checks with &&\n\nA leader that exited normally with a child still running was watched with\nthe cancellation deadline, so the child was SIGKILLed and the record said\nexitCode 0. The deadline now starts only when a signal is forwarded; a\nnatural exit waits for the group with no kill and reports the leader''s\ncode, and a record carries `killed` so a kill can never read as success.\nThe reference recipe joined lint to tests with `;`, which let a red lint\nend in a green exit code; it is `&&` throughout.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo8kMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQgMQAKng0rpNviohVCCa6oT+KCKW\ngdh1lK4hsy+MuVKiAuGCJsJPmqJkpJeprkAS41LjkmaDyXICt94iscJeohSxEr+E\nEx/icjh2GNXOKqxO16mVfwpVCbcGgpsUwrp2hNUuVYe8s5eyfzjMx2RrT+MXRZ1q\nwAN7ccU6m1+/p9rmLyrNAM+RHQzpu8v5YymJUD9o1J3V4KyvFyVYke1BVuWMxqfL\nOZW3VyhGqLbpKSzVDyBM9h1K3P2e/0UC5UB8qnjMGi6PhL/ejL9zoSPLQJqNnTIM\nJwwlnnN+YP5YjhTy6p2ZCChoTKjErUUkF+rbR7wuH/2fp+qyscvcbgrQ09t/CkB3\nwR+GJt7yPXmUK3ACxTrvsfm5XcONU5c7R6LNWca5YIc5X6oHUTwRAblaKpc0+lB7\n8zcR+ipoYyGZb7ETYXSe+q3JPjsj7A55d8eY9ANqcEPM9rOevXS+X8tRnDjiiO5y\nlhdaGcfarY8nzseqX+FmbdPiXcm1Ec5Yy6jSm0l3BW0MxkCOZ36b0OYclmLWxWSt\nov+TnnPi/hP2Z8P75KM0XXItkS7ckDnxtbIA/L94DCiqSPZ4QaOqa1iBB6QiyAvp\nnmIKdWBGiAhl/D7M8CXFL0JPq3ewoiz5SweYN7HEa+wFhpaqT4SCeopFMI6O6g6H\nHXwa/5JzLFLXm9si04Lx\n=BcM8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T09:25:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commit/e2f21d0390755dbd045216eb3ef83ec0c7451fe8","node_id":"C_kwDOSDZWYNoAKGUyZjIxZDAzOTA3NTVkYmQwNDUyMTZlYjNlZjgzZWMwYzc0NTFmZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commit/d3f89d78f643ba99bcd3a114e2dd37ad6c5c2788","sha":"d3f89d78f643ba99bcd3a114e2dd37ad6c5c2788","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/d3f89d78f643ba99bcd3a114e2dd37ad6c5c2788"}],"sha":"e2f21d0390755dbd045216eb3ef83ec0c7451fe8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/e2f21d0390755dbd045216eb3ef83ec0c7451fe8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15245608?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix","id":15245608,"login":"clicktronix","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjQ1NjA4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/d3f89d78f643ba99bcd3a114e2dd37ad6c5c2788/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T09:22:47Z","email":"s28.morgan@gmail.com","name":"Vladislav Manakov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T09:22:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(evidence): isolate eval cells, anonymise private provenance, move raw results out of git (#23)\n\n* fix(evidence): isolate eval cells, anonymise private provenance, move raw results out of git\n\nEvery eval cell inherited HOME, so the \"no skill\" arm could read the author''s\n~/.agents/skills; seven committed result sets show it doing so. Cells now run\nwith a fresh HOME and CODEX_HOME through scripts/eval-env.mjs, asserted by\nvalidate-eval-isolation.mjs with a canary that the old environment leaks.\nThe affected release conclusions are marked not reproducible as stated.\n\ndocs/evidence.md loses private product names and commits (treatment B:\nnumbers and conclusions stay); lint-provenance.mjs refuses them on every\nshipped surface. tests/architecture-evals/results leaves the tree and ships\nas a release asset.\n\n* fix(evidence): keep PATH in eval cells; name the release the archive ships with\n\nStripping home-owned PATH entries found an absolute codex but not the node\nits #!/usr/bin/env line needs under nvm, npm prefix or bun. PATH finds\nexecutables, not configuration, so it stays; the validator now asserts node\nresolves through the cell PATH. There is no GitHub release for 4.1.0, so the\nraw result archive ships with 4.2.0 under one name in README and script.\n\n* docs(evidence): the archive is not yet attached; say what the isolation check does not prove","tree":{"sha":"983787270f35a6dc6f5cbbeaeb2eb0e016d32e12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/trees/983787270f35a6dc6f5cbbeaeb2eb0e016d32e12"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/commits/d3f89d78f643ba99bcd3a114e2dd37ad6c5c2788","verification":{"payload":"tree 983787270f35a6dc6f5cbbeaeb2eb0e016d32e12\nparent 77ea43940e2c96673527ba17b1cc014cb681a03d\nauthor Vladislav Manakov <s28.morgan@gmail.com> 1789118567 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789118567 +0500\n\nfix(evidence): isolate eval cells, anonymise private provenance, move raw results out of git (#23)\n\n* fix(evidence): isolate eval cells, anonymise private provenance, move raw results out of git\n\nEvery eval cell inherited HOME, so the \"no skill\" arm could read the author''s\n~/.agents/skills; seven committed result sets show it doing so. Cells now run\nwith a fresh HOME and CODEX_HOME through scripts/eval-env.mjs, asserted by\nvalidate-eval-isolation.mjs with a canary that the old environment leaks.\nThe affected release conclusions are marked not reproducible as stated.\n\ndocs/evidence.md loses private product names and commits (treatment B:\nnumbers and conclusions stay); lint-provenance.mjs refuses them on every\nshipped surface. tests/architecture-evals/results leaves the tree and ships\nas a release asset.\n\n* fix(evidence): keep PATH in eval cells; name the release the archive ships with\n\nStripping home-owned PATH entries found an absolute codex but not the node\nits #!/usr/bin/env line needs under nvm, npm prefix or bun. PATH finds\nexecutables, not configuration, so it stays; the validator now asserts node\nresolves through the cell PATH. There is no GitHub release for 4.1.0, so the\nraw result archive ships with 4.2.0 under one name in README and script.\n\n* docs(evidence): the archive is not yet attached; say what the isolation check does not prove","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo8hnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZmoQAEBzFgTB5Zn0hAedGghO6Mf3\n2fKJoLvj++giSTPrnarYcrWlw9GprqvclIbrc/dvlWWocouXDgqBMzxSVoN8H8JF\ntcUxeWKg+H9f7VIgFPmhCUlKIyB9tbvLVZ+HTHCTptX9wa5NJ0eDybWu1pyOBw6d\nlUjGoMusHQQ1wiyHigJPhcSw0vbmTSU2m/KzTAkK+QLZQwu1BU5L4mXvn0Y8+cD7\nNc+3r817xXZvmbNKTKlM4vHQnMrnbFZrORRpXLBbId6/KSjZacqoMDpg9W4KzJjt\nnLpJYF9Kx/VlzWbSdLvPe+jT3p9bN6VdzvQRtRRHfaYy/OaqrqrLgPjrqohiZD9r\nOa0CoyGx0lg5Iq82SH0fRcKr1MShD3tghjS12mpr2OOhCra14bd3/jgcDl4fFaAZ\n3y6Js4Ef4lbA9B9VXkAFL8OrUIl3usZtdtaKtHGdythZWcFFGq6oGeep7sFfEK7/\ndJizbPyNvrDCxWKs8CyWWPEiCo8R4qvQ8CdJyVsBVnnef1v3YHR7K7042PPPGsdB\nbK/+IhCy7ktMDx7XXFBNA3+8V2dX9w2uFrzhBQE1M6LfW90fp1fzPADFZxG+mtx+\npNTXzEOexBXN0qmip9gX8SLn1s8xgpUyvU8tFzSaYWzYH8Rr6AO56U2XWVRJruTq\nRFZgbXpDJVm+QUwg9eZx\n=hlT2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T09:22:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commit/d3f89d78f643ba99bcd3a114e2dd37ad6c5c2788","node_id":"C_kwDOSDZWYNoAKGQzZjg5ZDc4ZjY0M2JhOTliY2QzYTExNGUyZGQzN2FkNmM1YzI3ODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commit/77ea43940e2c96673527ba17b1cc014cb681a03d","sha":"77ea43940e2c96673527ba17b1cc014cb681a03d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/77ea43940e2c96673527ba17b1cc014cb681a03d"}],"sha":"d3f89d78f643ba99bcd3a114e2dd37ad6c5c2788","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/d3f89d78f643ba99bcd3a114e2dd37ad6c5c2788"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15245608?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix","id":15245608,"login":"clicktronix","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjQ1NjA4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/77ea43940e2c96673527ba17b1cc014cb681a03d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T14:58:22Z","email":"s28.morgan@gmail.com","name":"Vladislav Manakov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T14:58:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(workflows): enumerate the inventory instead of summarising it (#22)\n\n* fix(workflows): enumerate the inventory instead of summarising it\n\nPhase 1 could not run against a large repository, and failed in a way that\nblamed the wrong step. On a 2210-file target the roots lens returned 808\ndirectories as its file list — while its own findings carried the correct\ncount — and Assign, asked for a row per file, returned 497 rows for those\n808 inputs without reporting a failure. The run died two phases later at the\npartition gate, naming directories nobody can own.\n\nBoth are one defect: a summary standing in for an enumeration, from an agent\nwhose output has to scale with the repository.\n\nSeparate the two things that were conflated. Listing is mechanical, so fan it\nout: the roots lens returns a partition of the source tree (non-overlapping\nsubtrees, each under 300 files) plus a total counted over the whole root, and\none agent lists each subtree. The total is taken before any subtree is listed,\nso a short listing fails in Inventory rather than passing quietly.\n\nDeciding stays one agent over the whole tree — the barrier is unchanged — but\nit answers with coverage rules, prefix or file, resolved by specificity. The\nscript expands them against the inventory, so rules track decisions rather than\nfile count, and an uncovered file stops the run. A broad prefix that longer\nrules override is doing its job; only a rule matching no file is rejected.\n\nTouched beyond the minimum: the manifest writer still receives one payload, so\nits size limit is untested and left alone.\n\nRefs marqa-tech/platform#813\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012Cx6xu7aqiJMSjTq3XfraX\n\n* fix(workflows): ask the roots lens for the partition its schema requires\n\nThe schema stopped requiring `files` but the prompt still asked for it, so the\nlens was being told to enumerate and then rejected for not partitioning — the\nsame \"blamed for the wrong step\" failure this branch exists to remove, one\nlevel up.\n\nThe new assertion reads the prompt as the call site passes it, alongside the\nschema, because only the schema was ever machine-checked.\n\nRefs marqa-tech/platform#813\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012Cx6xu7aqiJMSjTq3XfraX\n\n* fix(workflows): let an unassigned file carry a suggested placement\n\nThe gate treated \"here is where it would go, and I still cannot commit to it\"\nas a contradiction. On the first full live run it was the most useful answer in\nthe set: a Supabase realtime module that is a generic table-changes wrapper and\nalso exports two offers-capability subscriptions. The agent gave it a placement\nand listed it as unassigned. The run died on that one row after 37 minutes and\n133 agents, having produced 405 rules and 17 capabilities that nobody got to\nsee.\n\nNothing in the prompt forbade it either, so the refusal was over a rule the\nagent was never told.\n\nUnassigned wins — expansion already skips those files, so the placement stays a\nnote and never becomes an owner.\n\nRefs marqa-tech/platform#813\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012Cx6xu7aqiJMSjTq3XfraX\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"85d5319db0adf23886aecba52dd6e83baa6cfdb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/trees/85d5319db0adf23886aecba52dd6e83baa6cfdb5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/commits/77ea43940e2c96673527ba17b1cc014cb681a03d","verification":{"payload":"tree 85d5319db0adf23886aecba52dd6e83baa6cfdb5\nparent 134ce277ab27c13275d21172a4bbaa6a0373074f\nauthor Vladislav Manakov <s28.morgan@gmail.com> 1789052302 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789052302 +0500\n\nfix(workflows): enumerate the inventory instead of summarising it (#22)\n\n* fix(workflows): enumerate the inventory instead of summarising it\n\nPhase 1 could not run against a large repository, and failed in a way that\nblamed the wrong step. On a 2210-file target the roots lens returned 808\ndirectories as its file list — while its own findings carried the correct\ncount — and Assign, asked for a row per file, returned 497 rows for those\n808 inputs without reporting a failure. The run died two phases later at the\npartition gate, naming directories nobody can own.\n\nBoth are one defect: a summary standing in for an enumeration, from an agent\nwhose output has to scale with the repository.\n\nSeparate the two things that were conflated. Listing is mechanical, so fan it\nout: the roots lens returns a partition of the source tree (non-overlapping\nsubtrees, each under 300 files) plus a total counted over the whole root, and\none agent lists each subtree. The total is taken before any subtree is listed,\nso a short listing fails in Inventory rather than passing quietly.\n\nDeciding stays one agent over the whole tree — the barrier is unchanged — but\nit answers with coverage rules, prefix or file, resolved by specificity. The\nscript expands them against the inventory, so rules track decisions rather than\nfile count, and an uncovered file stops the run. A broad prefix that longer\nrules override is doing its job; only a rule matching no file is rejected.\n\nTouched beyond the minimum: the manifest writer still receives one payload, so\nits size limit is untested and left alone.\n\nRefs marqa-tech/platform#813\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012Cx6xu7aqiJMSjTq3XfraX\n\n* fix(workflows): ask the roots lens for the partition its schema requires\n\nThe schema stopped requiring `files` but the prompt still asked for it, so the\nlens was being told to enumerate and then rejected for not partitioning — the\nsame \"blamed for the wrong step\" failure this branch exists to remove, one\nlevel up.\n\nThe new assertion reads the prompt as the call site passes it, alongside the\nschema, because only the schema was ever machine-checked.\n\nRefs marqa-tech/platform#813\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012Cx6xu7aqiJMSjTq3XfraX\n\n* fix(workflows): let an unassigned file carry a suggested placement\n\nThe gate treated \"here is where it would go, and I still cannot commit to it\"\nas a contradiction. On the first full live run it was the most useful answer in\nthe set: a Supabase realtime module that is a generic table-changes wrapper and\nalso exports two offers-capability subscriptions. The agent gave it a placement\nand listed it as unassigned. The run died on that one row after 37 minutes and\n133 agents, having produced 405 rules and 17 capabilities that nobody got to\nsee.\n\nNothing in the prompt forbade it either, so the refusal was over a rule the\nagent was never told.\n\nUnassigned wins — expansion already skips those files, so the placement stays a\nnote and never becomes an owner.\n\nRefs marqa-tech/platform#813\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012Cx6xu7aqiJMSjTq3XfraX\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqosWOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAW+EQAC0UDX3uDhbpIVGw2a6GAxSG\nDJTYMZoQEQWJjYRkLBEASliH8KT4d05BeWdQcUnrqT8lKjMSBaxANRLbzee/QIq5\ng4RHnwPBwwq0Df2dizehEC3WUlwzPJXc5ZB//m46FxWJB4dIo/cD0Y9uRNR81CaW\nNuHrJ+bgYscH9MjBTyqwnabXpzvgb0vLMsQUFm2BSTS6OGGSPvo0Di51/TCZ4Biu\n0Y2PgabiMQhZ1adOh4fFalah+CBNW0cH0d+mJVbY5b3WMyehe+VNmwJ8eP/4V3ls\nTFlVxZxaIEa5unewz0O7dDbBt4IbrqRiTZPEwqKeShb1ek91vf/VLbhpCJ4e4u8V\nhvJM0+v9wvyV8+lMML7PV6O2TLxs4TPl7hxHyf5yE60IxoX7+KhiForjESCqS3SZ\nW3NmaaQ6WF0eTK1EgyCLoC4nm5YudlxwskdE0QpLPmnR5Mbv8GpWd1WjMwi5/tEG\n3ev9GCwz/OvJGtCS0NwvaJM7Xgk2vwugx133LU7my988gQYjQFBPIEV1Wjb4c1V/\nrNXXqFhQ0PQc61e0fScihJN1aBBtnJYreVjLXb2NY68ODiqlixKJt2nQSNmkzYHV\ndtKTI7l2GqxBeY86IVjDCwK68Sagf1eiW6VussekU9NeQcEUs0pnonePdFCSgDiG\nFf/qCPMK9zGIJnoa8cER\n=qbm8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-10T14:58:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commit/77ea43940e2c96673527ba17b1cc014cb681a03d","node_id":"C_kwDOSDZWYNoAKDc3ZWE0Mzk0MGUyYzk2NjczNTI3YmExN2IxY2MwMTRjYjY4MWEwM2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commit/134ce277ab27c13275d21172a4bbaa6a0373074f","sha":"134ce277ab27c13275d21172a4bbaa6a0373074f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/134ce277ab27c13275d21172a4bbaa6a0373074f"}],"sha":"77ea43940e2c96673527ba17b1cc014cb681a03d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/77ea43940e2c96673527ba17b1cc014cb681a03d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15245608?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix","id":15245608,"login":"clicktronix","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjQ1NjA4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/134ce277ab27c13275d21172a4bbaa6a0373074f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T08:10:34Z","email":"s28.morgan@gmail.com","name":"Vladislav Manakov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T08:10:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Harden and simplify capability-first architecture migration (#21)\n\n* Unblock phase 2 screening in migrate-capability\n\nThe first real run of migrate-capability rejected a correct plan before any\nwrite, twice, for three separate reasons in the screening step.\n\n1. `unknownSources` refused files planned with role=stay. The plan prompt\n   explicitly asks for role=stay on app-root files, which phase 1 assigns\n   placement \"app\" and never to a capability — so obeying the prompt\n   guaranteed rejection. `stay` is the one role that writes nothing, so it\n   is now exempt; every other role still refuses an unassigned file.\n\n2. `strayConsumers` required every surface consumer to appear in the\n   manifest''s recorded list, which is not satisfiable: phase 1 records\n   external consumers at page granularity, while a correct plan also names\n   route-private app files and — for query-cache, whose whole purpose is one\n   key identity shared by server prefetch and browser query — consumers\n   inside the capability. Three narrow admissions replace the exact match,\n   plus trimming a trailing annotation. A relaxed \"any path under the source\n   root\" was tried first and correctly rejected by the existing mutation\n   test that feeds an invented `src/app/invented.tsx`.\n\n3. The load agent copied the manifest''s consumer list verbatim. That list is\n   demonstrably incomplete — server-actions/labels.ts consumes work-items\n   cache tags, yet `labels` is absent from the recorded consumers — so it now\n   completes the list by grepping for real importers, including ones owned by\n   another capability.\n\nThe planner prompt is tightened alongside: bare repo-relative paths, one per\nentry, and an explicit statement that an unassigned file may appear only with\nrole=stay.\n\nnpm run validate passes 17/17, including the capability-pilot mutation suite.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Enforce shared admission and neutral-surface consumers\n\n* Make the pilot gate legible and name what is left\n\n* Declare the channel changes the architecture forces\n\n* Give the operator the answers the run asks for\n\n* Guard generated provider contracts behind their adapters\n\n* Address the two-axis review\n\n* Share one import resolver and widen the count check\n\n* Stop the admission check recommending deletion of live code\n\n* Waive regressions per counter and refuse undecided deps before writing\n\n* Read each capability''s layout from the tree, not from the manifest\n\n* Stop reading a dead agent as a reporting one\n\n* Admit only consumers that exist and make the channel assessment mandatory\n\n* Classify neutral-surface consumers by the effective module graph\n\n* Resolve emitted specifiers per extension and give exemptions a reason\n\n* Record the review round in the changelog\n\n* Make the two shipped checks agree and read one extension inventory\n\n* Ground every surface in a real consumer and carry unplaced files into phase 2\n\n* Count every source extension in the layout probe\n\n* Stop the runtimes flowing into each other and the aliases grounding themselves\n\n* Count capabilities, share one module graph, route every unplaced file\n\n* Give each check the edge view it needs and fail closed on what none can judge\n\n* refactor: simplify architecture skill and enforcement\n\n* Simplify skill decision guidance\n\n* Harden architecture migration handoff\n\n* fix: preserve named capabilities in cycle checks\n\n* fix: clarify architecture review decisions\n\n* test: bind architecture evaluation inputs\n\n* fix: reject overloaded capability ownership\n\n* test: record ownership decision baseline\n\n* test: record ownership decision correction\n\n* docs: keep domain helpers capability-owned\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"eb7d666d5b20eee8f056c395ffd93d9c3f057959","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/trees/eb7d666d5b20eee8f056c395ffd93d9c3f057959"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/commits/134ce277ab27c13275d21172a4bbaa6a0373074f","verification":{"payload":"tree eb7d666d5b20eee8f056c395ffd93d9c3f057959\nparent 510dd771344e9f876de03ee4e445022bddfaa50f\nauthor Vladislav Manakov <s28.morgan@gmail.com> 1788163834 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788163834 +0500\n\nHarden and simplify capability-first architecture migration (#21)\n\n* Unblock phase 2 screening in migrate-capability\n\nThe first real run of migrate-capability rejected a correct plan before any\nwrite, twice, for three separate reasons in the screening step.\n\n1. `unknownSources` refused files planned with role=stay. The plan prompt\n   explicitly asks for role=stay on app-root files, which phase 1 assigns\n   placement \"app\" and never to a capability — so obeying the prompt\n   guaranteed rejection. `stay` is the one role that writes nothing, so it\n   is now exempt; every other role still refuses an unassigned file.\n\n2. `strayConsumers` required every surface consumer to appear in the\n   manifest''s recorded list, which is not satisfiable: phase 1 records\n   external consumers at page granularity, while a correct plan also names\n   route-private app files and — for query-cache, whose whole purpose is one\n   key identity shared by server prefetch and browser query — consumers\n   inside the capability. Three narrow admissions replace the exact match,\n   plus trimming a trailing annotation. A relaxed \"any path under the source\n   root\" was tried first and correctly rejected by the existing mutation\n   test that feeds an invented `src/app/invented.tsx`.\n\n3. The load agent copied the manifest''s consumer list verbatim. That list is\n   demonstrably incomplete — server-actions/labels.ts consumes work-items\n   cache tags, yet `labels` is absent from the recorded consumers — so it now\n   completes the list by grepping for real importers, including ones owned by\n   another capability.\n\nThe planner prompt is tightened alongside: bare repo-relative paths, one per\nentry, and an explicit statement that an unassigned file may appear only with\nrole=stay.\n\nnpm run validate passes 17/17, including the capability-pilot mutation suite.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Enforce shared admission and neutral-surface consumers\n\n* Make the pilot gate legible and name what is left\n\n* Declare the channel changes the architecture forces\n\n* Give the operator the answers the run asks for\n\n* Guard generated provider contracts behind their adapters\n\n* Address the two-axis review\n\n* Share one import resolver and widen the count check\n\n* Stop the admission check recommending deletion of live code\n\n* Waive regressions per counter and refuse undecided deps before writing\n\n* Read each capability''s layout from the tree, not from the manifest\n\n* Stop reading a dead agent as a reporting one\n\n* Admit only consumers that exist and make the channel assessment mandatory\n\n* Classify neutral-surface consumers by the effective module graph\n\n* Resolve emitted specifiers per extension and give exemptions a reason\n\n* Record the review round in the changelog\n\n* Make the two shipped checks agree and read one extension inventory\n\n* Ground every surface in a real consumer and carry unplaced files into phase 2\n\n* Count every source extension in the layout probe\n\n* Stop the runtimes flowing into each other and the aliases grounding themselves\n\n* Count capabilities, share one module graph, route every unplaced file\n\n* Give each check the edge view it needs and fail closed on what none can judge\n\n* refactor: simplify architecture skill and enforcement\n\n* Simplify skill decision guidance\n\n* Harden architecture migration handoff\n\n* fix: preserve named capabilities in cycle checks\n\n* fix: clarify architecture review decisions\n\n* test: bind architecture evaluation inputs\n\n* fix: reject overloaded capability ownership\n\n* test: record ownership decision baseline\n\n* test: record ownership decision correction\n\n* docs: keep domain helpers capability-owned\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlTb6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzdYQAKJzKk0UInA64ZAKvYAy0bPP\nJJNG5h/ZXf3WLkoemyV2ZT6fOt4rQVV6Q4WR9vyB3kdTCsYfGoaQtVOAe1v8OA0q\nQyE1WRmuP/2BWEDERSoYg2F9vs/hW933DG7Hpj5JMi1Ul4D8+Z3AF9Ah4a0T9NPt\nm1nM0AuxzyDPj55R6bzCcRr0chcAIiZAjKes27P8Sj3erfzB3qBhvzAUZQAngZ7C\n66uQ6OeufTaFmFaAyN7gwhQSXxTH2+jbNLZuW2Wsu2v33D3GJP0B4FR9DYFDybAR\nCBiTMUZNREJAn1N4ZUf57+OVYEI2hVuFRFiyHQyHMJcoMylW/KZyfzitIUTNgG/O\n7ubP36Eaz9qYmdcoIk9zhvKTGLkUBmSr7FovdVj/ABhTlkJOdUDw84nrGewq3Eek\nOJt9VhxsRf67eDBQPfgfCqQBCf5Rz9QF/RjSJNnrB3goBTAHByK8aS5MTVTEgdta\n1ouBPju/FbVwyZR