=7XB9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-08T16:04:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commit/510dd771344e9f876de03ee4e445022bddfaa50f","node_id":"C_kwDOSDZWYNoAKDUxMGRkNzcxMzQ0ZTlmODc2ZGUwM2VlNGU0NDUwMjJiZGRmYWE1MGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commit/8eaac2decb8abfa7d50f6dc02b1fd0b92f836426","sha":"8eaac2decb8abfa7d50f6dc02b1fd0b92f836426","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/8eaac2decb8abfa7d50f6dc02b1fd0b92f836426"}],"sha":"510dd771344e9f876de03ee4e445022bddfaa50f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/510dd771344e9f876de03ee4e445022bddfaa50f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15245608?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix","id":15245608,"login":"clicktronix","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjQ1NjA4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/8eaac2decb8abfa7d50f6dc02b1fd0b92f836426/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T17:29:58Z","email":"s28.morgan@gmail.com","name":"Vladislav Manakov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T17:29:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add capability-first migration workflows (#19)\n\nMaintainer tooling under .claude/workflows/: two multi-agent workflows that adopt\nthe capability-first architecture in an existing Next.js repository, plus a repo\ncheck that keeps them honest. They execute the procedure already written in\ndocs/adoption-and-enforcement.md rather than inventing a second one; where the two\ndisagree, the document wins and the script is the defect. Not part of the\npublished plugin.\n\n10-migration-baseline inventories the target through six blind lenses, assigns\nevery source file one owner, role and runtime class, installs rules/ with a\ndrafted contract, and records the behavioural baseline plus a per-messageId\nviolation census. 20-migration-pilot migrates one capability against three\noracles - the target''s own typecheck/lint/tests/production build, rules/ as a\nburndown against that census, and an adversarial review of the properties static\nrules cannot prove - then stops at the human accept/revise/reject gate.\n\nDestinations are arithmetic, not judgement: agents decide a file''s role and the\nscript computes the path, screened for three properties before the first write -\nadmitted (nothing outside the contract vocabulary), closed (nothing resolves\noutside moduleRoot/<capability>/), injective (no two sources on one destination).\nAn oracle that did not report is never a verdict; reject belongs to the review\noracle alone and dominates the other two.\n\nFour review passes: one single-reviewer, one two-axis (standards + spec), and a\nworkflow-backed pass whose findings were recovered in full from the run journal\nafter its ten-finding cap dropped 28 of 38 survivors. Everything found is fixed.\nThe recurring defect across all four was assertions that cannot fail - a source\ntext grep standing in for a behavioural check - which is why the validator now\nhas two layers: extracted regions executed against tables to prove the logic is\ncorrect, and each body run against stubbed hooks to prove it is called.\n\nKnown and declared rather than papered over: step 7 says \"for the pilot\" while\nphase 1 enables the checks repo-wide to produce the census; placement=\"shared\"\nfiles are migrated by neither workflow; neither phase runs the target''s real user\nworkflow; the Product Profile is partially recorded; there is deliberately no\n30-migration-wave until the pilot''s human gate has been answered.\n\nNever executed against a live repository - all verification is static, mutation\nand stub-run based.\n\nnpm run validate green.","tree":{"sha":"623d8da530704e8bffd3cc336f03be4c2e781288","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/trees/623d8da530704e8bffd3cc336f03be4c2e781288"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/commits/8eaac2decb8abfa7d50f6dc02b1fd0b92f836426","verification":{"payload":"tree 623d8da530704e8bffd3cc336f03be4c2e781288\nparent e91dd4eab7fa19aa6b2b95f8505e78587cbe67c0\nauthor Vladislav Manakov <s28.morgan@gmail.com> 1785778198 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785778198 +0500\n\nAdd capability-first migration workflows (#19)\n\nMaintainer tooling under .claude/workflows/: two multi-agent workflows that adopt\nthe capability-first architecture in an existing Next.js repository, plus a repo\ncheck that keeps them honest. They execute the procedure already written in\ndocs/adoption-and-enforcement.md rather than inventing a second one; where the two\ndisagree, the document wins and the script is the defect. Not part of the\npublished plugin.\n\n10-migration-baseline inventories the target through six blind lenses, assigns\nevery source file one owner, role and runtime class, installs rules/ with a\ndrafted contract, and records the behavioural baseline plus a per-messageId\nviolation census. 20-migration-pilot migrates one capability against three\noracles - the target''s own typecheck/lint/tests/production build, rules/ as a\nburndown against that census, and an adversarial review of the properties static\nrules cannot prove - then stops at the human accept/revise/reject gate.\n\nDestinations are arithmetic, not judgement: agents decide a file''s role and the\nscript computes the path, screened for three properties before the first write -\nadmitted (nothing outside the contract vocabulary), closed (nothing resolves\noutside moduleRoot/<capability>/), injective (no two sources on one destination).\nAn oracle that did not report is never a verdict; reject belongs to the review\noracle alone and dominates the other two.\n\nFour review passes: one single-reviewer, one two-axis (standards + spec), and a\nworkflow-backed pass whose findings were recovered in full from the run journal\nafter its ten-finding cap dropped 28 of 38 survivors. Everything found is fixed.\nThe recurring defect across all four was assertions that cannot fail - a source\ntext grep standing in for a behavioural check - which is why the validator now\nhas two layers: extracted regions executed against tables to prove the logic is\ncorrect, and each body run against stubbed hooks to prove it is called.\n\nKnown and declared rather than papered over: step 7 says \"for the pilot\" while\nphase 1 enables the checks repo-wide to produce the census; placement=\"shared\"\nfiles are migrated by neither workflow; neither phase runs the target''s real user\nworkflow; the Product Profile is partially recorded; there is deliberately no\n30-migration-wave until the pilot''s human gate has been answered.\n\nNever executed against a live repository - all verification is static, mutation\nand stub-run based.\n\nnpm run validate green.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcNAWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtHsQAAJoQpwPUUgKvhTD2yFCb5Q4\nbQwf2ERQOiNyprwaqSJHT3k8+Q3geL2+E7fbBM2ltsr6N/9VmEb1boKi00JbeRJv\nTFu7xTxvLe8l3S3te2VFMzkt1oOZuGB4//+OlbW7bfDF/4NPrON7f2uLmG0u+4ii\nQAl9kyQPW+aV/b1k5/xoHD/iHGTH7BMDAkSEr/j7JMn0Hbrqw2d74PbxopCbH2jq\nQ18kbeshlZg/RM58s1gji/yn5DmyqCrhsw3rf0WtIzgIh8I57U7MPao/fvBd+4Qy\nUBE6ReTSJFWkDXn0nlxMw7XiJQ2GdRU6AdJRlda/woU4dpDWTPKlYD2vcwsotmLZ\nqMv9mQX7f5HVisO9nF4uiAXQhLxuroRfXhwWz03tlCaRSWGVCFxGSGot3pFYAjeS\nH95OHtNch5gpJ6svCf9VsMtqdihStZ2Y8/npb/s7SDXgmzPKvm7ytb51w0FbMHgU\ntCuYRPiFivDrAoZYM1M8y66XnMiy8zCYir+udaqpavf1LJEDU7FWoMfQvVEZUsai\nhcUK0yLv5qQ3KO51xlYACXcVstCUH/VjYB7p+AtR0E27GTW5RhUZi+9r6G+xTPm3\n1aPPHmyp59Pzq1h622GC4FhNhTpagWCg++iokNZj99rtkfIPeqGg6VPjccP8gqR5\nfKj5+6YDXA7fuxSwy8Zw\n=HMe/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-03T17:30:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https:/