wner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/e91dd4eab7fa19aa6b2b95f8505e78587cbe67c0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T20:22:04Z","email":"s28.morgan@gmail.com","name":"Vladislav Manakov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T20:22:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix architecture contract and documentation (#18)\n\nDerives source, module, app, shared, alias, ESLint-glob, cycle and database\nownership paths from one executable contract instead of eight independently\nhard-coded copies of src/** and @/. Scopes the Supabase resource canary to\nconfigured client identifiers so unrelated .from()/.rpc() receivers no longer\nproduce ownership failures. Prepares the breaking skill rename as plugin\nversion 3.0.0 and synchronizes capability-first marketplace metadata.\n\nAlso corrects accumulated documentation drift: decision and stream diagrams,\nHTTP versus Server Action examples, deletion-test wording, cache ownership,\nerror carriers, version history and evidence terminology; SKILL.md is\nrestructured from 1,840 to 1,158 words with its normative content pinned by\nscenarios and invariants.\n\nReview found one silent bypass in the newly configurable surface: alias\nprefixes were never validated, so a separatorless \"@\" made cross-capability\nimports and capability cycles resolve to nothing and both tools report clean.\nPrefixes must now end with a separator, refused at contract load, covered by a\nmutation next to the overlapping-roots one.\n\nnpm run validate green: 24 scenarios, 3 clean contract checks / 6 failing\nmutations, 13 invariant codes / 22 failing mutations, 22 clean fixtures /\n25 boundary mutations / 7 resolver, cycle and portability canaries.","tree":{"sha":"559ca1b12c6f2b5f0ba3a2188335d74fcd538937","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/trees/559ca1b12c6f2b5f0ba3a2188335d74fcd538937"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/commits/e91dd4eab7fa19aa6b2b95f8505e78587cbe67c0","verification":{"payload":"tree 559ca1b12c6f2b5f0ba3a2188335d74fcd538937\nparent 79d6bc5291bbb06ef23553d76803ae2ba2f69b9f\nauthor Vladislav Manakov <s28.morgan@gmail.com> 1785702124 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785702124 +0500\n\nFix architecture contract and documentation (#18)\n\nDerives source, module, app, shared, alias, ESLint-glob, cycle and database\nownership paths from one executable contract instead of eight independently\nhard-coded copies of src/** and @/. Scopes the Supabase resource canary to\nconfigured client identifiers so unrelated .from()/.rpc() receivers no longer\nproduce ownership failures. Prepares the breaking skill rename as plugin\nversion 3.0.0 and synchronizes capability-first marketplace metadata.\n\nAlso corrects accumulated documentation drift: decision and stream diagrams,\nHTTP versus Server Action examples, deletion-test wording, cache ownership,\nerror carriers, version history and evidence terminology; SKILL.md is\nrestructured from 1,840 to 1,158 words with its normative content pinned by\nscenarios and invariants.\n\nReview found one silent bypass in the newly configurable surface: alias\nprefixes were never validated, so a separatorless \"@\" made cross-capability\nimports and capability cycles resolve to nothing and both tools report clean.\nPrefixes must now end with a separator, refused at contract load, covered by a\nmutation next to the overlapping-roots one.\n\nnpm run validate green: 24 scenarios, 3 clean contract checks / 6 failing\nmutations, 13 invariant codes / 22 failing mutations, 22 clean fixtures /\n25 boundary mutations / 7 resolver, cycle and portability canaries.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCA