://github.com/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commit/79d6bc5291bbb06ef23553d76803ae2ba2f69b9f","sha":"79d6bc5291bbb06ef23553d76803ae2ba2f69b9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/79d6bc5291bbb06ef23553d76803ae2ba2f69b9f"}],"sha":"e91dd4eab7fa19aa6b2b95f8505e78587cbe67c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/e91dd4eab7fa19aa6b2b95f8505e78587cbe67c0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15245608?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/clicktronix","id":15245608,"login":"clicktronix","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjQ1NjA4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clicktronix","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/commits/79d6bc5291bbb06ef23553d76803ae2ba2f69b9f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-30T12:35:02Z","email":"s28.morgan@gmail.com","name":"Vladislav Manakov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-30T12:35:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: unblock frontmatter upgrades and finish the PR #16 rename (#17)\n\n* fix: unblock frontmatter upgrades and finish the PR #16 rename\n\nThe frontmatter schema allowed only name and description with\nadditionalProperties: false, so adopting any documented Claude Code field —\nwhen_to_use, paths, allowed-tools, effort — failed npm run validate. A guard\nagainst typos had become a ban on upgrades. The schema now lists the documented\nfields and keeps additionalProperties: false for its actual purpose.\n\nThe name enum is replaced by the Agent Skills charset and length rule.\nvalidate-skill-frontmatter.mjs already asserts name equals the directory name,\nso the enum only added a required schema edit per rename, and that edit is how\nthe rename in PR #16 shipped with its titles left behind.\n\nThose titles are fixed here: both H1s and both display_name values still named\nthe old skills, so the Codex UI disagreed with the invocation name. A new check\nasserts each title slugs back to the skill name, which ties titles to renames.\nNone of the previous 15 checks compared either against the skill.\n\nMutation-verified: old H1 and old display_name each fail; when_to_use, paths,\neffort, allowed-tools and a loose boolean all pass; a typo''d field still fails.\n\n* fix: accept the values and spec fields the frontmatter schema documented\n\nReview of the first pass found the same defect class it was fixing: the schema\nrejecting something documented, with CI green.\n\nlooseBoolean had a string-only branch, so `disable-model-invocation: 1` failed\nwith \"must be string\" — YAML parses an unquoted 1 as a number, and 1/0 are the\nvery values the field''s own description promised. Adds the integer branch.\n\nThe Agent Skills spec also defines `license` and `compatibility` (max 500), both\nof which hit additionalProperties, and caps `description` at 1024, which the\nschema only bounded from below. Adds all three, plus a guard on the reserved\nwords Anthropic''s Skills API rejects in a name.\n\nSeparately, the 1,536-character listing cap was measured over name + description\nonly. Now that when_to_use is permitted, the first skill to adopt it would have\nexceeded the cap without the check noticing; it now measures what Claude Code\ntruncates.\n\nThe schema had no negative fixtures, so nothing stopped a future simplification\nfrom reopening any of this. validate-json-schemas.mjs gains reject fixtures and\nreports the count, matching how every other validator here is pinned.\n\n* fix: drop the reserved-word guard on skill names\n\nAdded last commit on the reasoning that it was free. Review pushed back, and\nchecking the sources shows the justification was wrong: the rule appears in\nAnthropic''s authoring guidance with no statement of where it is enforced, the\nopen Agent Skills spec does not have it at all, and Claude Code loads\nclaude-md-writer from a marketplace today. \"Skills API rejects it\" was an\nunverified claim repeated through three reports, including mine.\n\nThe guard also could not fire in this repo while being guaranteed to misfire in\ncc-tuner, whose skill is named claude-md-writer, the moment this validator is\ncopied there — forcing a rename of a published skill to satisfy a constraint its\ndistribution channel may not apply. Unanchored, it also rejected any name merely\ncontaining the substring, such as claudette-.\n\nA guard that cannot fire locally, misfires downstream, and rests on an\nunverified enforcement point is the trade that made additionalProperties a ban\non upgrades. If these skills ever ship through the Skills API, the check belongs\nat that publish step, against the rule as actually enforced there.\n\n* docs: correct the rejected-mutation count in the changelog","tree":{"sha":"2a81d44726d4152493609580ebc152fb2c0cd73f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/trees/2a81d44726d4152493609580ebc152fb2c0cd73f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clicktronix/nextjs-clean-skills/git/commits/79d6bc5291bbb06ef23553d76803ae2ba2f69b9f","verification":{"payload":"tree 2a81d44726d4152493609580ebc152fb2c0cd73f\nparent fd8cb8fabeff99c1148bccf50cb97215a8b92047\nauthor Vladislav Manakov <s28.morgan@gmail.com> 1785414902 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785414902 +0500\n\nfix: unblock frontmatter upgrades and finish the PR #16 rename (#17)\n\n* fix: unblock frontmatter upgrades and finish the PR #16 rename\n\nThe frontmatter schema allowed only name and description with\nadditionalProperties: false, so adopting any documented Claude Code field —\nwhen_to_use, paths, allowed-tools, effort — failed npm run validate. A guard\nagainst typos had become a ban on upgrades. The schema now lists the documented\nfields and keeps additionalProperties: false for its actual purpose.\n\nThe name enum is replaced by the Agent Skills charset and length rule.\nvalidate-skill-frontmatter.mjs already asserts name equals the directory name,\nso the enum only added a required schema edit per rename, and that edit is how\nthe rename in PR #16 shipped with its titles left behind.\n\nThose titles are fixed here: both H1s and both display_name values still named\nthe old skills, so the Codex UI disagreed with the invocation name. A new check\nasserts each title slugs back to the skill name, which ties titles to renames.\nNone of the previous 15 checks compared either against the skill.\n\nMutation-verified: old H1 and old display_name each fail; when_to_use, paths,\neffort, allowed-tools and a loose boolean all pass; a typo''d field still fails.\n\n* fix: accept the values and spec fields the frontmatter schema documented\n\nReview of the first pass found the same defect class it was fixing: the schema\nrejecting something documented, with CI green.\n\nlooseBoolean had a string-only branch, so `disable-model-invocation: 1` failed\nwith \"must be string\" — YAML parses an unquoted 1 as a number, and 1/0 are the\nvery values the field''s own description promised. Adds the integer branch.\n\nThe Agent Skills spec also defines `license` and `compatibility` (max 500), both\nof which hit additionalProperties, and caps `description` at 1024, which the\nschema only bounded from below. Adds all three, plus a guard on the reserved\nwords Anthropic''s Skills API rejects in a name.\n\nSeparately, the 1,536-character listing cap was measured over name + description\nonly. Now that when_to_use is permitted, the first skill to adopt it would have\nexceeded the cap without the check noticing; it now measures what Claude Code\ntruncates.\n\nThe schema had no negative fixtures, so nothing stopped a future simplification\nfrom reopening any of this. validate-json-schemas.mjs gains reject fixtures and\nreports the count, matching how every other validator here is pinned.\n\n* fix: drop the reserved-word guard on skill names\n\nAdded last commit on the reasoning that it was free. Review pushed back, and\nchecking the sources shows the justification was wrong: the rule appears in\nAnthropic''s authoring guidance with no statement of where it is enforced, the\nopen Agent Skills spec does not have it at all, and Claude Code loads\nclaude-md-writer from a marketplace today. \"Skills API rejects it\" was an\nunverified claim repeated through three reports, including mine.\n\nThe guard also could not fire in this repo while being guaranteed to misfire in\ncc-tuner, whose skill is named claude-md-writer, the moment this validator is\ncopied there — forcing a rename of a published skill to satisfy a constraint its\ndistribution channel may not apply. Unanchored, it also rejected any name merely\ncontaining the substring, such as claudette-.\n\nA guard that cannot fire locally, misfires downstream, and rests on an\nunverified enforcement point is the trade that made additionalProperties a ban\non upgrades. If these skills ever ship through the Skills API, the check belongs\nat that publish step, against the rule as actually enforced there.\n\n* docs: correct the rejected-mutation count in the changelog","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa0T2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvhsQAGVfLApVgcn0iVmK/zFQPhq4\n2FAERVAD6c9WIVnyVujvwVdgUcRWF0sqrP5fIAwf1sDMAYI