ed{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TalGershanov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TalGershanov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TalGershanov/ClearMed/commits/7fd25c610787f1640a0c2dac27ebbfccbd93efeb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T10:14:43Z","email":"talgershanov@gmail.com","name":"Tal Gershanov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T10:14:43Z","email":"talgershanov@gmail.com","name":"Tal Gershanov"},"message":"Split create_clearmed_db.py into ai_services/translation_service/db_operations/build_db, add per-language config, and fix duplicate terms in the analyse endpoint\n\nReplaces the Hebrew-only hardcoded seeding script with a data-driven\nSUPPORTED_LANGUAGES loop so a new language is a config+data change, not a\ncode change. Translation now happens inline against the live DB short\nexplanation instead of a stale JSON snapshot, and a failed translation no\nlonger clobbers a previously-good one on re-run. Also dedupes /analyse''s\ndetected_terms by concept so a repeated term (e.g. \"fever\" x3) shows once\nin the Select Terms screen instead of once per occurrence.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f16208028f767e821320ef9912f10ed30794fd91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TalGershanov/ClearMed/git/trees/f16208028f767e821320ef9912f10ed30794fd91"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TalGershanov/ClearMed/git/commits/7fd25c610787f1640a0c2dac27ebbfccbd93efeb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/206593359?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TalGershanov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TalGershanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TalGershanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TalGershanov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TalGershanov","id":206593359,"login":"TalGershanov","node_id":"U_kgDODFBdTw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TalGershanov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TalGershanov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TalGershanov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TalGershanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TalGershanov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TalGershanov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TalGershanov/ClearMed/commit/7fd25c610787f1640a0c2dac27ebbfccbd93efeb","node_id":"C_kwDOSDc3rtoAKDdmZDI1YzYxMDc4N2YxNjQwYTBjMmRhYzI3ZWJiZmNjYmQ5M2VmZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TalGershanov/ClearMed/commit/6019e43fd4698bc042f6f226a94480b830060fe7","sha":"6019e43fd4698bc042f6f226a94480b830060fe7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TalGershanov/ClearMed/commits/6019e43fd4698bc042f6f226a94480b830060fe7"}],"sha":"7fd25c610787f1640a0c2dac27ebbfccbd93efeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TalGershanov/ClearMed/commits/7fd25c610787f1640a0c2dac27ebbfccbd93efeb"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TalGershanov/ClearMed/commits/fa1b2d0e38dc99f5b2a3449f75f32cd25131f95f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T09:02:46Z","email":"yuvalbashan7@gmail.com","name":"yuvalbashan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T09:02:46Z","email":"yuvalbashan7@gmail.com","name":"yuvalbashan"},"message":"Add OCR fallback for scanned PDFs, JPG, and PNG uploads\n\nRegisters an ImageOCRExtractor for image/jpeg and image/png, and wraps\nPDFTextExtractor with a fallback that OCRs a scanned PDF''s rendered pages\nwhen pypdf finds no meaningful text -- reusing the exact Gemini OCR call\nlogic/ocr.py already exposes via POST /ocr, never a separate\nimplementation. Every extractor still returns the same (text | None)\nshape, so webapp/documents/service.py, the 4-state extraction_status\nenum, and the whole downstream analyse/simplify pipeline needed no\nchanges at all -- no migration, no new endpoints.\n\nA shared is_meaningful_text() helper (webapp/extraction/quality.py)\nreplaces the old ad hoc length check so a whitespace/control-character-only\nresult is never reported as a successful extraction, whether it came from\npypdf or OCR. Extraction now runs via asyncio.to_thread inside\nsave_uploaded_document, since the OCR path is a real blocking network\ncall and must not stall the event loop.\n\nVerified live end-to-end with a real Gemini key: a genuinely text-less\nscanned PDF, a JPG, and a PNG all OCR correctly and flow through the\nexisting analyse -> Terms Found -> simplify pipeline unchanged; a blank\nimage correctly resolves to no_text_found rather than a false success.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AVuUmeGHmcBV1idTReqbgH","tree":{"sha":"09f54f226e122a0ffbbea00818ecb930bf0be660","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TalGershanov/ClearMed/git/trees/09f54f226e122a0ffbbea00818ecb930bf0be660"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TalGershanov/ClearMed/git/commits/fa1b2d0e38dc99f5b2a3449f75f32cd25131f95f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/TalGershanov/ClearMed/commit/fa1b2d0e38dc99f5b2a3449f75f32cd25131f95f","node_id":"C_kwDOSDc3rtoAKGZhMWIyZDBlMzhkYzk5ZjViMmEzNDQ5Zjc1ZjMyY2QyNTEzMWY5NWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TalGershanov/ClearMed/commit/e14ed52bb48c7a6a6464113e9228a06a333c5686","sha":"e14ed52bb48c7a6a6464113e9228a06a333c5686","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TalGershanov/ClearMed/commits/e14ed52bb48c7a6a6464113e9228a06a333c5686"}],"sha":"fa1b2d0e38dc99f5b2a3449f75f32cd25131f95f","url":"https://api.github.com/