user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TalGershanov/ClearMed/commits/ddf283598400ae5b40db2f48b65ab740063484d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T16:24:29Z","email":"talgershanov@gmail.com","name":"Tal Gershanov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T16:24:29Z","email":"talgershanov@gmail.com","name":"Tal Gershanov"},"message":"Fix OpenMRS dashboard registration, add note-picker pop-out screen\n\nThe widget''s nav button was unstyled/unclickable (\"Could not find a valid\ndashboard definition\") because routes.json registered it as a bare\nextension instead of via a proper createDashboard link + content pair.\nFixes that, and adds the requested pop-out screen: a dashboard tab where\na clinician picks one of the patient''s OpenMRS clinical notes (new\nGET /openmrs/patients/{uuid}/notes, backed by a configurable\nOPENMRS_NOTE_CONCEPT_UUID) and runs it through ClearMed''s existing\nanalyse/translate flow, skipping the file-upload step entirely.\n\nAlso mirrors /analyse and /translate onto the CORS-scoped /openmrs sub-app\nso the widget can call them cross-origin (they previously had no CORS\nheaders at all), fixes a pydantic crash when an observation''s value is\nnumeric rather than a string, and points the widget''s default\nclearmedApiBaseUrl at the real deployed backend instead of a placeholder.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"40e8e93c77de8a40520c86cb046862d5a529b240","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TalGershanov/ClearMed/git/trees/40e8e93c77de8a40520c86cb046862d5a529b240"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TalGershanov/ClearMed/git/commits/ddf283598400ae5b40db2f48b65ab740063484d3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/206593359?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TalGershanov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https: