},"email":"leandrorojas@gmail.com","name":"leandrorojas"},"authoredDate":"2026-04-26T17:53:17Z","committedDate":"2026-04-26T17:53:17Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:39:40.480Z","repositoryId":1211592100,"sha":"44818d6b25fa2b5d498b3de3460f3755dff71a52"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"leandrorojas","providerType":"User"},"email":"leandrorojas@gmail.com","name":"leandrorojas"},"authoredDate":"2026-04-18T14:42:56Z","committedDate":"2026-04-18T14:42:56Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:39:40.480Z","repositoryId":1211592100,"sha":"de3b186ebbb870f8a4272db4e255769ff5feda01"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"leandrorojas","providerType":"User"},"email":"leandrorojas@gmail.com","name":"Leandro Rojas"},"authoredDate":"2026-04-15T22:26:01Z","committedDate":"2026-04-15T22:26:01Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"leandrorojas","providerType":"User"},"email":"leandrorojas@gmail.com","name":"Leandro Rojas"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:39:40.480Z","repositoryId":1211592100,"sha":"db642e8aba6c7a94ba798226e9c43ae36e43f407"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:39:40.480Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","id":49699333,"login":"dependabot[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/c2e58ca1e750c21e2712d40ab55e76b586d3bfb9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T19:09:52Z","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T19:09:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(deps): Bump commander from 12.1.0 to 14.0.3 (#15)\n\n* chore(deps): Bump commander from 12.1.0 to 14.0.3\n\nBumps [commander](https://github.com/tj/commander.js) from 12.1.0 to 14.0.3.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/tj/commander.js/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/tj/commander.js/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/tj/commander.js/compare/v12.1.0...v14.0.3)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: commander\n  dependency-version: 14.0.3\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\n\n* test(cli): add Commander v13+ behavior regression suite\n\nCommander 13 changed `allowExcessArguments` from `true` to `false` by\ndefault — `bulma create my-site oops` now errors with \"too many\narguments\" instead of silently ignoring `oops`. Better UX (catches\ntypos), but it''s a behavior change worth pinning so a future\ndependency bump or our own option rework doesn''t accidentally\nre-enable the silent-ignore.\n\nRefactor: extract `buildProgram()` from `main()` so tests can\nconstruct the same program shape and exercise it with `exitOverride()`\n+ silenced stdio without main()''s side effects (process.exitCode,\nprocess.exit on errors, stderr noise in test output).\n\nTests added (`src/cli.test.ts`):\n- Excess positional args on `create` → `commander.excessArguments`\n- Unknown `--bogus-flag` on `create` → `commander.unknownOption`\n- Missing required `<site-name>` → `commander.missingArgument`\n\nEach Commander subcommand has its own exit/output callbacks, so\n`exitOverride()` on the parent doesn''t propagate. The test helper\nwalks the command tree and applies per-command.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(sonar): exclude cli.ts entry point from coverage gate\n\nAdding the cli.ts regression tests in the previous commit pulled the\nfile into Sonar''s \"new code coverage\" measurement, which dropped to\n0% because main() and the `require.main === module` bootstrap can''t\nbe exercised in unit tests (they call process.exit and are guarded\non import).\n\nThe testable surface — buildProgram() — IS now covered by\nsrc/cli.test.ts. Mark cli.ts as a coverage-exclusion in both jest''s\ncollectCoverageFrom and Sonar''s coverage.exclusions, with a comment\nexplaining why. Same pattern other entry-point files use.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Leandro Rojas <leandrorojas@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"364486f5867795a8c3783c7adfa886bdad950189","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/git/trees/364486f5867795a8c3783c7adfa886bdad950189"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/git/commits/c2e58ca1e750c21e2712d40ab55e76b586d3bfb9","verification":{"payload":"tree 364486f5867795a8c3783c7adfa886bdad950189\nparent d2a3820b1a88a0232bd1daa81e15e1f5c4b11192\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1777403392 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777403392 -0300\n\nchore(deps): Bump commander from 12.1.0 to 14.0.3 (#15)\n\n* chore(deps): Bump commander from 12.1.0 to 14.0.3\n\nBumps [commander](https://github.com/tj/commander.js) from 12.1.0 to 14.0.3.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/tj/commander.js/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/tj/commander.js/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/tj/commander.js/compare/v12.1.0...v14.0.3)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: commander\n  dependency-version: 14.0.3\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\n\n* test(cli): add Commander v13+ behavior regression suite\n\nCommander 13 changed `allowExcessArguments` from `true` to `false` by\ndefault — `bulma create my-site oops` now errors with \"too many\narguments\" instead of silently ignoring `oops`. Better UX (catches\ntypos), but it''s a behavior change worth pinning so a future\ndependency bump or our own option rework doesn''t accidentally\nre-enable the silent-ignore.\n\nRefactor: extract `buildProgram()` from `main()` so tests can\nconstruct the same program shape and exercise it with `exitOverride()`\n+ silenced stdio without main()''s side effects (process.exitCode,\nprocess.exit on errors, stderr noise in test output).\n\nTests added (`src/cli.test.ts`):\n- Excess positional args on `create` → `commander.excessArguments`\n- Unknown `--bogus-flag` on `create` → `commander.unknownOption`\n- Missing required `<site-name>` → `commander.missingArgument`\n\nEach Commander subcommand has its own exit/output callbacks, so\n`exitOverride()` on the parent doesn''t propagate. The test helper\nwalks the command tree and applies per-command.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(sonar): exclude cli.ts entry point from coverage gate\n\nAdding the cli.ts regression tests in the previous commit pulled the\nfile into Sonar''s \"new code coverage\" measurement, which dropped to\n0% because main() and the `require.main === module` bootstrap can''t\nbe exercised in unit tests (they call process.exit and are guarded\non import).\n\nThe testable surface — buildProgram() — IS now covered by\nsrc/cli.test.ts. Mark cli.ts as a coverage-exclusion in both jest''s\ncollectCoverageFrom and Sonar''s coverage.exclusions, with a comment\nexplaining why. Same pattern other entry-point files use.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Leandro Rojas <leandrorojas@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp8QYACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhBEQAE16T8XZFSrmLiOL9+9eqXXJ\niMf+yAazT4tsiluOnShAX3WXWSln97TvdgE3ottZoxkJXQZ1EvGId4Ga2oasKvtY\nSQHbEvYRfZKPo9StFjkY+dzZkMMB3L8KCqgyvSoIjffkKfsDVVLKlQIVAV/JuYAQ\n3BgVgIPl5XWbw18GL9WwZK8fMjctx3oZuQlEq3Rnc2gSJUHECIr2CIokuYrXs2dI\n9Qc3T3TRJqmXiVQnESP8T5VXx40PzAqtkHuxskg58g8CCQlS6hiJAONTbsilD2BE\nSQrB5jYHe4KT34XYYVPX1olLcMUdR27zvF8AnmBXUPJfvNARaeW6X5R5mHF76KdK\nfk8PnX5gZ4gXRRf21jpTRs/N4HYHs0PfkIUcTzrqxeD4ewXT2nj+nHydEyD2f+nb\nmKNQo9pg+TNU9Twqo7b6HiFFuDaOnODWMb0f4p7Z7qiiirXpsGG16qg64sOz2HOV\nML5s4kK1gsvuJVmenpzpedP181Kcwjc7kMPrKRmfAjAQkYgxQhqyDcFTrhxNzzeO\nZJDhmJHMH33mjIaidsgwRleZZlA3KAHQ0OYJAiNu1w04Ic0nRZh63OdHhcpgF+Tx\nd/4hRTlmWmc3E55UsLH9WNb0qF7Rnk5a8M8hPI/bqjP83HcY4QpAEyX8I9vE2SWq\n4ztBRfJsduGbwwQiR17B\n=KPeY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-28T19:09:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.git