ps://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/leandrorojas/bulma/commit/2511de48beb7574801255461c354d40185bcf3b5","node_id":"C_kwDOSDdtpNoAKDI1MTFkZTQ4YmViNzU3NDgwMTI1NTQ2MWMzNTRkNDAxODViY2YzYjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/leandrorojas/bulma/commit/6a69da4075ab9ee27a50d6b53032b55f5df90d61","sha":"6a69da4075ab9ee27a50d6b53032b55f5df90d61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/6a69da4075ab9ee27a50d6b53032b55f5df90d61"}],"sha":"2511de48beb7574801255461c354d40185bcf3b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/2511de48beb7574801255461c354d40185bcf3b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2161005?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leandrorojas","id":2161005,"login":"leandrorojas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjEwMDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/6a69da4075ab9ee27a50d6b53032b55f5df90d61/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T12:23:13Z","email":"leandrorojas@gmail.com","name":"leandrorojas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T12:23:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(devex): code quality + developer experience foundation (#10)\n\n* feat(devex): code quality + developer experience foundation\n\nGreenfield-to-baseline DevEx setup. None of these existed before this PR.\n\nPre-merge guardrails:\n- husky + lint-staged pre-commit hook runs eslint --fix and\n  prettier --write on staged files, so style issues get auto-fixed\n  before they hit CI\n- prettier with project-wide config (printWidth 100, double quotes,\n  es5 trailing commas, lf line endings)\n- .editorconfig for cross-editor consistency\n\nHygiene:\n- CONTRIBUTING.md extracted from README''s contributing section,\n  expanded with the local-checks recipe, the senzu PR-workflow link,\n  coding standards, commit conventions, review etiquette, and the\n  release flow\n- .github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md drives the Summary + Test plan\n  format we''ve been using consistently across PRs\n- .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/{bug_report,feature_request,config}\n  structured intake; blank issues disabled with a contact link to\n  the senzu workflow doc for PR-process questions\n\nAutomation:\n- .github/dependabot.yml — weekly npm + GitHub Actions updates,\n  minor+patch grouped to keep review noise down (majors still\n  individual PRs)\n- .coderabbit.yaml — pin the assertive review profile we''ve been\n  using and tune path filters (skip dist/, coverage/, lock files,\n  senzu/)\n\nNew npm scripts: format, format:check, prepare (husky install).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address 6 CodeRabbit findings on the DevEx PR\n\nMinor:\n- bug_report.md: add `text` language to the empty fenced block so\n  markdownlint MD040 is happy and the rendered intent is explicit.\n- ISSUE_TEMPLATE/config.yml: the \"PR workflow questions\" contact\n  link pointed at the private senzu repo, which 404s for any\n  external user clicking it from the issue chooser. Repoint to\n  CONTRIBUTING.md#pr-workflow which is public.\n- CONTRIBUTING.md: drop the \"158+\" test count (drifts every PR);\n  describe the suite without a number.\n- CONTRIBUTING.md: clarify that the senzu/workflows/pr-workflow.md\n  link only resolves with --recurse-submodules and that the senzu\n  repo is private.\n\nTrivial:\n- PR template: add `npm run format:check` to the test-plan\n  checklist so it matches the local checks contributors actually\n  run (and what the pre-commit hook enforces).\n- .lintstagedrc.json: scope the root-only Prettier glob to\n  `./*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}` instead of `*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}` so files\n  under src/ aren''t formatted twice (lint-staged v15 uses\n  matchBase semantics for slashless globs).\n\nSkipping the optional Issue Forms (.yml) migration — explicitly\nmarked \"not blocking\" by CR; current markdown templates are\nfunctional and migration is a meaningful rewrite better tracked as\na follow-up.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ed976ecbc86f97430959d2df6317034ff93881c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/git/trees/ed976ecbc86f97430959d2df6317034ff93881c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/git/commits/6a69da4075ab9ee27a50d6b53032b55f5df90d61","verification":{"payload":"tree ed976ecbc86f97430959d2df6317034ff93881c9\nparent 44a181951cedd0e63c691d00755085799383408d\nauthor leandrorojas <leandrorojas@gmail.com> 1777292593 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777292593 -0300\n\nfeat(devex): code quality + developer experience foundation (#10)\n\n* feat(devex): code quality + developer experience foundation\n\nGreenfield-to-baseline DevEx setup. None of these existed before this PR.\n\nPre-merge guardrails:\n- husky + lint-staged pre-commit hook runs eslint --fix and\n  prettier --write on staged files, so style issues get auto-fixed\n  before they hit CI\n- prettier with project-wide config (printWidth 100, double quotes,\n  es5 trailing commas, lf line endings)\n- .editorconfig for cross-editor consistency\n\nHygiene:\n- CONTRIBUTING.md extracted from README''s contributing section,\n  expanded with the local-checks recipe, the senzu PR-workflow link,\n  coding standards, commit conventions, review etiquette, and the\n  release flow\n- .github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md drives the Summary + Test plan\n  format we''ve been using consistently across PRs\n- .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/{bug_report,feature_request,config}\n  structured intake; blank issues disabled with a contact link to\n  the senzu workflow doc for PR-process questions\n\nAutomation:\n- .github/dependabot.yml — weekly npm + GitHub Actions updates,\n  minor+patch grouped to keep review noise down (majors still\n  individual PRs)\n- .coderabbit.yaml — pin the assertive review profile we''ve been\n  using and tune path filters (skip dist/, coverage/, lock files,\n  senzu/)\n\nNew npm scripts: format, format:check, prepare (husky install).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address 6 CodeRabbit findings on the DevEx PR\n\nMinor:\n- bug_report.md: add `text` language to the empty fenced block so\n  markdownlint MD040 is happy and the rendered intent is explicit.\n- ISSUE_TEMPLATE/config.yml: the \"PR workflow questions\" contact\n  link pointed at the private senzu repo, which 404s for any\n  external user clicking it from the issue chooser. Repoint to\n  CONTRIBUTING.md#pr-workflow which is public.\n- CONTRIBUTING.md: drop the \"158+\" test count (drifts every PR);\n  describe the suite without a number.\n- CONTRIBUTING.md: clarify that the senzu/workflows/pr-workflow.md\n  link only resolves with --recurse-submodules and that the senzu\n  repo is private.\n\nTrivial:\n- PR template: add `npm run format:check` to the test-plan\n  checklist so it matches the local checks contributors actually\n  run (and what the pre-commit hook enforces).\n- .lintstagedrc.json: scope the root-only Prettier glob to\n  `./*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}` instead of `*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}` so files\n  under src/ aren''t formatted twice (lint-staged v15 uses\n  matchBase semantics for slashless globs).\n\nSkipping the optional Issue Forms (.yml) migration — explicitly\nmarked \"not blocking\" by CR; current markdown templates are\nfunctional and migration is a meaningful rewrite better tracked as\na follow-up.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp71UxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqfwQAAUe8lgUtex/dErGhYd1MpxJ\nqeJEgJNDCQHsqZqtspye+m0w4Kq00W6Bu7ducK6XSv14jaPVvFjCAyffsw6gKZlx\nlWcNTXrKRn2sLlcQSR5+RZmnWOpfWXAIZzXhuIbku0lJ5fND7daalW3+9gN8LaZ1\nFbtufvGXTBUHCPO9MC4p9lHMVmRcyt9UX8ObTQhihG7/UswveagsZh8E/CaSr6Ur\nUtI5E0nS/P74sk5XPwRcHDXwwqIl9ktdfhQkWqjQ3bY5qy5Rd1+7ka33JTLcaL3Q\npaMAs/qclN/+Upf3LvPKVNj6FqvK16E4gWac6MjDAaETkwjfylzpHF2J96CBTacQ\n7ymz9+BC1aIG+kfxCzlOuGFwP5TN1+TOHr4xm/1Jv/2jUSh150DPzPFD0RK3He1S\nqfAUY6lBp5ek7qFhJAC9rSGKTRm5rfiyJAvQ5i+dCoc1hMhJqlpTFMPsrw5F/yHy\nWyp4cIbf/uRfQuX5zZpPzdXKWGkOXYYewtUVyDvuRuXPaMKzoenhC+ZUYzw+jwKa\ngN76Ms3Kp2i/obiZsny5Ihoa2+vbaatE+bFsH9cErNud0JC59aprJx2VscVFHFe3\n7vgEFYU0jfD46Ph49fQ80948FQuIDk0VNgKZiVlNJyEFMkzI7QjCpzrSuY9SF/VO\n6Rv5XLNvrrArVoWWzuq/\n=UNnP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-27T12:23:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/leandrorojas/bulma/commit/6a69da4075ab9ee27a50d6b53032b55f5df90d61","node_id":"C_kwDOSDdtpNoAKDZhNjlkYTQwNzVhYjllZTI3YTUwZDZiNTMwMzJiNTVmNWRmOTBkNjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/leandrorojas/bulma/commit/44a181951cedd0e63c691d00755085799383408d","sha":"44a181951cedd0e63c691d00755085799383408d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/44a181951cedd0e63c691d00755085799383408d"}],"sha":"6a69da4075ab9ee27a50d6b53032b55f5df90d61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/6a69da4075ab9ee27a50d6b53032b55f5df90d61"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2161005?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leandrorojas","id":2161005,"login":"leandrorojas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjEwMDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/44a181951cedd0e63c691d00755085799383408d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T03:25:19Z","email":"leandrorojas@gmail.com","name":"leandrorojas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T03:25:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: rewrite README to cover the full create flow + DevEx (#9)\n\n* docs: rewrite README to cover the full create flow + DevEx\n\nReplaces the foundation-only README (which still warned that the\nimplementation lands \"in subsequent PRs\") with a complete user-facing\ndoc covering the five sections the docs epic calls for:\n\n- Overview — what bulma is and what one command produces\n  end-to-end (private repo + GitHub Actions + Vercel + initial deploy)\n- Install — npm/npx + the GitHub Packages auth requirement\n- Prerequisites — gh scopes, VERCEL_TOKEN, Vercel GitHub App\n  install URL, and the optional env vars (BULMA_SONAR_TOKEN,\n  VERCEL_TEAM_ID)\n- Usage — `bulma create` (every flag with rationale + examples) and\n  `bulma help` (top-level vs. per-command)\n- What gets scaffolded — directory tree of the new local site,\n  GitHub repo state (secret + env), and Vercel project shape\n- Next steps — local dev, publish via push, tagged release through\n  the QA gate, consumer install\n- Development + Contributing — pointers to the integration test\n  suite, manual verification checklist, and the senzu PR workflow\n\nRemoves the \"Status: foundation only\" warning since the create flow\nhas been complete and end-to-end smoke validated for several PRs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: fix Sourcery-flagged grammar nit on previews bullet\n\n\"Per-branch preview deployments on for free\" was missing a verb —\nreads ungrammatical. Rewording to \"enabled by default\" aligns with\nhow Vercel describes the behavior in its own docs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6be198d48cd25b4b1724ab0258abeed2e387eaaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/git/trees/6be198d48cd25b4b1724ab0258abeed2e387eaaf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/git/commits/44a181951cedd0e63c691d00755085799383408d","verification":{"payload":"tree 6be198d48cd25b4b1724ab0258abeed2e387eaaf\nparent 66d45fb60a6206c0e59542f08204c3235032b2d5\nauthor leandrorojas <leandrorojas@gmail.com> 1777260319 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777260319 -0300\n\ndocs: rewrite README to cover the full create flow + DevEx (#9)\n\n* docs: rewrite README to cover the full create flow + DevEx\n\nReplaces the foundation-only README (which still warned that the\nimplementation lands \"in subsequent PRs\") with a complete user-facing\ndoc covering the five sections the docs epic calls for:\n\n- Overview — what bulma is and what one command produces\n  end-to-end (private repo + GitHub Actions + Vercel + initial deploy)\n- Install — npm/npx + the GitHub Packages auth requirement\n- Prerequisites — gh scopes, VERCEL_TOKEN, Vercel GitHub App\n  install URL, and the optional env vars (BULMA_SONAR_TOKEN,\n  VERCEL_TEAM_ID)\n- Usage — `bulma create` (every flag with rationale + examples) and\n  `bulma help` (top-level vs. per-command)\n- What gets scaffolded — directory tree of the new local site,\n  GitHub repo state (secret + env), and Vercel project shape\n- Next steps — local dev, publish via push, tagged release through\n  the QA gate, consumer install\n- Development + Contributing — pointers to the integration test\n  suite, manual verification checklist, and the senzu PR workflow\n\nRemoves the \"Status: foundation only\" warning since the create flow\nhas been complete and end-to-end smoke validated for several PRs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: fix Sourcery-flagged grammar nit on previews bullet\n\n\"Per-branch preview deployments on for free\" was missing a verb —\nreads ungrammatical. Rewording to \"enabled by default\" aligns with\nhow Vercel describes the behavior in its own docs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp7tcfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWFYQAIx5TCyZL39BHoGgKldLr97D\npJC7ThbypBDzFyVVh7aGym5IM7cLjgnQbkOBXavAftBOOk//TIEfv6aio1jDC4+B\nP8+WSaoytoVM9/QMFnw3RIQX2g0vAY52Fay0OCAC/JEFKYXuvEuvk6G/Y+yn3Ng7\nw4RWfu5fAtGvNb73SpjPngfGFj/qHoQCNV4t27zFqPtRojJhrswuKj5Worde8qSz\nPpDjuHMpv6VX/hJPtGTW7EPKrxrEQbLEtZXg/Qt2kPjuFfPAVfob79JFHfjvPF2N\nMgHKkhCLATUftVu+adaTDpy3L96I4ve5iXG0qKigNPgLvcz+eRcMDCexQeK/r6jP\ntGzb5QdHOg5f9HOGne4pWvMgSNC3IpDB5a15Uc/kRo0oDSPIJMmYCEVOxK3YkGq/\nlTj1b+lLB4tAN+jNGFJoHcMT4qeVvvwlk6sGNlSVuVAAm7uSbD8LGVdQ3J9gHOIo\nXouhxmxIwvWLU6cCuoAKrvFZW/oMITe2HucJ/35xt9DfiXSoF6G4HFIn3DRJ0GDq\n++dEI0nl/gy9cH9Q4yw1xbHpubtePgdjYjxOSe7HPyDw4aavSRHXRCw0nGuhnYf8\nvu9+fqZlq+7xv+1FSMqAYXYGuFMZHI7O3vTp2Q+d1RaJUcgWWB/9Q3yOQoTTl1yJ\nQiqtxXwugYYxuN2qIH85\n=QMqt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-27T03:25:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/leandrorojas/bulma/commit/44a181951cedd0e63c691d00755085799383408d","node_id":"C_kwDOSDdtpNoAKDQ0YTE4MTk1MWNlZGQwZTYzYzY5MWQwMDc1NTA4NTc5OTM4MzQwOGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/leandrorojas/bulma/commit/66d45fb60a6206c0e59542f08204c3235032b2d5","sha":"66d45fb60a6206c0e59542f08204c3235032b2d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/66d45fb60a6206c0e59542f08204c3235032b2d5"}],"sha":"44a181951cedd0e63c691d00755085799383408d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/44a181951cedd0e63c691d00755085799383408d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2161005?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leandrorojas","id":2161005,"login":"leandrorojas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjEwMDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/66d45fb60a6206c0e59542f08204c3235032b2d5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T02:17:01Z","email":"leandrorojas@gmail.com","name":"leandrorojas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T02:17:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: add integration suite + manual verification checklist (#8)\n\n* test: add integration suite + manual verification checklist\n\nCloses the testing-coverage story. Existing unit tests already cover\nfolder-structure generation, GitHub API calls, and Vercel API calls\nvia dependency injection. The two missing layers were:\n\n- **Integration tests** (`src/commands/create.integration.test.ts`):\n  exercises the create flow against the REAL filesystem — real\n  mkdtemp, mkdir, copyDir, writeFile, removeDir, pathExists. Mocks\n  only the network/process boundaries (git, GitHub REST, Vercel\n  REST) so it runs hermetically in CI. Catches bugs the pure-DI\n  tests can''t:\n    - parent dir not created before writeFile\n    - file contents round-tripping through fs\n    - cleanup races (tmpDir removed even on failure)\n    - --skip-vercel / --skip-actions interaction with the actual\n      directory tree\n  5 cases: full happy path, tmpdir cleanup, partial-write rollback,\n  --skip-vercel, --skip-actions.\n\n- **Manual verification checklist**\n  (`docs/manual-verification.md`): captures the end-to-end smoke\n  sequence we''ve been running by hand for the create flow against\n  real GitHub + Vercel. Documents prereqs, expected log output,\n  per-location verification, and teardown commands. Includes a\n  \"when to run this\" section so it''s clear which PRs warrant a\n  manual run beyond CI.\n\nCLAUDE.md updated to describe the three testing layers (unit /\nintegration / manual) and point at the new checklist.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: align \"All repositories\" wording with GitHub''s UI label\n\nSourcery noticed that \"All-repos\" with a hyphen is unconventional —\nGitHub''s actual settings UI says \"All repositories\". Updates the\nthree places this string appears (manual-verification checklist,\ntop-level help, and the App-not-installed error message) so the\nphrase users see in our output exactly matches what they need to\nclick in GitHub.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4f45d7511d61be3176cfb62dda38e226d0f7fd5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/git/trees/4f45d7511d61be3176cfb62dda38e226d0f7fd5c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/git/commits/66d45fb60a6206c0e59542f08204c3235032b2d5","verification":{"payload":"tree 4f45d7511d61be3176cfb62dda38e226d0f7fd5c\nparent 448d0e2776de8500814468b0dac78bd07c79619e\nauthor leandrorojas <leandrorojas@gmail.com> 1777256221 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777256221 -0300\n\ntest: add integration suite + manual verification checklist (#8)\n\n* test: add integration suite + manual verification checklist\n\nCloses the testing-coverage story. Existing unit tests already cover\nfolder-structure generation, GitHub API calls, and Vercel API calls\nvia dependency injection. The two missing layers were:\n\n- **Integration tests** (`src/commands/create.integration.test.ts`):\n  exercises the create flow against the REAL filesystem — real\n  mkdtemp, mkdir, copyDir, writeFile, removeDir, pathExists. Mocks\n  only the network/process boundaries (git, GitHub REST, Vercel\n  REST) so it runs hermetically in CI. Catches bugs the pure-DI\n  tests can''t:\n    - parent dir not created before writeFile\n    - file contents round-tripping through fs\n    - cleanup races (tmpDir removed even on failure)\n    - --skip-vercel / --skip-actions interaction with the actual\n      directory tree\n  5 cases: full happy path, tmpdir cleanup, partial-write rollback,\n  --skip-vercel, --skip-actions.\n\n- **Manual verification checklist**\n  (`docs/manual-verification.md`): captures the end-to-end smoke\n  sequence we''ve been running by hand for the create flow against\n  real GitHub + Vercel. Documents prereqs, expected log output,\n  per-location verification, and teardown commands. Includes a\n  \"when to run this\" section so it''s clear which PRs warrant a\n  manual run beyond CI.\n\nCLAUDE.md updated to describe the three testing layers (unit /\nintegration / manual) and point at the new checklist.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: align \"All repositories\" wording with GitHub''s UI label\n\nSourcery noticed that \"All-repos\" with a hyphen is unconventional —\nGitHub''s actual settings UI says \"All repositories\". Updates the\nthree places this string appears (manual-verification checklist,\ntop-level help, and the App-not-installed error message) so the\nphrase users see in our output exactly matches what they need to\nclick in GitHub.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp7scdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAffcQAEc9RMQhASiE4cWBFEHiBar0\n/9a/SNd2Nl6ug1L7Wz/6Fjpg0UCiH4pTvPMVA6EjQqh++2e6PMvHfvgzwH9X38h2\n5yc4cwGmXDg97nf7trXHmh83FxB+lLwBI9B2+LQRJUphgcDdvJ3IDXd9ikBmCFNP\nzAHvjn19buJB1Ci67SmkiYPnJtCGi7JYi5tgGVztGEOT