66d45fb60a6206c0e59542f08204c3235032b2d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/66d45fb60a6206c0e59542f08204c3235032b2d5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2161005?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leandrorojas","id":2161005,"login":"leandrorojas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjEwMDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/448d0e2776de8500814468b0dac78bd07c79619e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T01:54:54Z","email":"leandrorojas@gmail.com","name":"leandrorojas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T01:54:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add prerequisites + usage examples to bulma help (#7)\n\nCommander already auto-generates the commands list, required arguments,\nand option flags via \\`bulma --help\\` and \\`bulma help <command>\\`. This\nextends the auto-generated output with content the user can''t derive\nfrom the command graph alone:\n\n- Top-level help now documents the external prerequisites:\n  - gh CLI scopes required (repo, workflow, delete_repo)\n  - VERCEL_TOKEN env / vercel login\n  - Vercel GitHub App installation URL\n- Optional env vars (BULMA_SONAR_TOKEN, VERCEL_TEAM_ID) listed with\n  what each one enables.\n- create command help now includes runnable examples that explain\n  the tradeoff of each --skip-* flag and how cwd determines the\n  generated site path.\n\nHelp text lives in src/help.ts as plain string constants so it can\nbe unit-tested without invoking Commander (which calls process.exit\non --help).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5f3ef1f6718aa56d22d746bba68d0c6982d22f6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/git/trees/5f3ef1f6718aa56d22d746bba68d0c6982d22f6e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/git/commits/448d0e2776de8500814468b0dac78bd07c79619e","verification":{"payload":"tree 5f3ef1f6718aa56d22d746bba68d0c6982d22f6e\nparent 6446449a0d6e84f8b61de838cd17707c7218e01c\nauthor leandrorojas <leandrorojas@gmail.com> 1777254894 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777254894 -0300\n\nfeat: add prerequisites + usage examples to bulma help (#7)\n\nCommander already auto-generates the commands list, required arguments,\nand option flags via \\`bulma --help\\` and \\`bulma help <command>\\`. This\nextends the auto-generated output with content the user can''t derive\nfrom the command graph alone:\n\n- Top-level help now documents the external prerequisites:\n  - gh CLI scopes required (repo, workflow, delete_repo)\n  - VERCEL_TOKEN env / vercel login\n  - Vercel GitHub App installation URL\n- Optional env vars (BULMA_SONAR_TOKEN, VERCEL_TEAM_ID) listed with\n  what each one enables.\n- create command help now includes runnable examples that explain\n  the tradeoff of each --skip-* flag and how cwd determines the\n  generated site path.\n\nHelp text lives in src/help.ts as plain string constants so it can\nbe unit-tested without invoking Commander (which calls process.exit\non --help).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp7sHuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMRkQAJ0RryepIPt3Gzn9N6MQgscR\nhWto02j90JXf69QyEu3VdsRfm0guKErRKDYyuZMC2KMkHRpiqIwHuafE9EkpHZwD\n/mtFg+NY7L1vCQDq+cWA92ZsSKO+CeosF+Nux3oEtSw1uMeuQ6BWK9dlzwz66XEf\n6b2KOCHMmR+WxQau7xKHLmc+5QmukI5AfUOn+2urutERmpKIG8gwx5d7pVKKgBi9\nSRSVoUhkefia45le736F+abIa2p1iOQF6xnaH8JEcdgGmy/9qh9uIelJq8Aq8eI8\n0C1EQu+NspU9kbpc5+hrrBlIQ8LWqdwDvs6sGhvAcFOnDXrlqG16cQjtnQ13BEUm\nh4i2DzPyL+ef9qaDFNJ1uk91B/2py9kcs7wi85ne3wY7OaHil1nN0tKs81vvuLz1\n3WDKeh8LbBcaROKGQEmf3oa3+w4Vp/t0j7qbPhKV60wDbyodEM050OO+o5+wiQ4L\n7ENek4PDbLfLrlGWC5Fe35aoQoMh6uLuilbBouCUUoHB5rBNFNpDL4IloDK1XqVv\ng9qg69JVevAVufeJ+cdcD4q0oQGa5FzCXqyDRfctao1c07Dv65UId/AJcIf1hQ2X\ntXNZaMUthm7JX+QzQX84oiyuSl7Dgw9Vp/f6W8gx+QgDsKb2mMEYEVknaIinL+xz\ne19qOUtGih6JEh0+yvf1\n=MAGE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-27T01:54:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/leandrorojas/bulma/commit/448d0e2776de8500814468b0dac78bd07c79619e","node_id":"C_kwDOSDdtpNoAKDQ0OGQwZTI3NzZkZTg1MDA4MTQ0NjhiMGRhYzc4YmQwN2M3OTYxOWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/leandrorojas/bulma/commit/6446449a0d6e84f8b61de838cd17707c7218e01c","sha":"6446449a0d6e84f8b61de838cd17707c7218e01c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/6446449a0d6e84f8b61de838cd17707c7218e01c"}],"sha":"448d0e2776de8500814468b0dac78bd07c79619e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/448d0e2776de8500814468b0dac78bd07c79619e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2161005?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leandrorojas","id":2161005,"login":"leandrorojas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjEwMDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/6446449a0d6e84f8b61de838cd17707c7218e01c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-27T01:08:29Z","email":"leandrorojas@gmail.com","name":"leandrorojas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-27T01:08:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: scaffold GitHub Actions pipeline + QA approval gate in new sites (#6)\n\n* feat: scaffold GitHub Actions pipeline + QA approval gate in new sites\n\nAfter scaffolding the site repo, bulma now also:\n\n- **Writes 4 workflow files** into .github/workflows/ before the\n  initial commit, so they''re active from the first push:\n  - code-quality.yml — CodeRabbit (same-repo PRs only) + Unit Tests +\n    SonarQube quality gate, mirroring bulma''s own pipeline\n  - integration-tests.yml — runs `npm run test:integration` after\n    Code Quality completes on main, no-ops cleanly when the script\n    is absent\n  - prerelease.yml — publishes <pkg>-build-<run_number> to GitHub\n    Packages on every main push under the @leandrorojas scope\n  - release.yml — gated on a `production` environment (QA approval\n    gate) before publishing the stable release on v* tag pushes\n\n- **Sets the SONAR_TOKEN repo secret** when BULMA_SONAR_TOKEN is in\n  env. Delegated to `gh secret set --body -` (stdin pipe so the value\n  never touches argv or shell history). Failure is a warning, not\n  fatal.\n\n- **Pre-creates the production GitHub Environment** with the\n  authenticated user as required reviewer (the QA gate). On free-tier\n  private repos GitHub returns 422 for required-reviewer protection\n  rules — we detect that specific failure and skip pre-creation\n  cleanly (Actions auto-creates the env on first release.yml run,\n  just without the QA gate). Other failures degrade to warnings too.\n\n- **Rewrites push errors** that mention the missing `workflow` scope\n  into an actionable message pointing at\n  `gh auth refresh -h github.com -s workflow` and the orphan repo\n  URL for cleanup.\n\nAdds `--skip-actions` CLI flag for offline / dev runs, mirroring the\nexisting `--skip-vercel` pattern.\n\nValidated end-to-end with `bulma create site-pr6`:\n  ✓ all 4 workflow files committed and pushed\n  ✓ environment skip degraded gracefully on the free-tier 422\n  ✓ GitHub repo created with workflows in .github/workflows/\n  ✓ Vercel project + deployment still wire up correctly\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(sonar): satisfy S7786 + tssecurity:S6350 in github.ts\n\n- S7786: throw TypeError (not Error) for the type-check that data.id\n  must be a number — matches the rule''s expectation that type-check\n  failures are TypeError.\n- S6350: re-validate owner / repo / secretName immediately before the\n  `gh secret set` spawn call. The validation was already happening\n  via assertOwnerRepo + SECRET_NAME_PATTERN, but Sonar''s taint\n  analyzer doesn''t track regex assertions across helper boundaries.\n  Inlining the checks gives the analyzer a recognizable sanitization\n  shape and makes the safety property locally visible to readers.\n  Note: spawn does NOT use a shell here (no {shell: true}), so\n  there''s no actual injection vector — this is purely about\n  satisfying the static analysis.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address 11 CodeRabbit findings on Actions pipeline PR\n\nMajor:\n- workflows.ts: drop the deprecated coderabbitai/ai-pr-reviewer@v1\n  step from code-quality.yml. The action repo was archived in\n  Dec 2025; the supported integration is the CodeRabbit GitHub App\n  (installed account-wide, no workflow file needed). README will\n  document it as a manual prereq.\n- github.ts: setRepoSecret now redacts EVERY occurrence of the\n  secret value in stderr (replaceAll, not replace) — previously a\n  multi-occurrence stderr leaked the secret after the first match.\n\nMinor:\n- github.ts: add a 30s timeout to the `gh secret set` subprocess so\n  a hung CLI can''t stall the scaffold.\n- github.ts: handle stdin write errors on the gh subprocess instead\n  of letting them surface as uncaught exceptions.\n- github.ts: explicitly reject secret names with the reserved\n  GITHUB_ prefix (was implicit before — the regex allowed it).\n- workflows.ts: replace the hardcoded `@leandrorojas` scope with a\n  configurable scope passed by the caller. create.ts now resolves\n  the GitHub login via getAuthenticatedUser (replaces\n  getAuthenticatedUserId, returns {id, login}) and derives\n  `@${login}` for the scope at scaffold time. Sites under a\n  different account get the right scope.\n- create.ts: fix the duplicate \"step 8\" comment numbering.\n- create.test.ts: use path.normalize() in workflow-path substring\n  checks for Windows portability.\n- github.test.ts: assert multi-occurrence redaction; add the\n  GITHUB_ prefix rejection test.\n\nTrivial:\n- workflows.ts: deep-freeze the WORKFLOW_FILES result (array AND\n  each entry) so consumers can''t mutate either layer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f667750c3e6e3cee21533b53571943b48eced59e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/git/trees/f667750c3e6e3cee21533b53571943b48eced59e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/git/commits/6446449a0d6e84f8b61de838cd17707c7218e01c","verification":{"payload":"tree f667750c3e6e3cee21533b53571943b48eced59e\nparent 48b237eccd3c85a6a05098bf0a737345993ed628\nauthor leandrorojas <leandrorojas@gmail.com> 1777252109 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777252109 -0300\n\nfeat: scaffold GitHub Actions pipeline + QA approval gate in new sites (#6)\n\n* feat: scaffold GitHub Actions pipeline + QA approval gate in new sites\n\nAfter scaffolding the site repo, bulma now also:\n\n- **Writes 4 workflow files** into .github/workflows/ before the\n  initial commit, so they''re active from the first push:\n  - code-quality.yml — CodeRabbit (same-repo PRs only) + Unit Tests +\n    SonarQube quality gate, mirroring bulma''s own pipeline\n  - integration-tests.yml — runs `npm run test:integration` after\n    Code Quality completes on main, no-ops cleanly when the script\n    is absent\n  - prerelease.yml — publishes <pkg>-build-<run_number> to GitHub\n    Packages on every main push under the @leandrorojas scope\n  - release.yml — gated on a `production` environment (QA approval\n    gate) before publishing the stable release on v* tag pushes\n\n- **Sets the SONAR_TOKEN repo secret** when BULMA_SONAR_TOKEN is in\n  env. Delegated to `gh secret set --body -` (stdin pipe so the value\n  never touches argv or shell history). Failure is a warning, not\n  fatal.\n\n- **Pre-creates the production GitHub Environment** with the\n  authenticated user as required reviewer (the QA gate). On free-tier\n  private repos GitHub returns 422 for required-reviewer protection\n  rules — we detect that specific failure and skip pre-creation\n  cleanly (Actions auto-creates the env on first release.yml run,\n  just without the QA gate). Other failures degrade to warnings too.\n\n- **Rewrites push errors** that mention the missing `workflow` scope\n  into an actionable message pointing at\n  `gh auth refresh -h github.com -s workflow` and the orphan repo\n  URL for cleanup.\n\nAdds `--skip-actions` CLI flag for offline / dev runs, mirroring the\nexisting `--skip-vercel` pattern.\n\nValidated end-to-end with `bulma create site-pr6`:\n  ✓ all 4 workflow files committed and pushed\n  ✓ environment skip degraded gracefully on the free-tier 422\n  ✓ GitHub repo created with workflows in .github/workflows/\n  ✓ Vercel project + deployment still wire up correctly\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(sonar): satisfy S7786 + tssecurity:S6350 in github.ts\n\n- S7786: throw TypeError (not Error) for the type-check that data.id\n  must be a number — matches the rule''s expectation that type-check\n  failures are TypeError.\n- S6350: re-validate owner / repo / secretName immediately before the\n  `gh secret set` spawn call. The validation was already happening\n  via assertOwnerRepo + SECRET_NAME_PATTERN, but Sonar''s taint\n  analyzer doesn''t track regex assertions across helper boundaries.\n  Inlining the checks gives the analyzer a recognizable sanitization\n  shape and makes the safety property locally visible to readers.\n  Note: spawn does NOT use a shell here (no {shell: true}), so\n  there''s no actual injection vector — this is purely about\n  satisfying the static analysis.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address 11 CodeRabbit findings on Actions pipeline PR\n\nMajor:\n- workflows.ts: drop the deprecated coderabbitai/ai-pr-reviewer@v1\n  step from code-quality.yml. The action repo was archived in\n  Dec 2025; the supported integration is the CodeRabbit GitHub App\n  (installed account-wide, no workflow file needed). README will\n  document it as a manual prereq.\n- github.ts: setRepoSecret now redacts EVERY occurrence of the\n  secret value in stderr (replaceAll, not replace) — previously a\n  multi-occurrence stderr leaked the secret after the first match.\n\nMinor:\n- github.ts: add a 30s timeout to the `gh secret set` subprocess so\n  a hung CLI can''t stall the scaffold.\n- github.ts: handle stdin write errors on the gh subprocess instead\n  of letting them surface as uncaught exceptions.\n- github.ts: explicitly reject secret names with the reserved\n  GITHUB_ prefix (was implicit before — the regex allowed it).\n- workflows.ts: replace the hardcoded `@leandrorojas` scope with a\n  configurable scope passed by the caller. create.ts now resolves\n  the GitHub login via getAuthenticatedUser (replaces\n  getAuthenticatedUserId, returns {id, login}) and derives\n  `@${login}` for the scope at scaffold time. Sites under a\n  different account get the right scope.\n- create.ts: fix the duplicate \"step 8\" comment numbering.\n- create.test.ts: use path.normalize() in workflow-path substring\n  checks for Windows portability.\n- github.test.ts: assert multi-occurrence redaction; add the\n  GITHUB_ prefix rejection test.\n\nTrivial:\n- workflows.ts: deep-freeze the WORKFLOW_FILES result (array AND\n  each entry) so consumers can''t mutate either layer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp7rcNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8eEQAId1UCebfVG5kYnwi+KsG5sx\n9l8LGaqAahmyDkkFrkc36HSVUpyIv5PB0HDdJv3ZAYMoBop+qULciZd+MhSjr6lw\nRJx5ACwLAC4eb2ajXQexyYoVeR1jphxHCg8y4dNA9fVECAN6yZKwpCfK9FCO/Dvg\nueE5SzOJ0KTkZ/gVQP2JGTiHdjxtlpmW2wzqH0GVE1SCMBMIhGA1JlvN79RT/H/4\nygsdrkz+7yCGuMHnCDSHugE69nhPbSuR13XhXMDuFozmXyG0a6ph+TILBJwyqAIR\n3oXQyXfiEa2fbzjzSeQMhvn24pI5A4hEmWKL99wU9Rvw8wD+K9qza+UmIZFoLJ2Z\ng7Y2QoAWCV5xbQm9w1RKxrhUFREUUVRX4jF6nQ//oAvkojSQM43uEOsMemaL7/rk\nI/bwfD3gZLqf2UZxYJGdxAvn7dQjxCXfYFS5mFndg5M8h0+hAmOKYChkoduA5MUQ\neuukIC02pssCYha0hVYwkWkAT4o68CChKgKGrdzn0X1Bu5j+0pDFCq1mxAV8VnL1\nQ0AuadKnWdFRJeD1bu/NBcK3h2ORNbc5lSvWjyJ6s4pfMACLOAgt/sMeJrrjgBhO\neW9PyBGChzxe04OWZHMyojqG6J5J640MDvCKa2QaTaIxNj69b10mnIuNsnI6Ummx\n/0PSHczzrfKv8ZzOVlzh\n=zBSQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-27T01:08:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/leandrorojas/bulma/commit/6446449a0d6e84f8b61de838cd17707c7218e01c","node_id":"C_kwDOSDdtpNoAKDY0NDY0NDlhMGQ2ZTg0ZjhiNjFkZTgzOGNkMTc3MDdjNzIxOGUwMWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/leandrorojas/bulma/commit/48b237eccd3c85a6a05098bf0a737345993ed628","sha":"48b237eccd3c85a6a05098bf0a737345993ed628","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/48b237eccd3c85a6a05098bf0a737345993ed628"}],"sha":"6446449a0d6e84f8b61de838cd17707c7218e01c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/6446449a0d6e84f8b61de838cd17707c7218e01c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2161005?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leandrorojas","id":2161005,"login":"leandrorojas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjEwMDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/48b237eccd3c85a6a05098bf0a737345993ed628/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-26T23:22:10Z","email":"leandrorojas@gmail.com","name":"leandrorojas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-26T23:22:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: bump senzu submodule to pick up updated PR workflow (#5)\n\nPulls in the workflow doc updates from leandrorojas/senzu#2:\n- Sourcery documented as advisory check\n- SonarCloud API recipe for fetching actionable issue detail\n- Layered fix path for tssecurity:S8476 (which can''t be silenced\n  inline)\n- CodeRabbit incremental review behavior + empty-commit workaround\n- Rate-limit comments filtered by updated_at, not created_at\n\nSenzu now at 280e67d (was 73b6ec2 — the initial commit, two PRs\nbehind).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b6328fb99e80c2fd2c76b58a395228ce37041183","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/git/trees/b6328fb99e80c2fd2c76b58a395228ce37041183"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/git/commits/48b237eccd3c85a6a05098bf0a737345993ed628","verification":{"payload":"tree b6328fb99e80c2fd2c76b58a395228ce37041183\nparent 7b6f98104efd1cc19d308c17ba4b8a0f0d5b60d5\nauthor leandrorojas <leandrorojas@gmail.com> 1777245730 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777245730 -0300\n\nchore: bump senzu submodule to pick up updated PR workflow (#5)\n\nPulls in the workflow doc updates from leandrorojas/senzu#2:\n- Sourcery documented as advisory check\n- SonarCloud API recipe for fetching actionable issue detail\n- Layered fix path for tssecurity:S8476 (which can''t be silenced\n  inline)\n- CodeRabbit incremental review behavior + empty-commit workaround\n- Rate-limit comments filtered by updated_at, not created_at\n\nSenzu now at 280e67d (was 73b6ec2 — the initial commit, two PRs\nbehind).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp7p4iCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAg9wQAAT9F70nrSMYa4ANclNQl1f8\nQ+7BTlrVg5V6eLYdQrsS8v3MqvuOgoX9OJw/l4zigyu87zOQlnimOfcjmdrDzFZ+\nlaTeXybNU+iGFOCLrw7LNP+TFRAwXNZSmhlUqaRXx4UfpI/rzXXzFJqX6HsdJHQF\nNmvmn0vfuuxuposz/VEfRHsdAW0A0R/wTm5c7BOwIZlO0DcrMKB68JYEoPkAKu21\nAxB+xI4PR+7iIKod+I6VIT/FOEGxdw8H4lAp26uvwnHWrlpEcWP5Wn+BRrvhIz13\n4CU9MaURc8SPHHMfZ1u3S7m80qyatBapZM/yq0gC+vTwmYNFmhHEo/b/HGcPXua8\n8/AQ4F7NgGhtgS+beiuw4TtB2ojNDu2OHBBTfgFbLH8ybxr8PA5pzocC48BwVF4k\nMQl+aFgM+KWrT3czbi6SYfDMWxxIH+6MBqcK28RwaWGotQBQaZA++UWBrlrm28fG\nl9xjxkmlmfKCGV5dCyf53fjLUvOSqN8j4iA4KutxgcIM9F4DLGlyXOi7iBJPSsHr\nd6PPZ0TsVW+Khp/kRYBoN+heuk2LR1cF69cZjW3C+xysYySKWvvgh9a5YY6dxPr9\nyoD/FYJxAkGVvIfXgS7rMRvGYvuKc1zd4T/1+zw5HLBDCz2C6kRVULk9RZF0Ua3z\ngVsOJQ6D4jYgsEG2V1YT\n=A2lR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-26T23:22:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/leandrorojas/bulma/commit/48b237eccd3c85a6a05098bf0a737345993ed628","node_id":"C_kwDOSDdtpNoAKDQ4YjIzN2VjY2QzYzg1YTZhMDUwOThiZjBhNzM3MzQ1OTkzZWQ2Mjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/leandrorojas/bulma/commit/7b6f98104efd1cc19d308c17ba4b8a0f0d5b60d5","sha":"7b6f98104efd1cc19d308c17ba4b8a0f0d5b60d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/7b6f98104efd1cc19d308c17ba4b8a0f0d5b60d5"}],"sha":"48b237eccd3c85a6a05098bf0a737345993ed628","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/48b237eccd3c85a6a05098bf0a737345993ed628"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2161005?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leandrorojas","id":2161005,"login":"leandrorojas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjEwMDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/7b6f98104efd1cc19d308c17ba4b8a0f0d5b60d5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-26T22:59:11Z","email":"leandrorojas@gmail.com","name":"leandrorojas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-26T22:59:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vercel): pin nodeVersion + trigger initial deployment (#4)\n\n* fix(vercel): set nodeVersion via PATCH (POST /v10/projects rejects it)\n\nDiscovered by smoke test against the real Vercel API:\n\n  Vercel API error (create project): 400 Bad Request\n  Invalid request: should NOT have additional property `nodeVersion`.\n\nVercel''s POST /v10/projects endpoint doesn''t accept `nodeVersion` —\nthe only way to pin it is PATCH /v9/projects/{id} after creation.\n\n- Drop nodeVersion from CreateProjectOptions and the create body.\n- Add updateProjectNodeVersion(token, projectId, nodeVersion, scope?)\n  that issues the PATCH.\n- Wire it into the create flow right after createVercelProject. Treat\n  failure as a warning rather than fatal: the project itself is fine,\n  Vercel just falls back to its default Node version.\n- Update tests to assert the create body never contains nodeVersion\n  and the PATCH call happens with the right args.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(vercel): trigger initial production deployment after project create\n\nSecond bug surfaced by the smoke test (after the nodeVersion fix\nlanded): even with the project correctly created and linked to the\nGitHub repo, no deployment ever fired. Vercel doesn''t auto-deploy on\nproject creation — it only reacts to push *events* that occur after\nthe link is established. Since our flow pushes to GitHub before\ncreating the Vercel project, no event fires post-link and the project\nsits empty until somebody pushes again.\n\nFix: explicitly trigger a production deployment via\nPOST /v13/deployments with the linked repo''s gitSource right after\ncreateVercelProject + updateProjectNodeVersion. This requires the\nnumeric GitHub repo ID, so CreatedRepo now includes `id` (we already\ngot it back in the create-repo response, just weren''t returning it).\n\nValidated end-to-end with `bulma create site-pr4`:\n  ✓ Vercel project created (Node 20.x pinned)\n  ✓ Initial deployment triggered\n  ✓ pollDeploymentReady saw READY within 5 min\n  ✓ Production URL printed and live\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(sonar): suppress S8476 false positive on validated projectId\n\nSonarCloud''s tssecurity:S8476 (\"Tainted data should not flow into\nclient-side requests\") flags the URL template literal in\nupdateProjectNodeVersion despite:\n- assertValidProjectId(projectId) on the line above (regex-validated\n  against ^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,64}$),\n- encodeURIComponent(projectId) at the construction site itself.\n\nThe same pattern in pollDeploymentReady / getLatestProductionDeployment\ncleared the gate in PR #3, but Sonar''s analyzer doesn''t consistently\nrecognize the user-defined regex validator as a sanitizer for newly\nadded call paths. Suppress the specific false positive with a NOSONAR\ncomment + reason.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: log dashboard URL before propagating triggerDeployment failures\n\nCodeRabbit caught that triggerProductionDeployment was the only Vercel\ncall without dashboard-URL fallback on failure. Mirror the\npollDeploymentReady pattern: catch the error, log the resolved\ndashboard URL so the user has a breadcrumb, then re-throw — the\ndeployment didn''t fire, so this is a real failure (not best-effort\nlike updateProjectNodeVersion).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(sonar): build Vercel URLs via URL constructor instead of template literals\n\nInline NOSONAR is not honored for SonarCloud''s tssecurity:S8476 rule.\nRefactor URL construction to use new URL() + URL.pathname +\nURL.searchParams.set() — a \"URL builder\" shape that the analyzer\nrecognizes as safely encoded.\n\nReplaces the old withTeam helper with buildVercelUrl(pathSegments,\nquery). All callers migrated. encodeURIComponent is still applied at\neach call site for path segments derived from validated input\n(projectId, team slug). Query values pass through searchParams.set\nwhich percent-encodes automatically.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(sonar): assert API origin inside vercelFetch as the taint sink boundary\n\nThe URL-builder refactor in d3eb570 didn''t satisfy Sonar''s S8476 —\nthe pathname assignment in buildVercelUrl is still flagged as\n\"concatenation can propagate malicious content\".\n\nAdd an explicit `new URL(url)` parse + origin allow-list check inside\nvercelFetch itself. This is the actual sanitization boundary:\nregardless of how callers built the URL, we only ever issue requests\nto https://api.vercel.com. Sonar should recognize the URL constructor\n+ explicit origin check as a sanitizer; if it doesn''t, this still\nmakes the safety property explicit at the call site to fetch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(create): align nodeVersion catch comment with actual behavior\n\nSourcery flagged that the previous comment said \"4xx here doesn''t\ninvalidate the project\" but the catch block swallows *all* errors\n(4xx, 5xx, network). Sourcery''s suggested status-extraction fix uses\nad-hoc \\`any\\` casts across multiple error shapes — overkill given\nupdateProjectNodeVersion throws a plain Error, not a structured one.\n\nPragmatic call: swallowing every error here is correct. The Vercel\nproject was already created on the line above; the fallback is\nVercel''s default Node version, which works for React 19 + Webpack 5.\nForcing a full re-scaffold on a transient 5xx loses more than it\nsaves. The fix is to align the comment with the code, not narrow the\ncatch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: re-trigger CodeRabbit review on latest commit\n\nCodeRabbit''s incremental analyzer reviewed every commit since\n3d65b09 via the summary comment (\"No actionable comments were\ngenerated\") but didn''t post a fresh review-with-state. Pushing an\nempty commit forces a discrete APPROVED on the latest SHA so the\naudit trail matches workflow step 5 (review state must be APPROVED).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"50dc94c5b8f459bde838925b9561a9da935772b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/git/trees/50dc94c5b8f459bde838925b9561a9da935772b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/git/commits/7b6f98104efd1cc19d308c17ba4b8a0f0d5b60d5","verification":{"payload":"tree 50dc94c5b8f459bde838925b9561a9da935772b1\nparent 0e991927fa329d1d4557f592a227683121ce9c15\nauthor leandrorojas <leandrorojas@gmail.com> 1777244351 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777244351 -0300\n\nfix(vercel): pin nodeVersion + trigger initial deployment (#4)\n\n* fix(vercel): set nodeVersion via PATCH (POST /v10/projects rejects it)\n\nDiscovered by smoke test against the real Vercel API:\n\n  Vercel API error (create project): 400 Bad Request\n  Invalid request: should NOT have additional property `nodeVersion`.\n\nVercel''s POST /v10/projects endpoint doesn''t accept `nodeVersion` —\nthe only way to pin it is PATCH /v9/projects/{id} after creation.\n\n- Drop nodeVersion from CreateProjectOptions and the create body.\n- Add updateProjectNodeVersion(token, projectId, nodeVersion, scope?)\n  that issues the PATCH.\n- Wire it into the create flow right after createVercelProject. Treat\n  failure as a warning rather than fatal: the project itself is fine,\n  Vercel just falls back to its default Node version.\n- Update tests to assert the create body never contains nodeVersion\n  and the PATCH call happens with the right args.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(vercel): trigger initial production deployment after project create\n\nSecond bug surfaced by the smoke test (after the nodeVersion fix\nlanded): even with the project correctly created and linked to the\nGitHub repo, no deployment ever fired. Vercel doesn''t auto-deploy on\nproject creation — it only reacts to push *events* that occur after\nthe link is established. Since our flow pushes to GitHub before\ncreating the Vercel project, no event fires post-link and the project\nsits empty until somebody pushes again.\n\nFix: explicitly trigger a production deployment via\nPOST /v13/deployments with the linked repo''s gitSource right after\ncreateVercelProject + updateProjectNodeVersion. This requires the\nnumeric GitHub repo ID, so CreatedRepo now includes `id` (we already\ngot it back in the create-repo response, just weren''t returning it).\n\nValidated end-to-end with `bulma create site-pr4`:\n  ✓ Vercel project created (Node 20.x pinned)\n  ✓ Initial deployment triggered\n  ✓ pollDeploymentReady saw READY within 5 min\n  ✓ Production URL printed and live\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(sonar): suppress S8476 false positive on validated projectId\n\nSonarCloud''s tssecurity:S8476 (\"Tainted data should not flow into\nclient-side requests\") flags the URL template literal in\nupdateProjectNodeVersion despite:\n- assertValidProjectId(projectId) on the line above (regex-validated\n  against ^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,64}$),\n- encodeURIComponent(projectId) at the construction site itself.\n\nThe same pattern in pollDeploymentReady / getLatestProductionDeployment\ncleared the gate in PR #3, but Sonar''s analyzer doesn''t consistently\nrecognize the user-defined regex validator as a sanitizer for newly\nadded call paths. Suppress the specific false positive with a NOSONAR\ncomment + reason.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: log dashboard URL before propagating triggerDeployment failures\n\nCodeRabbit caught that triggerProductionDeployment was the only Vercel\ncall without dashboard-URL fallback on failure. Mirror the\npollDeploymentReady pattern: catch the error, log the resolved\ndashboard URL so the user has a breadcrumb, then re-throw — the\ndeployment didn''t fire, so this is a real failure (not best-effort\nlike updateProjectNodeVersion).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(sonar): build Vercel URLs via URL constructor instead of template literals\n\nInline NOSONAR is not honored for SonarCloud''s tssecurity:S8476 rule.\nRefactor URL construction to use new URL() + URL.pathname +\nURL.searchParams.set() — a \"URL builder\" shape that the analyzer\nrecognizes as safely encoded.\n\nReplaces the old withTeam helper with buildVercelUrl(pathSegments,\nquery). All callers migrated. encodeURIComponent is still applied at\neach call site for path segments derived from validated input\n(projectId, team slug). Query values pass through searchParams.set\nwhich percent-encodes automatically.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(sonar): assert API origin inside vercelFetch as the taint sink boundary\n\nThe URL-builder refactor in d3eb570 didn''t satisfy Sonar''s S8476 —\nthe pathname assignment in buildVercelUrl is still flagged as\n\"concatenation can propagate malicious content\".\n\nAdd an explicit `new URL(url)` parse + origin allow-list check inside\nvercelFetch itself. This is the actual sanitization boundary:\nregardless of how callers built the URL, we only ever issue requests\nto https://api.vercel.com. Sonar should recognize the URL constructor\n+ explicit origin check as a sanitizer; if it doesn''t, this still\nmakes the safety property explicit at the call site to fetch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(create): align nodeVersion catch comment with actual behavior\n\nSourcery flagged that the previous comment said \"4xx here doesn''t\ninvalidate the project\" but the catch block swallows *all* errors\n(4xx, 5xx, network). Sourcery''s suggested status-extraction fix uses\nad-hoc \\`any\\` casts across multiple error shapes — overkill given\nupdateProjectNodeVersion throws a plain Error, not a structured one.\n\nPragmatic call: swallowing every error here is correct. The Vercel\nproject was already created on the line above; the fallback is\nVercel''s default Node version, which works for React 19 + Webpack 5.\nForcing a full re-scaffold on a transient 5xx loses more than it\nsaves. The fix is to align the comment with the code, not narrow the\ncatch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: re-trigger CodeRabbit review on latest commit\n\nCodeRabbit''s incremental analyzer reviewed every commit since\n3d65b09 via the summary comment (\"No actionable comments were\ngenerated\") but didn''t post a fresh review-with-state. Pushing an\nempty commit forces a discrete APPROVED on the latest SHA so the\naudit trail matches workflow step 5 (review state must be APPROVED).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp7pi/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwIQQAFEDQlIPga0xZ1qZXC0mDKLX\nud9F/Bb+wggSVMqxYUkL20sLxsqFW9n66uKNcbbbc4TUXgQ2APPef/pZ1xLI9x7c\nubGW49CZY7HWe+lN17ffNjYJBZdycxpo81pSqwTefquEA5bOGC+VtksPme3NolFX\nDjvQ7esXe9l3jTs3wB6j0He9BAixwLh79J4B0yBVOfEkg03yjsxDTQijmjShCGmC\nWFsR2skHrU3ectFQ8dwbog/RrJss+UGVl36LiLLCTfSzhdQjNfaUxniGQHClFJ/k\ntkxzJuX2Tj1a5GHFFEJ0tprh5Z4m7JYVJzfe+9pLP7JloVJs8sF+Ezl1W37dtURd\nyWo+WukQoOqRwioJ+ERhrANytEfJXrX3k+w1nRKAmSeVt7BexTWr77RiJ2Oj73fH\nB/X8CDFOBfUwUso3Kox6utjql+dBaAjRSM3Y0GWSZKcby4+Xzc3zphpx2tcRjoos\nG5wa9CBDpuZUr5oPlLOZjmmLT75JANkxIDAZPYwv4FX5s271Dly0FUI8KrbAVbsk\nMTLKyMrLtQsjPaVD9fnzgqx9Hv2xzB/FDUEE4ISR4B4K/3GaYGAzMHQq8HJBgSlT\nsH4KOmbguV7YjLjsmBdLwTj2NSMo14YIf+KkpoxHGuSz3uRClFIx/XFdivQB4e0G\nfO+alstfi0Fmwm52WL6C\n=H5P0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-26T22:59:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/leandrorojas/bulma/commit/7b6f98104efd1cc19d308c17ba4b8a0f0d5b60d5","node_id":"C_kwDOSDdtpNoAKDdiNmY5ODEwNGVmZDFjYzE5ZDMwOGMxN2JhNGI4YTBmMGQ1YjYwZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/leandrorojas/bulma/commit/0e991927fa329d1d4557f592a227683121ce9c15","sha":"0e991927fa329d1d4557f592a227683121ce9c15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/0e991927fa329d1d4557f592a227683121ce9c15"}],"sha":"7b6f98104efd1cc19d308c17ba4b8a0f0d5b60d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/7b6f98104efd1cc19d308c17ba4b8a0f0d5b60d5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2161005?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leandrorojas","id":2161005,"login":"leandrorojas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjEwMDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leandrorojas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/commits/0e991927fa329d1d4557f592a227683121ce9c15/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-26T18:33:50Z","email":"leandrorojas@gmail.com","name":"leandrorojas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-26T18:33:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: automate Vercel project setup in bulma create (#3)\n\n* feat: automate Vercel project setup in `bulma create`\n\nAfter the GitHub repo is pushed, `bulma create` now:\n- Resolves a Vercel token (`VERCEL_TOKEN` env or vercel CLI auth.json) and\n  optional `VERCEL_TEAM_ID` for team scoping.\n- Verifies the Vercel GitHub App is installed for the target namespace with\n  unrestricted access — fails fast with a setup hint otherwise.\n- Writes a `vercel.json` (build/output/install + framework=null) into the\n  scaffolded site so the first deploy uses the right settings even before\n  the project''s CLI config catches up.\n- Creates a Vercel project linked to the new GitHub repo and pinned to\n  Node 20.x.\n- Polls the first production deployment for up to 5 min. READY → prints\n  the URL. Timeout → warning + dashboard link, scaffold succeeds. ERROR\n  or CANCELED → scaffold fails.\n\nPer-branch preview URLs are handled automatically by Vercel — no setup\nrequired on the bulma side.\n\nAdds `--skip-vercel` for offline / dev runs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address CodeRabbit findings and bump coverage on Vercel PR\n\n- vercel.ts: pollDeploymentReady now swallows transient API errors and\n  keeps polling until the deadline; only DeploymentFailedError\n  short-circuits, and the timeout message chains the last transient\n  error so callers can surface the real cause. Also tolerate a\n  malformed `deployments` field in getLatestProductionDeployment.\n- create.ts: when GitHub App isn''t installed, the error now points\n  the user at --skip-vercel and the orphan repo URL so they can clean\n  up explicitly. When pollDeploymentReady throws a non-timeout error,\n  we log the dashboard URL before re-throwing so the user has\n  somewhere to go.\n- auth.ts: separate JSON-parse failures from readFile failures so\n  corrupt CLI cache produces \"Corrupt vercel auth file\" instead of a\n  parser stack trace embedded in the fallback error. Extract\n  vercelCliAuthPaths and readVercelAuthFileFromPaths into pure,\n  parameterized helpers so they can be unit-tested.\n- vercel.test.ts: makeFetch now fails fast when a test exceeds its\n  scripted responses (catches double-fetch regressions) instead of\n  silently repeating the last response.\n- create.test.ts: replace the writeFile-vs-git-add ordering test\n  comment with an actual cross-spy ordering counter so a refactor\n  that moves writeFile after git add will fail loudly.\n- Coverage on new code is up materially (auth.ts 73% → 93%) so the\n  Sonar quality gate should pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(vercel): address Sonar quality-gate findings\n\n- Reduce pollDeploymentReady cognitive complexity from 17 to under 15\n  by extracting classifyDeployment + buildTimeoutMessage helpers.\n- Replace the nested ternary in the timeout-message construction with\n  a flat helper (formatUnknownError) that also covers unknown-shape\n  errors safely (Error → message, string → as-is, object → JSON,\n  fallback to literal \"unknown error\").\n- Validate Vercel project IDs at the API boundary\n  (assertValidProjectId) so taint analysis sees a clean source-to-sink\n  flow. Called in createVercelProject (response), pollDeploymentReady,\n  and getLatestProductionDeployment to defend any caller that bypasses\n  the create path.\n- Add tests for the validation rejection paths.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address 6 CodeRabbit findings on Vercel PR\n\n- create.ts: replace `vercelToken!` non-null assertions with a\n  discriminated VercelContext union so the post-skip-check path is\n  type-narrowed without the `!` operator.\n- create.ts: move the vercel.json write inside the same try/catch\n  that cleans up targetDir on copyDir failure, so a writeFile error\n  no longer leaks a partial scaffold.\n- create.ts: introduce getAccountSlug-based dashboard URLs. We now\n  resolve the actual Vercel account/team slug (via /v2/user or\n  /v2/teams/{id}) and use it for the warning + failure dashboard\n  links. Falls back to https://vercel.com/dashboard if resolution\n  fails so we never surface a 404 link.\n- vercel.ts: getAccountSlug helper supporting personal + team scope,\n  with both the nested ({user: {username}}) and flat ({username})\n  response shapes. Add Array.isArray() guard in\n  checkGitHubAppInstalled so a malformed response throws clearly\n  instead of crashing on .find().\n- auth.ts: correct the Windows CLI auth.json path —\n  %APPDATA%\\xdg.data\\com.vercel.cli\\auth.json (not\n  %LOCALAPPDATA%\\com.vercel.cli\\Data, which doesn''t exist).\n- create.test.ts: assert getVercelTeamId is not invoked under\n  --skip-vercel; cover the new dashboard slug + fallback paths and\n  the writeFile rollback boundary.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1c672f6501c42e4a4b8189f38ed97a55fd65f27e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/git/trees/1c672f6501c42e4a4b8189f38ed97a55fd65f27e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leandrorojas/bulma/git/commits/0e991927fa329d1d4557f592a227683121ce9c15","verification":{"payload":"tree 1c672f6501c42e4a4b8189f38ed97a55fd65f27e\nparent 44818d6b25fa2b5d498b3de3460f3755dff71a52\nauthor leandrorojas <leandrorojas@gmail.com> 1777228430 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777228430 -0300\n\nfeat: automate Vercel project setup in bulma create (#3)\n\n* feat: automate Vercel project setup in `bulma create`\n\nAfter the GitHub repo is pushed, `bulma create` now:\n- Resolves a Vercel token (`VERCEL_TOKEN` env or vercel CLI auth.json) and\n  optional `VERCEL_TEAM_ID` for team scoping.\n- Verifies the Vercel GitHub App is installed for the target namespace with\n  unrestricted access — fails fast with a setup hint otherwise.\n- Writes a `vercel.json` (build/output/install + framework=null) into the\n  scaffolded site so the first deploy uses the right settings even before\n  the project''s CLI config catches up.\n- Creates a Vercel project linked to the new GitHub repo and pinned to\n  Node 20.x.\n- Polls the first production deployment for up to 5 min. READY → prints\n  the URL. Timeout → warning + dashboard link, scaffold succeeds. ERROR\n  or CANCELED → scaffold fails.\n\nPer-branch preview URLs are handled automatically by Vercel — no setup\nrequired on the bulma side.\n\nAdds `--skip-vercel` for offline / dev runs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address CodeRabbit findings and bump coverage on Vercel PR\n\n- vercel.ts: pollDeploymentReady now swallows transient API errors and\n  keeps polling until the deadline; only DeploymentFailedError\n  short-circuits, and the timeout message chains the last transient\n  error so callers can surface the real cause. Also tolerate a\n  malformed `deployments` field in getLatestProductionDeployment.\n- create.ts: when GitHub App isn''t installed, the error now points\n  the user at --skip-vercel and the orphan repo URL so they can clean\n  up explicitly. When pollDeploymentReady throws a non-timeout error,\n  we log the dashboard URL before re-throwing so the user has\n  somewhere to go.\n- auth.ts: separate JSON-parse failures from readFile failures so\n  corrupt CLI cache produces \"Corrupt vercel auth file\" instead of a\n  parser stack trace embedded in the fallback error. Extract\n  vercelCliAuthPaths and readVercelAuthFileFromPaths into pure,\n  parameterized helpers so they can be unit-tested.\n- vercel.test.ts: makeFetch now fails fast when a test exceeds its\n  scripted responses (catches double-fetch regressions) instead of\n  silently repeating the last response.\n- create.test.ts: replace the writeFile-vs-git-add ordering test\n  comment with an actual cross-spy ordering counter so a refactor\n  that moves writeFile after git add will fail loudly.\n- Coverage on new code is up materially (auth.ts 73% → 93%) so the\n  Sonar quality gate should pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(vercel): address Sonar quality-gate findings\n\n- Reduce pollDeploymentReady cognitive complexity from 17 to under 15\n  by extracting classifyDeployment + buildTimeoutMessage helpers.\n- Replace the nested ternary in the timeout-message construction with\n  a flat helper (formatUnknownError) that also covers unknown-shape\n  errors safely (Error → message, string → as-is, object → JSON,\n  fallback to literal \"unknown error\").\n- Validate Vercel project IDs at the API boundary\n  (assertValidProjectId) so taint analysis sees a clean source-to-sink\n  flow. Called in createVercelProject (response), pollDeploymentReady,\n  and getLatestProductionDeployment to defend any caller that bypasses\n  the create path.\n- Add tests for the validation rejection paths.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address 6 CodeRabbit findings on Vercel PR\n\n- create.ts: replace `vercelToken!` non-null assertions with a\n  discriminated VercelContext union so the post-skip-check path is\n  type-narrowed without the `!` operator.\n- create.ts: move the vercel.json write inside the same try/catch\n  that cleans up targetDir on copyDir failure, so a writeFile error\n  no longer leaks a partial scaffold.\n- create.ts: introduce getAccountSlug-based dashboard URLs. We now\n  resolve the actual Vercel account/team slug (via /v2/user or\n  /v2/teams/{id}) and use it for the warning + failure dashboard\n  links. Falls back to https://vercel.com/dashboard if resolution\n  fails so we never surface a 404 link.\n- vercel.ts: getAccountSlug helper supporting personal + team scope,\n  with both the nested ({user: {username}}) and flat ({username})\n  response shapes. Add Array.isArray() guard in\n  checkGitHubAppInstalled so a malformed response throws clearly\n  instead of crashing on .find().\n- auth.ts: correct the Windows CLI auth.json path —\n  %APPDATA%\\xdg.data\\com.vercel.cli\\auth.json (not\n  %LOCALAPPDATA%\\com.vercel.cli\\Data, which doesn''t exist).\n- create.test.ts: assert getVercelTeamId is not invoked under\n  --skip-vercel; cover the new dashboard slug + fallback paths and\n  the writeFile rollback boundary.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp7lqOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAB0oQAKtRaUfsrT5voMHIrS67e2Im\niWFv7vc4rwmNDcJLQ54+ZcDN08x7nBb47hXCit8Xfu1nCDr0CVzLtOv3XgB1oHMW\ng0Mr4YkkHVNcv4775P+yfFLadmwTxzEc+1j0FcLKxA9C65/Z9LcOe09fC1GRj9UD\nqipN0SBydO7BRSI8B24DtBHDY+cbtUcoLuRYw1vfMUWI7/8GmnPuSRWTaeGd5Dhh\nL4lywAjGxeBAyXUgam2rCmVLgSVfhs/AlNLS6Xx3ahc0OLYuZYmOdkBa0w+3WkTP\niZhWdBc+fOZYM3mM/6fRnRpdcH7sn7ZD6GozcjqsBGRZS7Ozwj9c+GUgDEQwYF4P\n4pb1w6FU1s8kQFWe6/Qv2Zh8RRAfY2pjzO9Qr9aGGwvw+8DEVXmin6AI3yDShJGe\nbiaq8D2FLaAaKnL+u9mnxWgGWL1y3RbWGdP0S1u5v61WJCZOyYEy1B2jbaDUM4v+\n7g6tDN8Pvu67gzJaIw16dhsuqOh2eSC9AScG027WTkyxd37NsLyQBR4AbNTyAQQL\noOsGW382dnC/dyviywVbTwmaVzXV4YS/pQ4dvOXOUdQ/eNXMIsgLzxiC5uETqM/w\n62yCXYCwenOrjrsaf2vaNnEKfbWo9LOJudU3gNUX5V/olvCEoO7pgnr0bHhnn2ri\nNWaEt8EG2g+BdzT9H0QP\n=cMSb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-26T18:33:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/fol