thubusercontent.com/u/29812288?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel","id":29812288,"login":"jeandbonicel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5ODEyMjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/9f6943c10dc628eb3317d9863048be3bc5b41b75/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-19T09:02:15Z","email":"bonicel.ftl@gmail.com","name":"JD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-19T09:02:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(resources): add `reference` field type — FK relations across resources (#26)\n\n* feat(api-domain): add `reference` field type — FK relations across resources\n\nFirst-class `reference` field type unlocks two things at once: proper FK\nintegrity at the database level, and automatic Combobox pickers in the\ngenerated forms — including the self-references that power the `tree`\npage (which previously needed the caller to hand-roll a `parentId`).\n\nConfig shape:\n\n    {\"name\": \"departmentId\", \"type\": \"reference\", \"target\": \"department\"}\n\nBackend:\n* Java entity field → `Long` (plain FK id; keeps DTOs flat, no @ManyToOne\n  object navigation) with `@NotNull` when `required: true`.\n* Liquibase migration → `BIGINT` column + `addForeignKeyConstraint`\n  pointing at `{target}s(id)`. Self-references resolve within the same\n  changeset; cross-resource references require the target resource\n  earlier in the resources array.\n* TypeScript types → `number` on Create/Update/Response DTOs.\n* Integration-test generator skips `reference` fields from its sample\n  JSON body (can''t bootstrap target rows), and picks a non-reference\n  required field for the \"missing required field\" validation test.\n\nFrontend:\n* `form` / `edit` / `settings` auto-promote `type: \"reference\"` to a\n  Combobox lookup against the target''s list endpoint. Self-references\n  are now honoured (previously pre-filtered out by the emitters).\n* `tree` page resolves its parent pointer from the first\n  `type: \"reference\"` self-ref; falls back to the legacy `parentId`\n  literal so older configs keep working.\n* Body cast + state hydration for `reference` mirror the other numeric\n  types (`Number(form.x)` on write, `String(data.x)` on hydrate).\n\n17 new tests cover the backend/TS/frontend wiring; full suite is 245\ntests green. Vite build of a frontend-app fixture with form/edit/tree\npages over a self-referencing resource succeeds.\n\n* fix(ci): mypy col-reassign + ruff format in PR #26 files","tree":{"sha":"8587c3092fc167f9d6b4ae733b881b0541bbb1ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/trees/8587c3092fc167f9d6b4ae733b881b0541bbb1ee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/commits/9f6943c10dc628eb3317d9863048be3bc5b41b75","verification":{"payload":"tree 8587c3092fc167f9d6b4ae733b881b0541bbb1ee\nparent 24bd075e6401ca3aa71fff28b9b8b092413ad917\nauthor JD <bonicel.ftl@gmail.com> 1776589335 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776589335 +0200\n\nfeat(resources): add `reference` field type — FK relations across resources (#26)\n\n* feat(api-domain): add `reference` field type — FK relations across resources\n\nFirst-class `reference` field type unlocks two things at once: proper FK\nintegrity at the database level, and automatic Combobox pickers in the\ngenerated forms — including the self-references that power the `tree`\npage (which previously needed the caller to hand-roll a `parentId`).\n\nConfig shape:\n\n    {\"name\": \"departmentId\", \"type\": \"reference\", \"target\": \"department\"}\n\nBackend:\n* Java entity field → `Long` (plain FK id; keeps DTOs flat, no @ManyToOne\n  object navigation) with `@NotNull` when `required: true`.\n* Liquibase migration → `BIGINT` column + `addForeignKeyConstraint`\n  pointing at `{target}s(id)`. Self-references resolve within the same\n  changeset; cross-resource references require the target resource\n  earlier in the resources array.\n* TypeScript types → `number` on Create/Update/Response DTOs.\n* Integration-test generator skips `reference` fields from its sample\n  JSON body (can''t bootstrap target rows), and picks a non-reference\n  required field for the \"missing required field\" validation test.\n\nFrontend:\n* `form` / `edit` / `settings` auto-promote `type: \"reference\"` to a\n  Combobox lookup against the target''s list endpoint. Self-references\n  are now honoured (previously pre-filtered out by the emitters).\n* `tree` page resolves its parent pointer from the first\n  `type: \"reference\"` self-ref; falls back to the legacy `parentId`\n  literal so older configs keep working.\n* Body cast + state hydration for `reference` mirror the other numeric\n  types (`Number(form.x)` on write, `String(data.x)` on hydrate).\n\n17 new tests cover the backend/TS/frontend wiring; full suite is 245\ntests green. Vite build of a frontend-app fixture with form/edit/tree\npages over a self-referencing resource succeeds.\n\n* fix(ci): mypy col-reassign + ruff format in PR #26 files","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp5JoXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAx+cQAKQ6Qa5xxu73tv+jcGyoQk/j\n7UD2kexz9NnzgDepJuPlQWIDyhtb6doqS9A1/uv7/qq6jXOhyuQ0O/sk++ZVNK68\nyUjVOQudRPXmD1KikJoutIWlVvHI11Ou0b6jQuhSYdcL66bFFw5aAGF46YLOT9/M\nOk98ZuC8yJYVh3sWis6pFePrIlP26YiaNx6ZEKveW/YseGr4d+kPT2QsFh/B4S3N\n/5bJQ6viOJ+6T13fPHlLLCE0hQ9+mdg6L4mfu+bWmizbgyrXH7HqdOVLPpSkHsk1\nSl2TVioiQTV/uP8ACGJUepSD0k9Xpy3LVrcwK5YyOC/+fJ+R01jpVOB8VWZ3Sl3s\nrQCRDKReki8p6w85ozb30Par+8E3huRNOJjdARl8Y+QC90jheQEMGdeH2GGx4OZs\nr703jHR4J3oW3U2MbRwoFTjI+qmeu7jb7WEZ1nm464OqOFyvHHXCXRscXgHv9qJ4\nvqBBcfjZup88eYAizE2L1fjvJ06YV9ZTNQlQKemsJnxtSl4keja1amLQJIV0lNyx\nFgID93mkwajDjObYvTAx4JflwjfUl9D9FxLJkHEcbFhZldD4tHquaH+S/kkNBZ5i\nYd42f6sgJH5/hnlxeDZumK53ImVziM10/CBGi9lalZXTmYzNSucPvqMTlMhcL7VC\nxVhaeZ+mC1P1MixSvTK2\n=yTt/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-19T09:02:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commit/9f6943c10dc628eb3317d9863048be3bc5b41b75","node_id":"C_kwDOSDgQ39oAKDlmNjk0M2MxMGRjNjI4ZWIzMzE3ZDk4NjMwNDhiZTNiYzViNDFiNzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commit/24bd075e6401ca3aa71fff28b9b8b092413ad917","sha":"24bd075e6401ca3aa71fff28b9b8b092413ad917","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/24bd075e6401ca3aa71fff28b9b8b092413ad917"}],"sha":"9f6943c10dc628eb3317d9863048be3bc5b41b75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/9f6943c10dc628eb3317d9863048be3bc5b41b75"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29812288?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel","id":29812288,"login":"jeandbonicel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5ODEyMjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/24bd075e6401ca3aa71fff28b9b8b092413ad917/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T22:52:54Z","email":"bonicel.ftl@gmail.com","name":"JD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T22:52:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(pages): wire DatePicker and Combobox into form / edit / settings (#25)\n\nPost-audit PR B. Phase 0 shipped 12 shadcn components but the page\nemitters were still emitting native `<input type=\"date\">` and native\n`<select>` for resource lookups. Swapping those two widgets is the\ncheapest UX win available — zero backend changes, zero new libs,\npurely a different component the emitters reach for.\n\nSwaps (ui-kit branch only)\n--------------------------\n1. **Date fields** → ``<DatePicker>``\n   - Calendar-popover UX, keyboard navigation, locale-aware.\n   - Form state stays a ``YYYY-MM-DD`` string so the BE contract\n     doesn''t change: emitter converts ``string ↔ Date`` at the\n     component boundary via ``new Date(form.f)`` / ``d.toISOString().slice(0,10)``.\n\n2. **Resource-lookup dropdowns** → ``<Combobox>``\n   - Typeahead search built in; stays usable once the option list has\n     more than a handful of entries (native ``<select>`` on a list of\n     500 employees is unusable).\n   - Options built inline from the existing ``<resource>Options``\n     useQuery hook: ``{lkVar.map(opt => ({value: ..., label: ...}))}``.\n   - Value/onChange stay plain strings so form-state plumbing is\n     unchanged elsewhere.\n\nUnchanged on purpose:\n\n- ``datetime`` fields keep native ``<input type=\"datetime-local\">`` —\n  DatePicker has no time picker yet.\n- ``enum`` dropdowns keep native ``<select>`` — enum lists are short\n  enough that the native picker is fine.\n- Plain-HTML fallback (no ``--uikit``) keeps native ``<input>`` /\n  ``<select>`` — nothing to swap to without the ui-kit.\n\nAll three emitters (form, edit, settings) get the same treatment; their\nfield-input logic is still duplicated from the shared base — extracting\ninto ``pages/base.py`` is noted as a follow-up but deliberately out of\nscope for this PR.\n\nTests\n-----\ntests/test_page_types_edit.py gets 2 new tests:\n\n- ``test_edit_uses_datepicker_for_date_fields`` — asserts ``<DatePicker>``\n  is emitted, verifies the ``string ↔ Date`` bridge on both read and\n  write, and confirms no stale ``<Input type=\"date\">`` remains.\n- ``test_edit_uses_combobox_for_lookup_fields`` — asserts ``<Combobox>``\n  with an inline-built options array, Label wiring intact.\n\nThe existing ``test_edit_renders_type_aware_inputs`` is updated to match\nthe new DatePicker emission for dates (datetime-local stays the same).\n\nFull suite: 228/228. Ruff clean. End-to-end verified: generated a\nui-kit + api-client + frontend-app fixture with ``form`` / ``edit`` /\n``settings`` pages all using date + lookup fields; ``vite build``\nsucceeds.\n\nDocs: CLAUDE.md \"Smart form features\" section rewritten to describe\nthe new DatePicker/Combobox flow and the unchanged fallbacks.\n\nRoadmap\n-------\nThis was **PR B** from the post-Phase-2 audit. Remaining:\n\n- PR C — first-class ``reference`` field type + optional tree-traversal\n  endpoint\n- PR D (optional) — ``Form`` + react-hook-form refactor, row-click-to-detail\n- PR E — multi-select + tag input (new ui-kit components + new\n  ``stringArray`` / ``enumArray`` resource field types)","tree":{"sha":"5082b0590e7d98ea9bf5eadb10d889f07d904ea0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/trees/5082b0590e7d98ea9bf5eadb10d889f07d904ea0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/commits/24bd075e6401ca3aa71fff28b9b8b092413ad917","verification":{"payload":"tree 5082b0590e7d98ea9bf5eadb10d889f07d904ea0\nparent 7a123a88bc7c483749b692373433f5ea5df3b582\nauthor JD <bonicel.ftl@gmail.com> 1776552774 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776552774 +0200\n\nfeat(pages): wire DatePicker and Combobox into form / edit / settings (#25)\n\nPost-audit PR B. Phase 0 shipped 12 shadcn components but the page\nemitters were still emitting native `<input type=\"date\">` and native\n`<select>` for resource lookups. Swapping those two widgets is the\ncheapest UX win available — zero backend changes, zero new libs,\npurely a different component the emitters reach for.\n\nSwaps (ui-kit branch only)\n--------------------------\n1. **Date fields** → ``<DatePicker>``\n   - Calendar-popover UX, keyboard navigation, locale-aware.\n   - Form state stays a ``YYYY-MM-DD`` string so the BE contract\n     doesn''t change: emitter converts ``string ↔ Date`` at the\n     component boundary via ``new Date(form.f)`` / ``d.toISOString().slice(0,10)``.\n\n2. **Resource-lookup dropdowns** → ``<Combobox>``\n   - Typeahead search built in; stays usable once the option list has\n     more than a handful of entries (native ``<select>`` on a list of\n     500 employees is unusable).\n   - Options built inline from the existing ``<resource>Options``\n     useQuery hook: ``{lkVar.map(opt => ({value: ..., label: ...}))}``.\n   - Value/onChange stay plain strings so form-state plumbing is\n     unchanged elsewhere.\n\nUnchanged on purpose:\n\n- ``datetime`` fields keep native ``<input type=\"datetime-local\">`` —\n  DatePicker has no time picker yet.\n- ``enum`` dropdowns keep native ``<select>`` — enum lists are short\n  enough that the native picker is fine.\n- Plain-HTML fallback (no ``--uikit``) keeps native ``<input>`` /\n  ``<select>`` — nothing to swap to without the ui-kit.\n\nAll three emitters (form, edit, settings) get the same treatment; their\nfield-input logic is still duplicated from the shared base — extracting\ninto ``pages/base.py`` is noted as a follow-up but deliberately out of\nscope for this PR.\n\nTests\n-----\ntests/test_page_types_edit.py gets 2 new tests:\n\n- ``test_edit_uses_datepicker_for_date_fields`` — asserts ``<DatePicker>``\n  is emitted, verifies the ``string ↔ Date`` bridge on both read and\n  write, and confirms no stale ``<Input type=\"date\">`` remains.\n- ``test_edit_uses_combobox_for_lookup_fields`` — asserts ``<Combobox>``\n  with an inline-built options array, Label wiring intact.\n\nThe existing ``test_edit_renders_type_aware_inputs`` is updated to match\nthe new DatePicker emission for dates (datetime-local stays the same).\n\nFull suite: 228/228. Ruff clean. End-to-end verified: generated a\nui-kit + api-client + frontend-app fixture with ``form`` / ``edit`` /\n``settings`` pages all using date + lookup fields; ``vite build``\nsucceeds.\n\nDocs: CLAUDE.md \"Smart form features\" section rewritten to describe\nthe new DatePicker/Combobox flow and the unchanged fallbacks.\n\nRoadmap\n-------\nThis was **PR B** from the post-Phase-2 audit. Remaining:\n\n- PR C — first-class ``reference`` field type + optional tree-traversal\n  endpoint\n- PR D (optional) — ``Form`` + react-hook-form refactor, row-click-to-detail\n- PR E — multi-select + tag input (new ui-kit components + new\n  ``stringArray`` / ``enumArray`` resource field types)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp5AtGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANl4QAIzXOj2YixSOw2hQWsJbmfK9\nC4+ceeEA8v7zfF4BnqvFL3VxlsL+Mf+Wh0MyT2M3ZOKhAnOZeRRw86+n0NhhrKC4\n7OtHsMzOiuCq26yTcQIhWL9IECSOwQmBcN/Yd/ojC40VppGM9SbBOhKIFlqLzCJO\nIGIAFgWK76p2uyxdauGI8Gdz8O7RdmESFo9ylFFIK8O8LKYwroCj/4rDKsits1II\n6gKV3F61XYWPccnFwp1DHlnqPipwGX0AoM7vTJ8RPpOVbtH7V8Bka8FhtnbQ05Wt\nRTYMkMWc1gAEJ0iw9HxiCTN6lFrBJKVTee3r8TB1C+apiqcOd7gJ6kDy8f4bxKRQ\nKWNt+ftNEDRvfFCjnzfM5gy0tmcvMVkKLxvOe0dWkkuntsbRcSgRRsCl6KIyR8KH\ntuCQB5J/4Q4hUOAtmmArURrEuSlGNJFufIfXsRo0YiP7/aZxuG196jNFc4K75xYN\nh47DsbLULpTw/tycJ8HXLCr6jPbEcOm2iDJeJgtYB0r5mngp257OQ2i90kGM1pP8\n2AKIlSdafLm2zfIBRvn9zP1O8HAxh8mO1nU+6vsjlaq2/+0zprp6dXvEaukY26dI\nxbSCW7PUAxB8MAbGc2II+5sdv+SdvWqN1m/iNuNvqrDAP+1A80LxWF6bJlTBJ3Cv\njuf6cFH820kZ9M96ziCQ\n=hYWG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-18T22:52:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commit/24bd075e6401ca3aa71fff28b9b8b092413ad917","node_id":"C_kwDOSDgQ39oAKDI0YmQwNzVlNjQwMWNhM2FhNzFmZmYyOGI5YjhiMDkyNDEzYWQ5MTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commit/7a123a88bc7c483749b692373433f5ea5df3b582","sha":"7a123a88bc7c483749b692373433f5ea5df3b582","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/7a123a88bc7c483749b692373433f5ea5df3b582"}],"sha":"24bd075e6401ca3aa71fff28b9b8b092413ad917","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/24bd075e6401ca3aa71fff28b9b8b092413ad917"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29812288?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel","id":29812288,"login":"jeandbonicel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5ODEyMjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/7a123a88bc7c483749b692373433f5ea5df3b582/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T22:39:31Z","email":"bonicel.ftl@gmail.com","name":"JD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T22:39:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(api-domain): PATCH endpoint + singleton resources + enum-DTO fix (#24)\n\nCloses two real correctness gaps between the Phase 2 frontend page types\nand what the api-domain controller actually exposes. Before this PR,\nthe `kanban` and `settings` page types would 405/404 against a freshly\ngenerated backend.\n\nPATCH endpoint (for `kanban`)\n-----------------------------\nThe kanban page drags a card and sends `PATCH /{resource}/{id}` with a\npartial body like ``{\"status\": \"done\"}``. The generated controller only\nhad PUT, so every drop would 405. And even if PATCH were routed, the\nexisting ``UpdateXxxRequest`` DTO applied ``@NotBlank``/``@NotNull`` to\nevery required field — the partial body would fail validation.\n\nNow each non-singleton resource gets:\n\n* ``Patch{Entity}Request`` DTO — identical field list to Update, but\n  **never** emits ``@NotBlank`` / ``@NotNull``. Size / Min / Max /\n  Pattern stay because those only fire when the field is present.\n* ``service.patch(id, PatchXxxRequest)`` — null-checks each field and\n  only overwrites the non-null ones. Booleans are already `Boolean`\n  wrappers, so null means \"don''t change\".\n* Controller ``@PatchMapping(\"/{id}\")`` wired to the service method.\n\nSingleton mode (for `settings`)\n-------------------------------\nThe settings page treats the resource as one record per tenant:\n``GET /{resource}`` returns the singleton, ``PUT /{resource}`` updates\nit — no id in the URL, no pagination. The standard CRUD controller\nhardcoded `/{id}` in every method, so both calls 404ed.\n\nNew resource flag:\n\n    {\"name\": \"orgSettings\", \"singleton\": true, \"fields\": [...]}\n\nWhen present:\n\n* Service gets ``getSingleton()`` / ``updateSingleton()``. The getter\n  lazily creates the one-per-tenant row on first read, so callers\n  never have to bootstrap. Hibernate''s tenant filter scopes\n  ``findAll()`` for free.\n* Controller emits ``GET /{resource}`` + ``PUT /{resource}`` only —\n  no POST, DELETE, PATCH, or list.\n* ``Create*Request`` and ``Patch*Request`` DTOs are skipped (nothing\n  to create, nothing to partially update against).\n* Integration test is skipped for now — the existing template assumes\n  collection endpoints.\n\nEnum-DTO import bug (pre-existing, surfaced by new tests)\n---------------------------------------------------------\nRegression I stumbled into while verifying PATCH on a resource with\nenum fields: enum classes live in ``{pkg}.domain.model`` but DTOs live\nin ``{pkg}.interfaces.rest.dto``. ``_collect_imports`` didn''t emit the\ncross-package import for enums, so every Create/Update/Response DTO\nwith an enum field has been referencing undeclared types — the\ngenerated code only happened to compile if the consumer was in the\nsame package (the entity class itself).\n\nAdded ``_collect_enum_imports(pkg, fields)`` and wired it into all\nfour DTO generators (Create, Update, Patch, Response).\n\nTests\n-----\ntests/test_resources.py adds 9 assertions:\n\n* PATCH: PatchRequest DTO shape (no NotBlank/NotNull, keeps Size/Min),\n  controller PATCH endpoint, service merges-only-non-null logic\n* Singleton: controller with no `/{id}` paths and no POST/DELETE/PATCH,\n  service lazy-create-on-read, skipped Create/Patch DTOs, skipped\n  integration test, mixed singleton + regular resources side by side\n* Enum import regression guard\n\nFull suite: 226/226. Ruff clean. Generated fixture (regular ticket\nresource + singleton orgSettings, both with enum fields) produces\nsyntactically valid Java — hand-verified the controller, service, and\nall four DTOs.\n\nDocs: CLAUDE.md gets an updated endpoint list, a singleton mode\nsubsection, and a PATCH note.","tree":{"sha":"a0c23ab3b112bfe9cc6f9cd1539711dd410d9775","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/trees/a0c23ab3b112bfe9cc6f9cd1539711dd410d9775"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/commits/7a123a88bc7c483749b692373433f5ea5df3b582","verification":{"payload":"tree a0c23ab3b112bfe9cc6f9cd1539711dd410d9775\nparent 86f28585fecb9ca9d463b11827652fbd6147aec3\nauthor JD <bonicel.ftl@gmail.com> 1776551971 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776551971 +0200\n\nfeat(api-domain): PATCH endpoint + singleton resources + enum-DTO fix (#24)\n\nCloses two real correctness gaps between the Phase 2 frontend page types\nand what the api-domain controller actually exposes. Before this PR,\nthe `kanban` and `settings` page types would 405/404 against a freshly\ngenerated backend.\n\nPATCH endpoint (for `kanban`)\n-----------------------------\nThe kanban page drags a card and sends `PATCH /{resource}/{id}` with a\npartial body like ``{\"status\": \"done\"}``. The generated controller only\nhad PUT, so every drop would 405. And even if PATCH were routed, the\nexisting ``UpdateXxxRequest`` DTO applied ``@NotBlank``/``@NotNull`` to\nevery required field — the partial body would fail validation.\n\nNow each non-singleton resource gets:\n\n* ``Patch{Entity}Request`` DTO — identical field list to Update, but\n  **never** emits ``@NotBlank`` / ``@NotNull``. Size / Min / Max /\n  Pattern stay because those only fire when the field is present.\n* ``service.patch(id, PatchXxxRequest)`` — null-checks each field and\n  only overwrites the non-null ones. Booleans are already `Boolean`\n  wrappers, so null means \"don''t change\".\n* Controller ``@PatchMapping(\"/{id}\")`` wired to the service method.\n\nSingleton mode (for `settings`)\n-------------------------------\nThe settings page treats the resource as one record per tenant:\n``GET /{resource}`` returns the singleton, ``PUT /{resource}`` updates\nit — no id in the URL, no pagination. The standard CRUD controller\nhardcoded `/{id}` in every method, so both calls 404ed.\n\nNew resource flag:\n\n    {\"name\": \"orgSettings\", \"singleton\": true, \"fields\": [...]}\n\nWhen present:\n\n* Service gets ``getSingleton()`` / ``updateSingleton()``. The getter\n  lazily creates the one-per-tenant row on first read, so callers\n  never have to bootstrap. Hibernate''s tenant filter scopes\n  ``findAll()`` for free.\n* Controller emits ``GET /{resource}`` + ``PUT /{resource}`` only —\n  no POST, DELETE, PATCH, or list.\n* ``Create*Request`` and ``Patch*Request`` DTOs are skipped (nothing\n  to create, nothing to partially update against).\n* Integration test is skipped for now — the existing template assumes\n  collection endpoints.\n\nEnum-DTO import bug (pre-existing, surfaced by new tests)\n---------------------------------------------------------\nRegression I stumbled into while verifying PATCH on a resource with\nenum fields: enum classes live in ``{pkg}.domain.model`` but DTOs live\nin ``{pkg}.interfaces.rest.dto``. ``_collect_imports`` didn''t emit the\ncross-package import for enums, so every Create/Update/Response DTO\nwith an enum field has been referencing undeclared types — the\ngenerated code only happened to compile if the consumer was in the\nsame package (the entity class itself).\n\nAdded ``_collect_enum_imports(pkg, fields)`` and wired it into all\nfour DTO generators (Create, Update, Patch, Response).\n\nTests\n-----\ntests/test_resources.py adds 9 assertions:\n\n* PATCH: PatchRequest DTO shape (no NotBlank/NotNull, keeps Size/Min),\n  controller PATCH endpoint, service merges-only-non-null logic\n* Singleton: controller with no `/{id}` paths and no POST/DELETE/PATCH,\n  service lazy-create-on-read, skipped Create/Patch DTOs, skipped\n  integration test, mixed singleton + regular resources side by side\n* Enum import regression guard\n\nFull suite: 226/226. Ruff clean. Generated fixture (regular ticket\nresource + singleton orgSettings, both with enum fields) produces\nsyntactically valid Java — hand-verified the controller, service, and\nall four DTOs.\n\nDocs: CLAUDE.md gets an updated endpoint list, a singleton mode\nsubsection, and a PATCH note.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp5AgjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAxEQAAy8W32smgqJPpda5M39M0db\nyzEUG2exybzWy4gVcdNejooBaWlx8G/JFyOoK6suW09OaqNjC8sj/TIEezOORZSV\nfzo8T0k2mpp4jreANFKZtdNMUHhNp26NxaVbno8wp1sTFyEnHjRsyxNaZ1aD7S+s\n6y2ORoAAOG+Ug57PdIqqgDX1HHC1fu+IaKU8S0PqIRHUwpDgLd99J6ssxx46seWE\nKcNK6HKTzcQpwma6W8ODFSjEHqzSLdePrBFkRa1pyEhoTE+ghpdHoSharxHxW0Mp\nKeot2LZVkGafbraU3tYkHZSeWB6bKviRTF69m3XAujv8Enjo19uuOutszi1sYB1f\nE7Ub7H1RV87s0GFOX9acSk/1yxtm1asxgnAaUj9EvkXNSuAG7kbaAbGb2yPB1G0w\ngpNt1EZwNC+a09MaaZVds3LlcLbG74eM9WKuvEEYYtmwKXrpMwB1nj2nGiXmKTow\nmm7/gzjXyN4oujRYqsTaqNIa35jTUXDkyaQ2iUA84yWEx2wqw4L8glz7AduPl9y3\nQO9Uh9ZhiSXELyJMPL5ZZYqoqzbCZUP+c9UnxBUDkElxRIdhNqc4nwG67TbD6/yA\nk/4+dUNE3JWE9gOlhQZ2IObNghoJpO3GfZfbyteTg5FNQWfZMT6YvXRaveUPQE87\n7BXFzLn4nFXwVMBeu623\n=SjBs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-18T22:39:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commit/7a123a88bc7c483749b692373433f5ea5df3b582","node_id":"C_kwDOSDgQ39oAKDdhMTIzYTg4YmM3YzQ4Mzc0OWI2OTIzNzM0MzNmNWVhNWRmM2I1ODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commit/86f28585fecb9ca9d463b11827652fbd6147aec3","sha":"86f28585fecb9ca9d463b11827652fbd6147aec3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/86f28585fecb9ca9d463b11827652fbd6147aec3"}],"sha":"7a123a88bc7c483749b692373433f5ea5df3b582","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/7a123a88bc7c483749b692373433f5ea5df3b582"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29812288?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel","id":29812288,"login":"jeandbonicel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5ODEyMjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/86f28585fecb9ca9d463b11827652fbd6147aec3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T22:20:53Z","email":"bonicel.ftl@gmail.com","name":"JD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T22:20:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(pages): add `calendar` page type — schedule-x month/week/day view (#23)\n\nSeventh and final Phase 2 page type. **Completes the catalog of 10\npage types** (3 pre-existing + 7 net-new) and closes out the SmartHR\nskeleton coverage goal from the original plan.\n\nTransforms records into `schedule-x` events and renders them in a\nmulti-view calendar (month grid, week, day). Suited for attendance,\nleave requests, bookings, deadlines — anything with a primary date and\nan optional end date.\n\nField picking\n-------------\n1. Date (required): explicit `dateField` > name hint (`date` / `startDate`\n   / `start` / `when` on a temporal field) > first `date`/`datetime` field.\n2. End (optional): explicit `endField` > next temporal field after start\n   > same field as start (degrades into a single-cell event).\n3. Title: first `string` field; falls back to `id`.\n\nIf the resource has no `date` or `datetime` field at all, the emitter\nbails gracefully and writes a read-only placeholder page keyed on a new\ni18n string (`calendarNeedsDateField`) — better than a runtime crash.\n\nDate formatting\n---------------\nschedule-x expects `YYYY-MM-DD` (all-day) or `YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm` (timed).\nThe emitter generates the right conversion per field type:\n\n  date     -> String(v).slice(0, 10)\n  datetime -> String(v).slice(0, 16).replace(\"T\", \" \")\n\nRecords with null start are skipped at transform time so schedule-x\nnever sees a malformed event.\n\nDeps\n----\nAdded to frontend-app runtime deps:\n  @schedule-x/react         (^2.0.0)\n  @schedule-x/calendar      (^2.0.0)\n  @schedule-x/theme-default (^2.0.0)  -- CSS imported directly in the\n                                         emitted page\n\ni18n\n----\nOne new key: `calendarNeedsDateField` (EN: \"This calendar has no date\nfield configured.\" / FR: \"Ce calendrier n''a pas de champ de date\nconfiguré.\").\n\nTests\n-----\ntests/test_page_types_calendar.py adds 17 tests covering registration,\nthe three-tier date-field resolution (name hint / explicit / first\ntemporal), explicit + default end-field resolution, the\nend-defaults-to-start edge case, no-date-field graceful fallback, the\npaginated fetch with calendar-scoped queryKey, null-start skipping,\ntitle resolution (string field / id fallback), useMemo wrapping,\nschedule-x imports + month/week/day views, datetime-to-schedule-x\nformat conversion, and both wrappers (ui-kit Card vs plain bordered\ndiv).\n\nFull suite: 217/217. Ruff clean. End-to-end verified: fixture with\nui-kit + api-client + frontend-app, `vite build` succeeds.\n\nPhase 2: 7/7 landed. Catalog complete:\n  list · form · dashboard  (pre-existing)\n  detail · grid · edit · settings · tree · kanban · calendar  (new)","tree":{"sha":"a5c55aafbea9c5b1af4afd1723619385c0f030ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/trees/a5c55aafbea9c5b1af4afd1723619385c0f030ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/commits/86f28585fecb9ca9d463b11827652fbd6147aec3","verification":{"payload":"tree a5c55aafbea9c5b1af4afd1723619385c0f030ac\nparent 124429fdf8c3c2b7db6a60effa3d62c8f922f8fc\nauthor JD <bonicel.ftl@gmail.com> 1776550853 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776550853 +0200\n\nfeat(pages): add `calendar` page type — schedule-x month/week/day view (#23)\n\nSeventh and final Phase 2 page type. **Completes the catalog of 10\npage types** (3 pre-existing + 7 net-new) and closes out the SmartHR\nskeleton coverage goal from the original plan.\n\nTransforms records into `schedule-x` events and renders them in a\nmulti-view calendar (month grid, week, day). Suited for attendance,\nleave requests, bookings, deadlines — anything with a primary date and\nan optional end date.\n\nField picking\n-------------\n1. Date (required): explicit `dateField` > name hint (`date` / `startDate`\n   / `start` / `when` on a temporal field) > first `date`/`datetime` field.\n2. End (optional): explicit `endField` > next temporal field after start\n   > same field as start (degrades into a single-cell event).\n3. Title: first `string` field; falls back to `id`.\n\nIf the resource has no `date` or `datetime` field at all, the emitter\nbails gracefully and writes a read-only placeholder page keyed on a new\ni18n string (`calendarNeedsDateField`) — better than a runtime crash.\n\nDate formatting\n---------------\nschedule-x expects `YYYY-MM-DD` (all-day) or `YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm` (timed).\nThe emitter generates the right conversion per field type:\n\n  date     -> String(v).slice(0, 10)\n  datetime -> String(v).slice(0, 16).replace(\"T\", \" \")\n\nRecords with null start are skipped at transform time so schedule-x\nnever sees a malformed event.\n\nDeps\n----\nAdded to frontend-app runtime deps:\n  @schedule-x/react         (^2.0.0)\n  @schedule-x/calendar      (^2.0.0)\n  @schedule-x/theme-default (^2.0.0)  -- CSS imported directly in the\n                                         emitted page\n\ni18n\n----\nOne new key: `calendarNeedsDateField` (EN: \"This calendar has no date\nfield configured.\" / FR: \"Ce calendrier n''a pas de champ de date\nconfiguré.\").\n\nTests\n-----\ntests/test_page_types_calendar.py adds 17 tests covering registration,\nthe three-tier date-field resolution (name hint / explicit / first\ntemporal), explicit + default end-field resolution, the\nend-defaults-to-start edge case, no-date-field graceful fallback, the\npaginated fetch with calendar-scoped queryKey, null-start skipping,\ntitle resolution (string field / id fallback), useMemo wrapping,\nschedule-x imports + month/week/day views, datetime-to-schedule-x\nformat conversion, and both wrappers (ui-kit Card vs plain bordered\ndiv).\n\nFull suite: 217/217. Ruff clean. End-to-end verified: fixture with\nui-kit + api-client + frontend-app, `vite build` succeeds.\n\nPhase 2: 7/7 landed. Catalog complete:\n  list · form · dashboard  (pre-existing)\n  detail · grid · edit · settings · tree · kanban · calendar  (new)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp5APFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbBsQACrQMYp54X17aGnjhpGBT7hu\nQep9Tk6Dupe8f3wMMF076Xrn3hIk6g/D3xIy1hnYiPZKoE9AbsE2eNS5bbXiBRTU\ntjDZCvo3ycH3YlXWhusIAG8Fuub80MnChmvgUdL6SGA5hChUcqODt4kfgaiJvwTZ\nlZ+MlVxKLZUdEdAzQWaN/E9XPROZs1IRTL1wvFaH0wuXxu/83c3p8vLe4nCGW5Bl\n6SFFwcgCpODH0e6BEibBhKN62DoLFvKC+LTIgvbxCr/3rADbfmggBcXxktEqAjEa\ntiwrW32CLJfJhV3DonTTkrJVt8hZxri9XvLFhrTIHMQLQXaWHWsUtHtth8UZxsog\nW7vj6LLJu4z+D3/jGQN3YvuQen9M000ok11SU7ZzEoR3pp+Rf0ZY/WTmEyou3jPO\nVs1WKZe5PNUNm3yE8XXD+Z35XhrwxKaMPOO5EPlbPdKK4+lP2CaPjix6sHDfq/GG\n9sJJpaIL4E+0Kz69Gcs765EurWjwq2vn8kolwdgb2OUbrOnJqYGbJ2N3bOM+l1f0\nIv9U7+ooddUzNp0mK397nWYM4FPsCANXUrPclyW+uXMqPGb+U8UIUuwQzZAzqYUN\nLUMeIHS+o7zYJyjK5BDDtz58IgCQ8Qza5MGh5dswf6YygypHR8Jw/qKV1f9KUqnz\nYh55bYBjHQDz0/nDR9cT\n=rjmZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-18T22:20:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commit/86f28585fecb9ca9d463b11827652fbd6147aec3","node_id":"C_kwDOSDgQ39oAKDg2ZjI4NTg1ZmVjYjljYTlkNDYzYjExODI3NjUyZmJkNjE0N2FlYzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commit/124429fdf8c3c2b7db6a60effa3d62c8f922f8fc","sha":"124429fdf8c3c2b7db6a60effa3d62c8f922f8fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/124429fdf8c3c2b7db6a60effa3d62c8f922f8fc"}],"sha":"86f28585fecb9ca9d463b11827652fbd6147aec3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/86f28585fecb9ca9d463b11827652fbd6147aec3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29812288?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel","id":29812288,"login":"jeandbonicel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5ODEyMjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/124429fdf8c3c2b7db6a60effa3d62c8f922f8fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T22:10:25Z","email":"bonicel.ftl@gmail.com","name":"JD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T22:10:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(pages): add `kanban` page type — drag-and-drop board by status enum (#22)\n\nSixth Phase 2 page type. Renders records in columns keyed by an enum\nfield''s values; dropping a card into a different column PATCHes the\nrecord''s status field with the new column value, with an optimistic\nlocal update so the UI never lags while the mutation is in flight.\n\nColumn resolution\n-----------------\n1. Explicit `statusField` in the page config wins.\n2. Otherwise, prefer an enum field whose name matches a status-y hint:\n   `status` / `state` / `stage` / `phase`. That convention matches\n   nearly every kanban board in the wild — auto-detection picks the\n   right field when a resource has multiple enums (e.g. `priority`\n   alongside `status`).\n3. Fall back to the first enum field with a `values` array.\n4. With no enum at all, the emitter still generates a valid page — a\n   single \"Backlog\" column containing every record. Graceful fallback\n   rather than a hard error.\n\nDrag + drop\n-----------\n- `@dnd-kit/core` `DndContext` wraps the board; each column is a\n  `SortableContext` with `verticalListSortingStrategy`.\n- `PointerSensor` with `distance: 4` activation — small enough to feel\n  responsive, big enough to avoid firing on accidental clicks.\n- `onDragEnd` guards: no-op if dropped outside a column or on an\n  unknown status.\n- Optimistic local update mirrors the move before the PATCH:\n  `setLocal(prev => prev.map(...))` then `mutation.mutate(...)`.\n- Mutation invalidates the resource queryKey on settle, so a failed\n  PATCH refetches and the UI heals.\n\nCard rendering\n--------------\n- Title = first string field other than the status field.\n- Body shows every remaining field as compact label/value rows, with\n  type-aware formatting (decimal → toFixed(2), date/datetime →\n  toLocaleDateString, boolean → t(\"yes\")/t(\"no\")).\n- Status field is consumed by the column header, not repeated on the\n  card.\n- ui-kit branch uses Card for the card chrome and Badge for the column\n  count. Plain fallback uses matching Tailwind styles.\n\nDeps\n----\n`@dnd-kit/core` (^6.1.0) + `@dnd-kit/sortable` (^8.0.0) +\n`@dnd-kit/utilities` (^3.2.2) added to frontend-app runtime dependencies.\nAll MIT, tree-shakable, zero peer conflicts with our React 18 setup.\n\nTests\n-----\ntests/test_page_types_kanban.py adds 18 tests covering registration,\nthe three-tier status-field resolution (explicit / name heuristic /\nfirst-enum / backlog fallback), the paginated fetch with kanban-scoped\nqueryKey, the PATCH mutation body, the optimistic local mirror,\ndrag-end guards, all the dnd-kit imports and props, card title/body\nrendering, type-aware value formatting, and the ui-kit vs plain column\nheaders.\n\nFull suite: 200/200. Ruff clean. End-to-end verified with a generated\nui-kit + api-client + frontend-app fixture; `vite build` succeeds.\n\nPhase 2: 6/7 landed. Only `calendar` left.","tree":{"sha":"3f4e5cbcf313fa952a4606543cefff92d484c349","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/trees/3f4e5cbcf313fa952a4606543cefff92d484c349"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/commits/124429fdf8c3c2b7db6a60effa3d62c8f922f8fc","verification":{"payload":"tree 3f4e5cbcf313fa952a4606543cefff92d484c349\nparent 0ec0d736c4f6f57167eec1bc621a4f519bf48047\nauthor JD <bonicel.ftl@gmail.com> 1776550225 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776550225 +0200\n\nfeat(pages): add `kanban` page type — drag-and-drop board by status enum (#22)\n\nSixth Phase 2 page type. Renders records in columns keyed by an enum\nfield''s values; dropping a card into a different column PATCHes the\nrecord''s status field with the new column value, with an optimistic\nlocal update so the UI never lags while the mutation is in flight.\n\nColumn resolution\n-----------------\n1. Explicit `statusField` in the page config wins.\n2. Otherwise, prefer an enum field whose name matches a status-y hint:\n   `status` / `state` / `stage` / `phase`. That convention matches\n   nearly every kanban board in the wild — auto-detection picks the\n   right field when a resource has multiple enums (e.g. `priority`\n   alongside `status`).\n3. Fall back to the first enum field with a `values` array.\n4. With no enum at all, the emitter still generates a valid page — a\n   single \"Backlog\" column containing every record. Graceful fallback\n   rather than a hard error.\n\nDrag + drop\n-----------\n- `@dnd-kit/core` `DndContext` wraps the board; each column is a\n  `SortableContext` with `verticalListSortingStrategy`.\n- `PointerSensor` with `distance: 4` activation — small enough to feel\n  responsive, big enough to avoid firing on accidental clicks.\n- `onDragEnd` guards: no-op if dropped outside a column or on an\n  unknown status.\n- Optimistic local update mirrors the move before the PATCH:\n  `setLocal(prev => prev.map(...))` then `mutation.mutate(...)`.\n- Mutation invalidates the resource queryKey on settle, so a failed\n  PATCH refetches and the UI heals.\n\nCard rendering\n--------------\n- Title = first string field other than the status field.\n- Body shows every remaining field as compact label/value rows, with\n  type-aware formatting (decimal → toFixed(2), date/datetime →\n  toLocaleDateString, boolean → t(\"yes\")/t(\"no\")).\n- Status field is consumed by the column header, not repeated on the\n  card.\n- ui-kit branch uses Card for the card chrome and Badge for the column\n  count. Plain fallback uses matching Tailwind styles.\n\nDeps\n----\n`@dnd-kit/core` (^6.1.0) + `@dnd-kit/sortable` (^8.0.0) +\n`@dnd-kit/utilities` (^3.2.2) added to frontend-app runtime dependencies.\nAll MIT, tree-shakable, zero peer conflicts with our React 18 setup.\n\nTests\n-----\ntests/test_page_types_kanban.py adds 18 tests covering registration,\nthe three-tier status-field resolution (explicit / name heuristic /\nfirst-enum / backlog fallback), the paginated fetch with kanban-scoped\nqueryKey, the PATCH mutation body, the optimistic local mirror,\ndrag-end guards, all the dnd-kit imports and props, card title/body\nrendering, type-aware value formatting, and the ui-kit vs plain column\nheaders.\n\nFull suite: 200/200. Ruff clean. End-to-end verified with a generated\nui-kit + api-client + frontend-app fixture; `vite build` succeeds.\n\nPhase 2: 6/7 landed. Only `calendar` left.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp5AFRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmR0QAFj0jM6Mp8w0zIyvr/twPhZV\na9+YHszeijOt+KAeHCesZtOB6Ga5eojkPR1ElcVNPGLr7z2lgf7ynHWyXfaNQObD\n2bD2LjWVoYzEFOdUpxZ/dA0AsI8atKda4NFPd4yTEEtfQ9gxOfZ16zq2ISpgNH6n\neKxL9TqIHiny4mBfLWaLj8j0es3zKTKn2kkKYqtW/3LniWH5LCqCP8fbpzxj/K1/\n7rfIqSE7aoS3UTsbF7SNKTyWBLdc9fSSFvrGHjbB81JKf44MI8tHW8usiiosYFN4\nciy+49UsB34vL6eG4hhXWXeoRxqffnCU1iw4g7KKlGK8zniTy0jkMc6dxV4Gn8Rw\nms01cB8lWwlXDkxjB2D779KDD7SXmXY2yDeNiDFxz/86yG8POdSBMxRUj6Jd8X0U\nX2giV791tmcFq7r5w8mLbh1JLDd0k/39PH3SFJWSZyfhPrAqidOjKPVsebR4H3qG\nK0KVruACKTPI4J5WAHGC/VfYLvjTmqcDZkVzUr53gBchDUja4tk0yg+v1lNbC+Qy\nHrGsB/Fkm++Fd2WRtIOydFIWZBZ6VHnolOh+FynfzCfdnXQP5GFdCq4xGqSfR3Qx\nkggu5TpexP/4M8yEa0UBrm8ZhHyeVGrl67KLOwlh0kA9EpZIYczYNXzXmFZ7+pAv\nHQpYreab+HQaVgzCtozq\n=Mh65\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-18T22:10:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commit/124429fdf8c3c2b7db6a60effa3d62c8f922f8fc","node_id":"C_kwDOSDgQ39oAKDEyNDQyOWZkZjhjM2MyYjdkYjZhNjBlZmZhM2Q2MmM4ZjkyMmY4ZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commit/0ec0d736c4f6f57167eec1bc621a4f519bf48047","sha":"0ec0d736c4f6f57167eec1bc621a4f519bf48047","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/0ec0d736c4f6f57167eec1bc621a4f519bf48047"}],"sha":"124429fdf8c3c2b7db6a60effa3d62c8f922f8fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/124429fdf8c3c2b7db6a60effa3d62c8f922f8fc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29812288?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel","id":29812288,"login":"jeandbonicel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5ODEyMjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/0ec0d736c4f6f57167eec1bc621a4f519bf48047/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T22:01:08Z","email":"bonicel.ftl@gmail.com","name":"JD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T22:01:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(pages): add `tree` page type — hierarchical view via react-arborist (#21)\n\nFifth Phase 2 page type — and the first one that pulls in a third-party\nlib. Renders a self-referencing resource (anything with a nullable\n`parentId`) as a collapsible, keyboard-navigable, virtualized tree using\nreact-arborist. Suitable for department hierarchies, folder structures,\norg charts, category trees.\n\nBehaviour\n---------\n1. Fetch up to 1000 records in one paginated call with a distinct\n   queryKey `[resource, \"tree\"]` so the slice doesn''t collide with the\n   list page''s cache.\n2. Build the nested structure client-side with a single pass: put every\n   record in a Map keyed by id, then wire each record into its parent''s\n   children array. Records whose `parentId` isn''t in the result fall\n   through as roots, so the view degrades gracefully if pagination cuts\n   off an ancestor.\n3. Pick the first string field as the node label; fall back to the id if\n   no string field is configured.\n4. Render with react-arborist''s `<Tree>`, fixed 600×500 viewport (callers\n   can tweak the emitted file after generation).\n5. Node renderer shows ▾/▸ for open/closed internals and • for leaves;\n   clicking an internal node toggles it, clicking a leaf navigates to\n   `./view?id={id}` — the `?id=` convention used by `detail` and `edit`.\n\nPlain-HTML fallback still uses react-arborist (it''s not ui-kit-scoped);\nonly the outer chrome differs — bordered `<div>` + `<h1>` instead of\nCard/CardTitle.\n\nDeps\n----\n`react-arborist` (^3.4.0) added to the frontend-app template''s runtime\ndependencies, unconditional. It''s ~30 KB, tree-shakable, and the only\npage type that needs it; a conditional mechanism would be more scaffold\nwork than the dep is worth.\n\nTests\n-----\ntests/test_page_types_tree.py adds 11 tests covering registration, the\npaginated fetch with a tree-scoped queryKey, the flat-to-nested builder\n(ID map, dangling-children-as-roots fallback, useMemo wrap), node-label\nselection (first string / id fallback), react-arborist import, the\ncanonical Tree props, the node-renderer toggle/navigate logic, empty +\nerror states, and both wrappers (ui-kit Card vs plain bordered div).\n\nFull suite: 182/182. Ruff clean. End-to-end verified: fixture with ui-kit\n+ api-client + frontend-app, `vite build` succeeds.\n\nDocs: CLAUDE.md gets a `tree` entry and the `pages/` tree extended. No\nnew i18n keys needed (reuses loading/failedToLoad/noDataFound).\n\nPhase 2: 5/7 new page types landed. Remaining: `kanban`, `calendar`.","tree":{"sha":"d4527c4b3bf82bffee06db7adb4ed12d154339bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/trees/d4527c4b3bf82bffee06db7adb4ed12d154339bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/commits/0ec0d736c4f6f57167eec1bc621a4f519bf48047","verification":{"payload":"tree d4527c4b3bf82bffee06db7adb4ed12d154339bc\nparent 094830959035d81249d553fd999da67894f20907\nauthor JD <bonicel.ftl@gmail.com> 1776549668 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776549668 +0200\n\nfeat(pages): add `tree` page type — hierarchical view via react-arborist (#21)\n\nFifth Phase 2 page type — and the first one that pulls in a third-party\nlib. Renders a self-referencing resource (anything with a nullable\n`parentId`) as a collapsible, keyboard-navigable, virtualized tree using\nreact-arborist. Suitable for department hierarchies, folder structures,\norg charts, category trees.\n\nBehaviour\n---------\n1. Fetch up to 1000 records in one paginated call with a distinct\n   queryKey `[resource, \"tree\"]` so the slice doesn''t collide with the\n   list page''s cache.\n2. Build the nested structure client-side with a single pass: put every\n   record in a Map keyed by id, then wire each record into its parent''s\n   children array. Records whose `parentId` isn''t in the result fall\n   through as roots, so the view degrades gracefully if pagination cuts\n   off an ancestor.\n3. Pick the first string field as the node label; fall back to the id if\n   no string field is configured.\n4. Render with react-arborist''s `<Tree>`, fixed 600×500 viewport (callers\n   can tweak the emitted file after generation).\n5. Node renderer shows ▾/▸ for open/closed internals and • for leaves;\n   clicking an internal node toggles it, clicking a leaf navigates to\n   `./view?id={id}` — the `?id=` convention used by `detail` and `edit`.\n\nPlain-HTML fallback still uses react-arborist (it''s not ui-kit-scoped);\nonly the outer chrome differs — bordered `<div>` + `<h1>` instead of\nCard/CardTitle.\n\nDeps\n----\n`react-arborist` (^3.4.0) added to the frontend-app template''s runtime\ndependencies, unconditional. It''s ~30 KB, tree-shakable, and the only\npage type that needs it; a conditional mechanism would be more scaffold\nwork than the dep is worth.\n\nTests\n-----\ntests/test_page_types_tree.py adds 11 tests covering registration, the\npaginated fetch with a tree-scoped queryKey, the flat-to-nested builder\n(ID map, dangling-children-as-roots fallback, useMemo wrap), node-label\nselection (first string / id fallback), react-arborist import, the\ncanonical Tree props, the node-renderer toggle/navigate logic, empty +\nerror states, and both wrappers (ui-kit Card vs plain bordered div).\n\nFull suite: 182/182. Ruff clean. End-to-end verified: fixture with ui-kit\n+ api-client + frontend-app, `vite build` succeeds.\n\nDocs: CLAUDE.md gets a `tree` entry and the `pages/` tree extended. No\nnew i18n keys needed (reuses loading/failedToLoad/noDataFound).\n\nPhase 2: 5/7 new page types landed. Remaining: `kanban`, `calendar`.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp4/8kCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOngQAFXsIyZb6O7nVwq0Nyyj/9IJ\nSOpP1a3ABQq9BebXwD1escW1UTA/8hGws+wvLLqZtjenydkWI2+POVsl0us4yVoi\nS1/rizyjPbrwZeIjxht0WaObiN2kf4CGCI77g1q6t64mRIKrvO5LFJ3HVthKaIC