apps-generator/commits/094830959035d81249d553fd999da67894f20907"}],"sha":"0ec0d736c4f6f57167eec1bc621a4f519bf48047","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/0ec0d736c4f6f57167eec1bc621a4f519bf48047"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29812288?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel","id":29812288,"login":"jeandbonicel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5ODEyMjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/094830959035d81249d553fd999da67894f20907/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T21:52:03Z","email":"bonicel.ftl@gmail.com","name":"JD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T21:52:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(pages): add `settings` page type — singleton config form with grouped sections (#20)\n\nFourth Phase 2 page type. Unlike `form` / `edit` which operate on a\ncollection (`/resource` for listing, `/resource/{id}` for one record),\n`settings` treats the resource as a single record: `GET /{resource}`\nreturns the one record, `PUT /{resource}` replaces it. No id plumbing.\n\nWhy it''s a distinct type\n------------------------\nSaaS apps routinely have singleton config pages — org settings, user\npreferences, billing details, feature flags. Wrapping these in the\nlist+detail+edit pattern forces synthetic ids and multi-record list\npages nobody needs. `settings` is the idiomatic shape.\n\nBehaviour\n---------\n1. `useQuery` fetches the singleton via GET with queryKey `[\"<resource>\"]`.\n2. `useEffect` hydrates the form state once the fetch resolves (numbers\n   stringified for `<input type=\"number\">`, datetime trimmed for\n   `<input type=\"datetime-local\">`, booleans default to false).\n3. Fields group via an optional `group` key on each field. Groups render\n   as shadcn `Accordion` items with `type=\"multiple\"` and every group\n   open by default — settings should be visible at a glance, not hidden\n   behind clicks. Ungrouped fields collect under \"General\".\n4. PUT saves the singleton and invalidates the query so the form rehydrates.\n5. No DELETE — settings are persistent config.\n\nPlain-HTML fallback renders each group as a bordered `<section>` with a\n`<h2>` heading (no Accordion), so the visual hierarchy still reads\nwithout the ui-kit.\n\nInput rendering covers the same types as `form` / `edit` (string, text,\ninteger, long, decimal, boolean, date, datetime, enum). Resource-lookup\nauto-detection is intentionally skipped — a singleton has no meaningful\ncross-resource relations in this pattern.\n\nTests\n-----\ntests/test_page_types_settings.py adds 14 tests covering registration,\nsingleton fetch (GET without id), PUT save, absence of DELETE,\nhydration rules, Accordion with all groups expanded by default, grouping\nby the `group` key, ungrouped fields falling into \"General\", type-aware\ninputs, required-field stars, plain-HTML section fallback, no-shadcn\nimports in the plain branch, loading/error states, and the all-ungrouped\nedge case (one \"General\" section).\n\nFull suite: 171/171. Ruff clean. End-to-end verified with a generated\nfixture — `vite build` succeeds.\n\nDocs: CLAUDE.md gets a `settings` entry and the `pages/` tree extended;\nno new i18n keys needed (reuses save / saving / updatedSuccessfully /\nloading / failedToLoad).","tree":{"sha":"610cadb9201c38dd35f406717343d04b19ffa355","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/trees/610cadb9201c38dd35f406717343d04b19ffa355"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/commits/094830959035d81249d553fd999da67894f20907","verification":{"payload":"tree 610cadb9201c38dd35f406717343d04b19ffa355\nparent 16cb689ec98a6f3ed75320f112d0b32c2cdd48af\nauthor JD <bonicel.ftl@gmail.com> 1776549123 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776549123 +0200\n\nfeat(pages): add `settings` page type — singleton config form with grouped sections (#20)\n\nFourth Phase 2 page type. Unlike `form` / `edit` which operate on a\ncollection (`/resource` for listing, `/resource/{id}` for one record),\n`settings` treats the resource as a single record: `GET /{resource}`\nreturns the one record, `PUT /{resource}` replaces it. No id plumbing.\n\nWhy it''s a distinct type\n------------------------\nSaaS apps routinely have singleton config pages — org settings, user\npreferences, billing details, feature flags. Wrapping these in the\nlist+detail+edit pattern forces synthetic ids and multi-record list\npages nobody needs. `settings` is the idiomatic shape.\n\nBehaviour\n---------\n1. `useQuery` fetches the singleton via GET with queryKey `[\"<resource>\"]`.\n2. `useEffect` hydrates the form state once the fetch resolves (numbers\n   stringified for `<input type=\"number\">`, datetime trimmed for\n   `<input type=\"datetime-local\">`, booleans default to false).\n3. Fields group via an optional `group` key on each field. Groups render\n   as shadcn `Accordion` items with `type=\"multiple\"` and every group\n   open by default — settings should be visible at a glance, not hidden\n   behind clicks. Ungrouped fields collect under \"General\".\n4. PUT saves the singleton and invalidates the query so the form rehydrates.\n5. No DELETE — settings are persistent config.\n\nPlain-HTML fallback renders each group as a bordered `<section>` with a\n`<h2>` heading (no Accordion), so the visual hierarchy still reads\nwithout the ui-kit.\n\nInput rendering covers the same types as `form` / `edit` (string, text,\ninteger, long, decimal, boolean, date, datetime, enum). Resource-lookup\nauto-detection is intentionally skipped — a singleton has no meaningful\ncross-resource relations in this pattern.\n\nTests\n-----\ntests/test_page_types_settings.py adds 14 tests covering registration,\nsingleton fetch (GET without id), PUT save, absence of DELETE,\nhydration rules, Accordion with all groups expanded by default, grouping\nby the `group` key, ungrouped fields falling into \"General\", type-aware\ninputs, required-field stars, plain-HTML section fallback, no-shadcn\nimports in the plain branch, loading/error states, and the all-ungrouped\nedge case (one \"General\" section).\n\nFull suite: 171/171. Ruff clean. End-to-end verified with a generated\nfixture — `vite build` succeeds.\n\nDocs: CLAUDE.md gets a `settings` entry and the `pages/` tree extended;\nno new i18n keys needed (reuses save / saving / updatedSuccessfully /\nloading / failedToLoad).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp4/0ECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALn8QAJ+q1VZJmvW3EJVOOPsB72Sc\n+8IH3Ct+tdyG/yE+Pa+3pI7G+wTRNqsiTfNp4zJ7irYBPO8ybB0puWGQ8Aw9vqxI\n7wXqO+HUo9MEM+aFsusBTcxQJHFlvfnaZZWggwrHF0h6Q5AZZFY44WNt2mNc2gEL\n42NpuduQVZECh4GQH+Ob8MevzdWP9K+gydV6EGGD2EroHnEUvlsD8aByzzd+zgzl\nCMml8O4rJL8ScyQB9FcJCrZpqvDdND9JrN9VdgEjcpcx6jaQ7luZsLzxwQkWJlgu\nwtYPEiJKPuhSImKHLzaLGycA4UjU/qZl02g5uyZoW7AXlpxbCVZ9sDdcVFPPGQBN\nqfZEwhi+0BuqqlHjHcJ3Repbwpxk7pNkYDcz7s7g1BAmuPdRiuWGH/pGzQPBq7Vq\nF8ps9p9XvmLYDcY2XkcN1em5O86LTgJnJjWd15F/Byw3zUsoAUSky6b8iOMlCizP\nAQwrsbkUXdPp3XobSq4SdN417TDL26T3wo5evdXAvTJ3zK+acR3OcNQFEW7KRGlq\n4hDHAsvfEWjyu5HAfi2ZjdmllwO8Qz8Cfto18nAP0ckn9+9rl36yJ2NvlMFFaoOB\ngobqurt5VxPrXXm+8beH/9XtWBx28e73wMi6/jZkb9Qa5IOuG6HGEoJeSzQLH1v6\nkql2NEFnxh4qgzZL+LOX\n=Xwng\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-18T21:52:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commit/094830959035d81249d553fd999da67894f20907","node_id":"C_kwDOSDgQ39oAKDA5NDgzMDk1OTAzNWQ4MTI0OWQ1NTNmZDk5OWRhNjc4OTRmMjA5MDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commit/16cb689ec98a6f3ed75320f112d0b32c2cdd48af","sha":"16cb689ec98a6f3ed75320f112d0b32c2cdd48af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/16cb689ec98a6f3ed75320f112d0b32c2cdd48af"}],"sha":"094830959035d81249d553fd999da67894f20907","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/094830959035d81249d553fd999da67894f20907"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29812288?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel","id":29812288,"login":"jeandbonicel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5ODEyMjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/16cb689ec98a6f3ed75320f112d0b32c2cdd48af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T21:42:05Z","email":"bonicel.ftl@gmail.com","name":"JD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T21:42:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(pages): add `edit` page type — hydrated update form + destructive delete (#19)\n\nThird Phase 2 page type, and the first one to lean on the Phase 0 ui-kit\nadditions (AlertDialog). Closes the biggest single gap from the SmartHR\nskeleton audit — every resource now has a full Create/Read/Update/Delete\nloop via `form` + `detail` + `edit`.\n\nBehaviour\n---------\n`edit` mirrors `form` (same type-aware inputs, same resource-lookup\nauto-detection) and layers on:\n\n1. useQuery fetch of the existing record, using the `?id=` query string\n   like `detail` (the generated frontend-app has no URL-param routing).\n2. useEffect that hydrates the form state as soon as the fetch lands.\n   Numbers are stringified (HTML `<input type=\"number\">` wants strings),\n   datetime values are trimmed to the 16 chars `<input type=\"datetime-local\">`\n   expects, booleans fall back to false, strings to \"\".\n3. PUT mutation (`api.put<Entity>(/{resource}/{id}, data)`) with\n   t(\"updatedSuccessfully\") feedback.\n4. DELETE mutation fronted by an AlertDialog confirm (Phase 0 component),\n   returning to the previous page via window.history.back() on success.\n   Plain-HTML fallback uses window.confirm.\n\nBoth mutations invalidate the resource''s cached queryKey so the list and\ngrid pages refresh automatically.\n\ni18n keys\n---------\nNine new translation entries wired in both en.json and fr.json:\n  save, saving, updatedSuccessfully,\n  delete, deleting,\n  confirmDelete, confirmDeleteDesc,\n  confirm, cancel\n\nTests\n-----\ntests/test_page_types_edit.py adds 15 tests covering registration, id\nextraction, fetch + hydrate, PUT endpoint, DELETE endpoint,\nhistory.back(), cache invalidation of both mutations, AlertDialog wiring\nfor the destructive confirm, plain-HTML confirm fallback, type-aware\ninputs (text/checkbox/date/datetime/number/decimal/enum), required-field\nstars, loading/error states, and a regression guard that the inline\nstyle prop is a single JSX object literal (`{{ ... }}`) rather than the\nover-escaped `{{{{ ... }}}}` that an earlier draft emitted and broke\nvite build.\n\nEnd-to-end verified by generating a full ui-kit + api-client +\napi-domain + frontend-app stack with an edit page; `vite build` succeeds.\n\nFull suite: 157/157. Ruff clean.\n\nNotes\n-----\nThe field-input rendering in edit_type.py is a direct copy of the\nequivalent block in form_type.py. Extracting the shared helper into\nbase.py is a reasonable follow-up but was kept out of this PR to keep\nthe diff focused on the new page type.","tree":{"sha":"7a4364e4b86893f9b2b24218c9f6eab930efb574","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/trees/7a4364e4b86893f9b2b24218c9f6eab930efb574"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/commits/16cb689ec98a6f3ed75320f112d0b32c2cdd48af","verification":{"payload":"