allback, type-aware\ninputs (text/checkbox/date/datetime/number/decimal/enum), required-field\nstars, loading/error states, and a regression guard that the inline\nstyle prop is a single JSX object literal (`{{ ... }}`) rather than the\nover-escaped `{{{{ ... }}}}` that an earlier draft emitted and broke\nvite build.\n\nEnd-to-end verified by generating a full ui-kit + api-client +\napi-domain + frontend-app stack with an edit page; `vite build` succeeds.\n\nFull suite: 157/157. Ruff clean.\n\nNotes\n-----\nThe field-input rendering in edit_type.py is a direct copy of the\nequivalent block in form_type.py. Extracting the shared helper into\nbase.py is a reasonable follow-up but was kept out of this PR to keep\nthe diff focused on the new page type.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp4/qtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdzgQAKpWRGpkZvUsg311aycFKo0D\nzbpRvPycyqlyb0F28ID0qCmO/7zK0Ah+M8wbq5sgy4jtVRAvBce2GGzY3UIIrNZS\n+ceqNlkM4dWC57tb46/pinT8/w8iii1jHD0FEOnd8mhS23+dkCZPsQd4gjjDTNhp\nJzn6IPeJCbaRzPVermni2Mz9T+OpGzL4PJpKtl9Nc0Nvsd+9MAlvz2ch1/p+9p+C\nnTDHTq80S38H4yRMH4sUkhqrwlwm9kb2YWpmyzogANTtprbe8fQGQHA+XhSemLrr\nyHLoXxBIVJOT3zy4V6QRtS66Km1L6NPMxPT2IoTuTMey1m8/yDOSlbOr7F8G6cgz\nD2sNTEqQBQBBUTdue++i2PPQgGv231H/jPtJNG/4JrKsf0htBVi6mKZDpoQ0PQSc\ngDN6j/KLtF1yo0RoGwdHoxi2q2yRWCIxEITGrx7OjpxyoHoSGHQKvK4E81wCurhd\n/SvsWgJRuZPanr518G41H+HysuranKcrTVbWKf4SrjkyRaVS3b/bh1KoLboQaxwD\nVZq+0n6dsdyjhx9/VIHZhgigz8jqDUogTSlQblNLZgcKtv4gtf/qaJoAcb9RuB4B\na0aSti6EuL0uVi9wdvOKZAP+NgJdvWaLL7nduBgieZ9kuhKGgMrPSBO3C/r3tj2G\n5I569JpuJjKQbwnXM6ph\n=p7ar\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-18T21:42:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commit/16cb689ec98a6f3ed75320f112d0b32c2cdd48af","node_id":"C_kwDOSDgQ39oAKDE2Y2I2ODllYzk4YTZmM2VkNzUzMjBmMTEyZDBiMzJjMmNkZDQ4YWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commit/bd3e7730613be588d86533272dd5ae9e542620e9","sha":"bd3e7730613be588d86533272dd5ae9e542620e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/bd3e7730613be588d86533272dd5ae9e542620e9"}],"sha":"16cb689ec98a6f3ed75320f112d0b32c2cdd48af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/16cb689ec98a6f3ed75320f112d0b32c2cdd48af"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29812288?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel","id":29812288,"login":"jeandbonicel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5ODEyMjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/bd3e7730613be588d86533272dd5ae9e542620e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T21:28:20Z","email":"bonicel.ftl@gmail.com","name":"JD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T21:28:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(pages): add `grid` page type — responsive card-grid view (#18)\n\nSecond of the Phase 2 page types. Same data shape as `list` (paginated,\nnull-safe) but rendered as a responsive 1/2/3-column grid of Cards\ninstead of a Table. Matches SmartHR-style \"Employee Grid\" / \"Candidates\nGrid\" layouts.\n\nWhat the generator emits\n------------------------\n- Responsive grid container: `grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3`\n- Each record becomes a shadcn <Card>:\n  - First string field -> CardTitle\n  - Second string field -> CardDescription (omitted if only one string)\n  - Remaining fields  -> compact `<dl>` label/value rows in CardContent\n- Type-aware body values (mirrors list/detail):\n    decimal -> $NNN.NN via toFixed(2)\n    date    -> toLocaleDateString\n    boolean -> <Badge variant=\"default\">Yes</Badge>\n             / <Badge variant=\"outline\">No</Badge>\n    enum    -> <Badge variant=\"secondary\">value</Badge>\n    other   -> plain text, null -> \"—\"\n- Pagination controls identical to list (previous/next, 20/page)\n- Empty state message spans all grid columns\n- Separate queryKey [\"{resource}\", \"grid\", page] so list + grid don''t\n  share a cached page\n\nPlain-HTML fallback (no --uikit) renders matching structure with raw\n<div>/<h3>/<dl> and Tailwind classes, so the layout is consistent with\nor without the ui-kit. Boolean fields fall back to t(\"yes\")/t(\"no\").\n\nTests\n-----\n`tests/test_page_types_grid.py` adds 13 tests covering registration, the\npaginated useQuery hook, the responsive grid container, title/description\nfield promotion, body formatting per field type, ui-kit Badge usage,\npagination, empty state, plain-HTML fallback, and the single-string-field\nedge case (no description).\n\nEnd-to-end verified: generated a ui-kit + api-client + frontend-app with\na grid page; `vite build` succeeds.\n\nFull suite: 142/142. Ruff clean.","tree":{"sha":"64bfedabe470c4e5f8dfb44ad0e930d012319685","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/trees/64bfedabe470c4e5f8dfb44ad0e930d012319685"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/commits/bd3e7730613be588d86533272dd5ae9e542620e9","verification":{"payload":"tree 64bfedabe470c4e5f8dfb44ad0e930d012319685\nparent 9ccd383c70ed5e26c8be33d0b266b02b32fba529\nauthor JD <bonicel.ftl@gmail.com> 1776547700 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776547700 +0200\n\nfeat(pages): add `grid` page type — responsive card-grid view (#18)\n\nSecond of the Phase 2 page types. Same data shape as `list` (paginated,\nnull-safe) but rendered as a responsive 1/2/3-column grid of Cards\ninstead of a Table. Matches SmartHR-style \"Employee Grid\" / \"Candidates\nGrid\" layouts.\n\nWhat the generator emits\n------------------------\n- Responsive grid container: `grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3`\n- Each record becomes a shadcn <Card>:\n  - First string field -> CardTitle\n  - Second string field -> CardDescription (omitted if only one string)\n  - Remaining fields  -> compact `<dl>` label/value rows in CardContent\n- Type-aware body values (mirrors list/detail):\n    decimal -> $NNN.NN via toFixed(2)\n    date    -> toLocaleDateString\n    boolean -> <Badge variant=\"default\">Yes</Badge>\n             / <Badge variant=\"outline\">No</Badge>\n    enum    -> <Badge variant=\"secondary\">value</Badge>\n    other   -> plain text, null -> \"—\"\n- Pagination controls identical to list (previous/next, 20/page)\n- Empty state message spans all grid columns\n- Separate queryKey [\"{resource}\", \"grid\", page] so list + grid don''t\n  share a cached page\n\nPlain-HTML fallback (no --uikit) renders matching structure with raw\n<div>/<h3>/<dl> and Tailwind classes, so the layout is consistent with\nor without the ui-kit. Boolean fields fall back to t(\"yes\")/t(\"no\").\n\nTests\n-----\n`tests/test_page_types_grid.py` adds 13 tests covering registration, the\npaginated useQuery hook, the responsive grid container, title/description\nfield promotion, body formatting per field type, ui-kit Badge usage,\npagination, empty state, plain-HTML fallback, and the single-string-field\nedge case (no description).\n\nEnd-to-end verified: generated a ui-kit + api-client + frontend-app with\na grid page; `vite build` succeeds.\n\nFull suite: 142/142. Ruff clean.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp4/d0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyUIQAKFat/9OukdVeVLhk8mV9gJq\nGWsELJYiVF6eROJ0vsK7uu5hoZORHVcbpZKNSlnrPiYrHnmE55WZjRPtlvM1U1St\nX2vc6O1bbycGytzGPPUC7hTN69FWo+D0RFQmArx6za9vTuurJ6n9nfcvaobfZvHm\nKAOg3hGaSmRPxX0Dtq87dJiSDcsCuoE4lMGNwuHPMmSgeNJq+c2x/JRPDtFdiYea\n9Wn7X4FmG7hlJft08Q+nnyjJ7pNg1QGim5R4urOJ4WJlK5oU8Nkc/DpbaMJaNM2Y\nX14NjG99j1RoG+oMoq/eA5Vx7hRB2xNmbRlN0euyMOJX4xUGqXPyqRSXJjUirkCC\nmQv4Owg2J+v9nUrnAA2Bc1oU++Yf4PvLXoB84JYJoYVImc3BTx75Kkly2T3QUtiH\n73ugCkH3Q7nO4mvnlaD+Ox01Gjz9IFJzEHGYybQsSHP68LM42UYuGywmg2KzQET/\ndOipVLRvF9qdRMgWwk0gqT54t4Y4PBRTkk+Fz+CD2i/s5f6yjtdIVVi3GAV7lGPX\nlIViC3WO1as3UNGDs5NvJbI6FHMN0mFxQjtQoUFYNnj9XoSKod0s8mzDKo6hvbtP\n5tJsAH2TWOUOiFqiFPehknAk02MvSrhAAHDnUZx7gJ3ZRAUzdV2uv4qAYLTERyJH\nyJQQBnIoSCuwy14Q3keZ\n=8KkL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-18T21:28:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commit/bd3e7730613be588d86533272dd5ae9e542620e9","node_id":"C_kwDOSDgQ39oAKGJkM2U3NzMwNjEzYmU1ODhkODY1MzMyNzJkZDVhZTllNTQyNjIwZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commit/9ccd383c70ed5e26c8be33d0b266b02b32fba529","sha":"9ccd383c70ed5e26c8be33d0b266b02b32fba529","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/9ccd383c70ed5e26c8be33d0b266b02b32fba529"}],"sha":"bd3e7730613be588d86533272dd5ae9e542620e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/bd3e7730613be588d86533272dd5ae9e542620e9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29812288?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel","id":29812288,"login":"jeandbonicel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5ODEyMjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/9ccd383c70ed5e26c8be33d0b266b02b32fba529/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T21:15:17Z","email":"bonicel.ftl@gmail.com","name":"JD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T21:15:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(pages): add `detail` page type — read-only single-record view (#17)\n\nFirst of the seven new page types from Phase 2 of the page-type catalog\nwork. Picked as the vertical-slice proof that the PageTypeRegistry\narchitecture actually unlocks drop-in page types: a new emitter module,\na registry tuple update, and the dispatcher routes to it unchanged.\n\nWhat the generator emits\n------------------------\nA detail page renders one record''s field values inside a shadcn Card as\na two-column definition list. The record id is read from the ``?id=``\nquery string, since the generated frontend-app maps paths to components\ndirectly (no URL params). When id is absent we show ``t(\"missingId\")``;\notherwise TanStack Query fetches ``GET /{resource}/{id}``, with a\nSkeleton placeholder per field while loading.\n\nType-aware value rendering:\n  string / int / long  -> plain text, null -> \"—\"\n  decimal              -> $NNN.NN via toFixed(2)\n  date / datetime      -> toLocaleDateString()\n  boolean              -> <Badge variant=\"default\">Yes</Badge>\n                          or <Badge variant=\"outline\">No</Badge>\n  enum                 -> <Badge variant=\"secondary\">value</Badge>\n  text                 -> <span className=\"whitespace-pre-wrap\">\n\nNull-safety mirrors the `list` page: every field falls back to \"—\" or\na muted-foreground placeholder when the value is nullish.\n\nPlain-HTML fallback (no --uikit) works identically but drops the Card\nwrapper and uses a plain pulsing <div> for the skeleton and t(\"yes\") /\nt(\"no\") for booleans.\n\ni18n\n----\nThree new translation keys wired in both en.json and fr.json:\n  yes        / Oui\n  no         / Non\n  missingId  / Aucun ID fourni\n\nTests\n-----\n`tests/test_page_types_detail.py` adds 11 tests covering registration,\nthe React Query hook and query-string id extraction, every field label\nemitted, type-specific value formatters, ui-kit imports and Badge usage,\nthe plain-HTML fallback, the Skeleton count, and the error state.\n\nVerified end-to-end: generated a ui-kit + api-client + frontend-app with\na detail page, `vite build` succeeds, output looks right.\n\nFull suite: 129/129. Ruff clean.\n\nDocs\n----\nCLAUDE.md and README.md updated with the new page type, and CLAUDE.md''s\ncode-structure section now reflects the pages/ package introduced in\nPhase 1 (list_type.py / form_type.py / dashboard_type.py / detail_type.py).","tree":{"sha":"eaa17793855144c4afdca37eafb7ea921ef4d26b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/trees/eaa17793855144c4afdca37eafb7ea921ef4d26b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/commits/9ccd383c70ed5e26c8be33d0b266b02b32fba529","verification":{"payload":"tree eaa17793855144c4afdca37eafb7ea921ef4d26b\nparent bc23a97a24290306c0313339ab4c16c23ade8f65\nauthor JD <bonicel.ftl@gmail.com> 1776546917 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776546917 +0200\n\nfeat(pages): add `detail` page type — read-only single-record view (#17)\n\nFirst of the seven new page types from Phase 2 of the page-type catalog\nwork. Picked as the vertical-slice proof that the PageTypeRegistry\narchitecture actually unlocks drop-in page types: a new emitter module,\na registry tuple update, and the dispatcher routes to it unchanged.\n\nWhat the generator emits\n------------------------\nA detail page renders one record''s field values inside a shadcn Card as\na two-column definition list. The record id is read from the ``?id=``\nquery string, since the generated frontend-app maps paths to components\ndirectly (no URL params). When id is absent we show ``t(\"missingId\")``;\notherwise TanStack Query fetches ``GET /{resource}/{id}``, with a\nSkeleton placeholder per field while loading.\n\nType-aware value rendering:\n  string / int / long  -> plain text, null -> \"—\"\n  decimal              -> $NNN.NN via toFixed(2)\n  date / datetime      -> toLocaleDateString()\n  boolean              -> <Badge variant=\"default\">Yes</Badge>\n                          or <Badge variant=\"outline\">No</Badge>\n  enum                 -> <Badge variant=\"secondary\">value</Badge>\n  text                 -> <span className=\"whitespace-pre-wrap\">\n\nNull-safety mirrors the `list` page: every field falls back to \"—\" or\na muted-foreground placeholder when the value is nullish.\n\nPlain-HTML fallback (no --uikit) works identically but drops the Card\nwrapper and uses a plain pulsing <div> for the skeleton and t(\"yes\") /\nt(\"no\") for booleans.\n\ni18n\n----\nThree new translation keys wired in both en.json and fr.json:\n  yes        / Oui\n  no         / Non\n  missingId  / Aucun ID fourni\n\nTests\n-----\n`tests/test_page_types_detail.py` adds 11 tests covering registration,\nthe React Query hook and query-string id extraction, every field label\nemitted, type-specific value formatters, ui-kit imports and Badge usage,\nthe plain-HTML fallback, the Skeleton count, and the error state.\n\nVerified end-to-end: generated a ui-kit + api-client + frontend-app with\na detail page, `vite build` succeeds, output looks right.\n\nFull suite: 129/129. Ruff clean.\n\nDocs\n----\nCLAUDE.md and README.md updated with the new page type, and CLAUDE.md''s\ncode-structure section now reflects the pages/ package introduced in\nPhase 1 (list_type.py / form_type.py / dashboard_type.py / detail_type.py).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp4/RlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyYIQAI+Qwrx4CtBRKOrWqXYaI9Iw\nhYm7deUwlKdEZ3MhFiVTZ2qIqSk8Oqp7oZFcwyISusleFRpFRSlW1WAuLUK4KF/1\nGGnZCxHD2pC2BN+kNAr7OvlqOGIjpLXrsPlBCNIvvQIjEqj6IhaomPaGjBG+ty+X\nV3+QtzOUC3cmrRnMzb09cUkEGmZOR49lKwIhBCEQfH8efcwFTOf235efMmJgCJYK\nbiF08G1ryiMenVdd4qSHqL2VMA/bf4P2sIT0YDT7jt2BUehRvqcgv3vGP0+9gxQr\nWXiZ0y0zQ577PMsDYKnCfOhGLdr4W2HpWa+vob2nrf40k4x0nz3JW3614PnVrRns\nveX96WK7u3ApLxA6SMzRzwLRcdUcz0M+7HiY1ef5Mzilvc6EtKUa3Ygvr9t+n1wS\n0z8ePl5mhOjFmxhgug3y/tohDE91N9Fd8er7JIJDAfDDW+5OU5gS8ewDvH8tVdw+\ncBqGZmhQGlNGUTaex2jOz9kNARIDCWR06TIPqnWBPfBxmibht+k58eJuvayyEsUD\nR+kD0eJdC9G0OYbslVv4KQi468IbRf9O/1dQuCv8eankMOe+mPl7VGrpNqr1adLz\nA7nZ7MLUkCnsl6MO5hp1sUjxYr3973YKThB2gCtJ7Ej36KA2sGKlTPYr1/7vEH5j\nLecIWufmuYGgXeXMiNLF\n=tsQr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-18T21:15:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commit/9ccd383c70ed5e26c8be33d0b266b02b32fba529","node_id":"C_kwDOSDgQ39oAKDljY2QzODNjNzBlZDVlMjZjOGJlMzNkMGIyNjZiMDJiMzJmYmE1Mjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commit/bc23a97a24290306c0313339ab4c16c23ade8f65","sha":"bc23a97a24290306c0313339ab4c16c23ade8f65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/bc23a97a24290306c0313339ab4c16c23ade8f65"}],"sha":"9ccd383c70ed5e26c8be33d0b266b02b32fba529","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/9ccd383c70ed5e26c8be33d0b266b02b32fba529"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29812288?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel","id":29812288,"login":"jeandbonicel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5ODEyMjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/bc23a97a24290306c0313339ab4c16c23ade8f65/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T20:59:12Z","email":"bonicel.ftl@gmail.com","name":"JD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T20:59:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ui-kit): add 12 shadcn components for Phase 0 of page-type catalog (#16)\n\n* feat(ui-kit): add 12 shadcn components for Phase 0 of page-type catalog\n\nAdds the ui-kit primitives that unblock the remaining page-type work\n(detail, edit, grid, kanban, calendar, tree, settings):\n\n  Overlays/disclosures: Popover, AlertDialog, Collapsible, Accordion\n  Data entry:           Calendar, DatePicker, RadioGroup, Combobox, Form\n  Command palette:      Command (cmdk)\n  Navigation:           Sidebar, NavigationMenu\n\nEach ships with:\n  - Component file under src/components/ui/, following the existing\n    shadcn + cva + forwardRef + displayName conventions\n  - Named exports wired into src/index.ts barrel\n  - CSF3 Storybook entry under stories/ with a working Default story\n\nDependencies added to ui-kit package.json:\n  @radix-ui/{popover,radio-group,alert-dialog,collapsible,accordion,\n             navigation-menu}\n  react-day-picker, date-fns              (Calendar, DatePicker)\n  react-hook-form, @hookform/resolvers, zod (Form)\n  cmdk                                     (Command, Combobox)\n\nTheme and build plumbing:\n  - Sidebar CSS variables (light + dark) in globals.css\n  - tailwind-preset.ts + ui-kit''s own tailwind.config.ts expose\n    sidebar.* color tokens and accordion-up/down keyframes\n  - linking.py expanded to emit the same tokens + accordion animation\n    into consumer tailwind configs, plus safelist entries for the\n    new component classes\n\nTests:\n  - tests/test_ui_kit.py: 18 tests asserting every new component file\n    exists, barrel exports the expected symbols, package.json declares\n    the new deps, globals.css + tailwind-preset.ts carry sidebar tokens,\n    all 12 Storybook entries are present\n  - Full suite green: 117/117\n\nVerified end-to-end by generating the fixture, running npm install, and\nlaunching Storybook on port 6006 - every new component renders.\n\n* fix(ui-kit): drop Jinja raw blocks + fix chart.tsx TypeScript errors\n\nThe Phase 0 Form and Calendar components used `{{ obj }}` JSX patterns\nthat collide with Jinja''s variable delimiter. The original fix wrapped\nboth files in `{% raw %} ... {% endraw %}`, matching the convention\nused by tooltip.tsx, dropdown-menu.tsx, and chart.tsx. Problem: raw\nblocks are a footgun - any future Jinja variable added inside silently\nstops being substituted, and leaked markers break the generated .tsx\nat parse time (we''ve hit this in a sibling project).\n\nFix: keep the files Jinja-renderable (no raw blocks) and avoid the\noffending `{{` by spacing the braces apart - semantically identical\nin JSX, invisible to Jinja:\n\n  value={{ name: props.name }}   ->  value={ { name: props.name } }\n  classNames={{                  ->  classNames={ {\n\nApplied to form.tsx, calendar.tsx, and chart.tsx.\n\nWhile touching chart.tsx also fixed three pre-existing TypeScript\nerrors that surface when running `npm run lint` on a generated ui-kit:\n\n  * CSSProperties doesn''t expose an index signature, so indexing\n    `style[\\`--color-${key}\\`]` broke. Switch to building the map as\n    Record<string, string> and cast once when passing to `style`.\n    React/DOM accept unknown custom properties at runtime.\n  * `React.ComponentProps<typeof Legend>` (Recharts) pulls in a\n    LegacyRef<ReactElement> that isn''t assignable to LegacyRef<Legend>\n    when the whole bag is spread. We don''t forward a ref here - strip\n    `ref` from the type before spreading.\n\nRegression guard: test_generated_output_has_no_jinja_residue scans every\ngenerated .ts/.tsx/.js/.jsx/.json/.css/.md file for leftover\n{% raw %}/{% endraw %} markers and fails if any are found, so anyone\nreaching for a raw block in the future gets a red test instead of a\nbroken build.\n\nFull suite: 118/118. Generated fixture + `npm run lint` now zero errors.\n\n* style: ruff format test_ui_kit.py","tree":{"sha":"96fb71a24e28fe0293a2571853416e8aba49a4cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/trees/96fb71a24e28fe0293a2571853416e8aba49a4cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/commits/bc23a97a24290306c0313339ab4c16c23ade8f65","verification":{"payload":"tree 96fb71a24e28fe0293a2571853416e8aba49a4cb\nparent 70c24e4bfcf84f498ca473920e0489efbf43717d\nauthor JD <bonicel.ftl@gmail.com> 1776545952 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776545952 +0200\n\nfeat(ui-kit): add 12 shadcn components for Phase 0 of page-type catalog (#16)\n\n* feat(ui-kit): add 12 shadcn components for Phase 0 of page-type catalog\n\nAdds the ui-kit primitives that unblock the remaining page-type work\n(detail, edit, grid, kanban, calendar, tree, settings):\n\n  Overlays/disclosures: Popover, AlertDialog, Collapsible, Accordion\n  Data entry:           Calendar, DatePicker, RadioGroup, Combobox, Form\n  Command palette:      Command (cmdk)\n  Navigation:           Sidebar, NavigationMenu\n\nEach ships with:\n  - Component file under src/components/ui/, following the existing\n    shadcn + cva + forwardRef + displayName conventions\n  - Named exports wired into src/index.ts barrel\n  - CSF3 Storybook entry under stories/ with a working Default story\n\nDependencies added to ui-kit package.json:\n  @radix-ui/{popover,radio-group,alert-dialog,collapsible,accordion,\n             navigation-menu}\n  react-day-picker, date-fns              (Calendar, DatePicker)\n  react-hook-form, @hookform/resolvers, zod (Form)\n  cmdk                                     (Command, Combobox)\n\nTheme and build plumbing:\n  - Sidebar CSS variables (light + dark) in globals.css\n  - tailwind-preset.ts + ui-kit''s own tailwind.config.ts expose\n    sidebar.* color tokens and accordion-up/down keyframes\n  - linking.py expanded to emit the same tokens + accordion animation\n    into consumer tailwind configs, plus safelist entries for the\n    new component classes\n\nTests:\n  - tests/test_ui_kit.py: 18 tests asserting every new component file\n    exists, barrel exports the expected symbols, package.json declares\n    the new deps, globals.css + tailwind-preset.ts carry sidebar tokens,\n    all 12 Storybook entries are present\n  - Full suite green: 117/117\n\nVerified end-to-end by generating the fixture, running npm install, and\nlaunching Storybook on port 6006 - every new component renders.\n\n* fix(ui-kit): drop Jinja raw blocks + fix chart.tsx TypeScript errors\n\nThe Phase 0 Form and Calendar components used `{{ obj }}` JSX patterns\nthat collide with Jinja''s variable delimiter. The original fix wrapped\nboth files in `{% raw %} ... {% endraw %}`, matching the convention\nused by tooltip.tsx, dropdown-menu.tsx, and chart.tsx. Problem: raw\nblocks are a footgun - any future Jinja variable added inside silently\nstops being substituted, and leaked markers break the generated .tsx\nat parse time (we''ve hit this in a sibling project).\n\nFix: keep the files Jinja-renderable (no raw blocks) and avoid the\noffending `{{` by spacing the braces apart - semantically identical\nin JSX, invisible to Jinja:\n\n  value={{ name: props.name }}   ->  value={ { name: props.name } }\n  classNames={{                  ->  classNames={ {\n\nApplied to form.tsx, calendar.tsx, and chart.tsx.\n\nWhile touching chart.tsx also fixed three pre-existing TypeScript\nerrors that surface when running `npm run lint` on a generated ui-kit:\n\n  * CSSProperties doesn''t expose an index signature, so indexing\n    `style[\\`--color-${key}\\`]` broke. Switch to building the map as\n    Record<string, string> and cast once when passing to `style`.\n    React/DOM accept unknown custom properties at runtime.\n  * `React.ComponentProps<typeof Legend>` (Recharts) pulls in a\n    LegacyRef<ReactElement> that isn''t assignable to LegacyRef<Legend>\n    when the whole bag is spread. We don''t forward a ref here - strip\n    `ref` from the type before spreading.\n\nRegression guard: test_generated_output_has_no_jinja_residue scans every\ngenerated .ts/.tsx/.js/.jsx/.json/.css/.md file for leftover\n{% raw %}/{% endraw %} markers and fails if any are found, so anyone\nreaching for a raw block in the future gets a red test instead of a\nbroken build.\n\nFull suite: 118/118. Generated fixture + `npm run lint` now zero errors.\n\n* style: ruff format test_ui_kit.py","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp4/CgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeq8QABoT/iCMYXnuifDzhLR18/ib\nj1Yhof2Y8fpM8ST/rqpLxkQtrLSxzbJzaCTddU5411BL+gudII4Ztl6z0ecMBI/F\nWGmrqp32T6ZG3mAETBeabGqA0Ki9qLoIoK6k7WQ9/8k0AR5+SnrZTEmyBn5pBWSm\nW6bjAQ8sjzrQgVXIOomVD5ns7Zq4WjnvWkQvsiIYyIOCVSNKQd8Y2ZRtuxgODYPT\nHOGbLtPLHh1FebtGQpwcnX/hgbthufIOKXkBbj4ZP0x1crBcI76XfzPmdi4cKOPu\nUTAHHBuy4d49oALAluL4a9c165nh+tQq6CZjgTFTRhmtSVaMhYiiZnkiZbykr4SO\nvgkLP4MfPiRfkYkiVW13k9mMh1Ujp6ALY1DLGPQBAPJprZfvmQfdMDBMtL4OKyL8\nP4jv9VDyXqQUpYrGB3RpvBcbyrLGKz/VXCxRGPjK2dGEHWYTXiDwFvKuub54KzPD\noOlqDbTy7MfXwohJQ3EMsnwlGCaiHCv8hkriu+t9ac43xssA4wcVlp/xt/sVPMFI\nhIfG28+YSDR2NrBbi7Hu9/Lkc/0B9x84kZdSUUw+mWXK8lf785OOuKD/HpxayrgY\ne+7PCs3plFaAhLNhxGkvAGFPgnOo/I1YkSURdAXpAkb3HJQoUS6gN1YpJpIU1aXs\no1F1ugbFWaGbrSaMpzKc\n=4YA9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-18T20:59:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commit/bc23a97a24290306c0313339ab4c16c23ade8f65","node_id":"C_kwDOSDgQ39oAKGJjMjNhOTdhMjQyOTAzMDZjMDMxMzMzOWFiNGMxNmMyM2FkZThmNjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commit/70c24e4bfcf84f498ca473920e0489efbf43717d","sha":"70c24e4bfcf84f498ca473920e0489efbf43717d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/70c24e4bfcf84f498ca473920e0489efbf43717d"}],"sha":"bc23a97a24290306c0313339ab4c16c23ade8f65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/bc23a97a24290306c0313339ab4c16c23ade8f65"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29812288?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeandbonicel","id":29812288,"login":"jeandbonicel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5ODEyMjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeandbonicel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/commits/70c24e4bfcf84f498ca473920e0489efbf43717d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T19:30:39Z","email":"bonicel.ftl@gmail.com","name":"JD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T19:30:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: split pages.py into PageTypeRegistry + per-type modules (#15)\n\nPhase 1 of the page-type catalog refactor. The 774-line pages.py is replaced\nby a pages/ package where each built-in page type (list, form, dashboard)\nlives in its own module and self-registers via a PageTypeRegistry. The\ndispatcher in __init__.py now routes by registry lookup instead of an\nif/elif chain, which is what lets future phases add new page types (detail,\nedit, grid, kanban, calendar, tree, settings) without touching the\ndispatcher, and lets plugins register custom types via entry points.\n\nPublic API (parse_pages, find_project_root, generate_page_components) is\npreserved, so cli/generate.py and the test suite work unchanged. Generator\noutput is byte-identical to the pre-refactor version.\n\nBuilt-in emitter modules are named *_type.py rather than list.py / form.py /\ndashboard.py because Python binds submodules as package attributes, which\nwould shadow the built-in list type inside parse_pages and break\nisinstance(x, list).\n\nIncludes 10 new tests covering the registry contract; full suite is 99/99.","tree":{"sha":"48fbebd37ee5990ffa2741342fc98f4974a9f39e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/trees/48fbebd37ee5990ffa2741342fc98f4974a9f39e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeandbonicel/apps-generator/git/commits/70c24e4bfcf84f498ca473920e0489efbf43717d","verification":{"payload":"tree 48fbebd37ee5990ffa2741342fc98f4974a9f39e\nparent 4c77a0ba7681dc67c339a46027cf2d0c289d7139\nauthor JD <bonicel.ftl@gmail.com> 1776540639 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776540639 +0200\n\nrefactor: split pages.py into PageTypeRegistry + per-type modules (#15)\n\nPhase 1 of the page-type catalog refactor. The 774-line pages.py is replaced\nby a pages/ package where each built-in page type (list, form, dashboard)\nlives in its own module and self-registers via a PageTypeRegistry. The\ndispatcher in __init__.py now routes by registry lookup instead of an\nif/elif chain, which is what lets future phases add new page types (detail,\nedit, grid, kanban, calendar, tree, settings) without touching the\ndispatcher, and lets plugins register custom types via entry points.\n\nPublic API (parse_pages, find_project_root, generate_page_components) is\npreserved, so cli/generate.py and the test suite work unchanged. Generator\noutput is byte-identical to the pre-refactor version.\n\nBuilt-in emitter modules are named *_type.py rather than list.py / form.py /\ndashboard.py because Python binds submodules as package attributes, which\nwould shadow the built-in list type inside parse_pages and break\nisinstance(x, list).\n\nIncludes 10 new tests covering the registry contract; full suite is 99/99.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp49vfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtPIQAIO/epODg0Jpg+cT7yz/SvEk\nJqryrDLrqpuuXbsVHN24AubwRCROE1KWo+Pj2n9AB2Vjf9ByvsFDX3nuMkMTR2lD\nh9jPxTt7gzP4Ry4WtBbMGGlzp5opUFQCOYR3saiMFPh7oYo+MuOURAyR/wc302Ey\n2KwXyGzcnCvKoMLGuSxdQsqPo+kurrlrS1CsRt/o+QpShlSQoXu4VjVPpoboLjU+\n8eb886L1MyPP2tdIUu6rOMFynBsxRADvjfv1yN4q75A7E+K6HupJbj8vszfEhD0q\ngEOzFrLke7+vWkl9sYJcvxhaXtOtvZWe842MmUb8ax8JoY1V6CKi6mnfUpv03xzu\nGfQAWLDgB3SC4EGoOaDMazB5GX2tNk4XGi8xp/nXjs90CE8xPeMGoPrTnf3IVJTA\nqM2ZlWfNpc0Qf66nfch8TFYQq1F1uTFfTSKYFfJNOM8T0uC5lkGL61ygqCpIWGLu\nKJCYem1NLimEuSzwC85XN1sAMf0nvd56QFxIG4+hxMCaSb/aUdpYd+0ne3yjKyAK\nd00vMLlvQwvOR2sTZY8bB3zG9ugTCoFAn2cRJ1Iu1FMSSJCF4Lh3DPQaBK8JLMCJ\n1FxYpMyjg7pt5Nl5MCvZJsmcfXFRKi9i+d+2Om+Bioe/0jmY/ijJMRKrkZiZW/fv\nldJziaTNwUJJOPWopcmh\n=C+WY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-18T19:30:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers"